{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1428599-v5-vampire-companion","id":1428599,"title":"V5 Vampire Companion","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-12-16T08:04:45-08:00","id":1428599,"title":"V5 Vampire Companion","content":"Today will see the publication of the V5 Vampire Companion. It will be home to rules for V5 Ravnos, Tzimisce, Salubri, ghouls and will also be home to unimaginable levels of malign malignity and malevolence.<br /> <br /> I'm just starting a thread on the book early.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","name":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1208_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-15T09:29:03-08:00","id":1424028,"title":"","content":"We've got good news for those who have been lacking their Tzimisce and Ravnos fixes. Both those Clans and a full write-up for the Salubri are going to be in the V5 companion.<br /> <br /> This is going to be a discussion of how you want them done and what pitfalls you hope they avoid.<br /> <br /> Carried over from the Modiphius thread.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1423253-modiphius-is-bo-longer-the-publisher-of-vtm-renegade-studios-is/page9\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/filedata/fetch?filedataid=1074\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1423253-modiphius-is-bo-longer-the-publisher-of-vtm-renegade-studios-is/page9\"> Modiphius is bo longer the publisher of vtm,Renegade studios is. - Onyx Path Forums </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1423253-modiphius-is-bo-longer-the-publisher-of-vtm-renegade-studios-is/page9\"> http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1423253-modiphius-is-bo-longer-the-publisher-of-vtm-renegade-studios-is/page9 </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> There will also be a new book with tzimisce in it Edit from Moderator: Vampire: The Masquerade Companion Key Features http://www.geek-pride.co.uk/tabletop/all </div> </div> </div><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-16T08:10:25-08:00","id":1428600,"title":"","content":"Assuming you have a membership, it is available here;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://www.worldofdarkness.com/account\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.worldofdarkness.com/account\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.worldofdarkness.com/account\" target=\"_blank\"> https://www.worldofdarkness.com/account </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","name":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1208_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-16T08:17:41-08:00","id":1428601,"title":"","content":"I like the art and the presentation of the Ravnos and Tzimisce. I am a little ambivalent on the presentation of the Salubri.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","name":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1208_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-16T08:42:46-08:00","id":1428604,"title":"","content":"YOU MUSN'T OPEN THE PDF!<br /> <br /> *The spirit of Saulot is released*<br /> <br /> NOOOOOO!<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Okay, well now it's okay to open the PDF.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-16T09:07:18-08:00","id":1428606,"title":"","content":"So what's everyone's take? At a quick glance, here's what I think:<br /> <br /> I like the Ravnos, I expected the whole &quot;trickster&quot; angle to play up and while I think it somewhat steps on the Malkavian's toes as jester it might also dissuade Fishmalks and push Malks back into Oracle territory. The Bane seems super annoying, but the disciplines are fun to use both on their own and via Chimerstry. Since Chimerstry requires high Presence I think the two will complement each other well. Oddly, Fata Morgana doesn't require Chimerstry as a prereq so you could feasibly not take Chimerstry at all and just use Fata Morgana at higher levels.<br /> <br /> Salubri I'm not crazy about, mostly because of the lore of them being super special no matter what. It feels like you could never play one without having some Grand Design in play, which I would like the option not to have. The healing-type Discipline powers are interesting but mechanically kind of clunky, very clearly limited because otherwise they'd be broken, and end up using up a lot of your Discipline options so you can't build very freely. I'm glad I was never expecting these, or I'd probably be disappointed.<br /> <br /> Tzimisce I'm so-so about. I like them as being avaricious dragons, but I feel like they've lost some of the &quot;old country nobility&quot; style that they used to have. I think the Bane of being surrounded by something thematically important to them is very interesting, it's more versatile than just grave dirt and gives an option for character customization like a Ventrue's feeding preference. I think a lot of people will be disappointed by how underpowered Vicissitude is but I'm happy because it was obviously OVERpowered in previous editions. Giving it a finite resource in the form of physical ability dots and also making it healable (albeit difficult, but possible) really stops Vicissitude from being the ridiculousness that it was previously. As per the Tzimisce homebrew discussions had here I do agree that Dominate feels bad on a Tzimisce since so much of their legacy has been about commanding fear and respect due to what they can do, and not by breaking someone's will supernaturally. If Tzimisce had been Animalism, Auspex, and Protean with all the Viscissitude powers being Protean/Auspex amalgams I think it would have been ideal.<br /> <br /> I do really love the One with the Land power for both Tzimisce and Gangrel.<br /> <br /> I think the Clan Coterie Merits are extremely flavorful and fun, even if some are clearly better than others. I'm a sucker for reliable once-per-session abilities.<br /> <br /> Having rules for playing a mortal or ghoul is definitely good just to cover bases, even though I think they probably shouldn't BE played. But it'll definitely be helpful to flesh out custom SPCs at least, and for anyone who insists that they do want to play a mortal.<br /> <br /> As for Errata, let's see. Everyone gets a boost to Blood Surge, which is nice since I think it's often underappreciated. Bane Severity is also stronger now, which makes some things that could normally be largely ignored suddenly more critical to pay attention to. Lingering Kiss is back to I think the first version of its errata? I wasn't sure where that ended up. While disappointing, I agree that granting 2 dice to any category of pools was too strong for what it should have been, so limiting it to Social only and reducing the duration is fine. Better than the original.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25972-illithidactivity","name":"IllithidActivity","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25972_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"103"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-16T09:07:34-08:00","id":1428607,"title":"","content":"It seems Salubri are now Sabbat Ventrue. <br /> <br /> I'll read it later but seems like losing the normal Dominate functions will be painful.<br /> <br /> Ravnos using Obfuscate seems obvious but also a loss for certain play styles.<br /> <br /> Tzimice losing Protean seems the least detrimental. I'm most looking forward to seeing how Vicissitude works in volume 5.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24221-vamps-like-us","name":"Vamps Like Us","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"390"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-16T09:13:48-08:00","id":1428608,"title":"","content":"Read the three 'Clan' write-ups so far and my thoughts on them...<br /> <br /> Ravnos: For the most I like it but I am ambivalent on their Bane. Though I admit I do like that they take the time to explain it and that Ravnos could actually stay in a city rather always moving. However the Clan Compulsion does make up for it as it feels both in-line with the old Clan Flaw and their state in a post-Week of Nightmares world.<br /> <br /> Salubri: Of the three, these are the most disappointing for me. It feels like the same old, same old without anything new or interesting being added. The one new thing, their new Bane, feels like something that will rarely ever come up as it's now that their Blood is especially tasty and Kindred could become overwhelmed in drinking from them.<br /> <br /> Tzimisce: Pretty much everything I was hoping for with them. They have continued the trend from Anarchs Unbound in making the Clan more than just the Sabbat which had long been one of my biggest complaints about the Tzimisce. But then given the state of the Sabbat in V5 that's unsurprising. I like their new Bane, a refinement on their original where instead of sleeping in their 'native' soil (which is still possible for individual Tzimisce), they must rest in places that have significance to them on some level. This could be a physical location, among a certain kind of people or an organization or even more esoteric things.<br /> <br /> It's just a question as to how they handle Vicissitude, which is the next chapter.<br /> <br /> There's also write-ups on the Szlachta and Vozhd of the Tzimisce but nothing particularly noteworthy about those pages.<br /> <br /> Oh and on a sidenote, I find the character art in this chapter as one of my personal complaints about the initial V5 books was the often terrible character art, especially in the Rulebook and it's Clan write-ups. Also, one artist clearly likes Peaky Blinders.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://youtu.be/_yBS2EZFduI?t=2m13s\" target=\"_blank\">Homo sapiens. What an inventive, invincible species. It's only a few million years since they crawled up out of the mud and learned to walk. Puny, defenceless bipeds. They've survived flood, famine and plague. They've survived cosmic wars and holocausts. And now, here they are, out among the stars, waiting to begin a new life. Ready to outsit eternity. They're indomitable. Indomitable.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/420-akatsukileader13","name":"AkatsukiLeader13","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar420_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1637"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-16T09:58:03-08:00","id":1428611,"title":"","content":"Yeah, it's so-so. I like the clans. The Tzimisce seem a bit too focused now, but it's a neat twist. The Salubri are still the same but their new flaw is strange, to say the least. The Ravnos flaw is interesting.<br /> <br /> The errata was short. I was expecting more. The ghouls are good, though that first picture of a szlachta is a bit B-movie. The vozhd makes up for it, though!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-16T10:26:43-08:00","id":1428615,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Merged these two threads. </span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-16T10:30:57-08:00","id":1428617,"title":"","content":"Yeah, I too must chime in on the whole replacing Auspex with Dominate, especially with Vicissitude being a combo-Discipline with Dominate instead of a branch of Protean. I have ask, what was the thought process behind that? I could see an argument for Vicissitude being Protean/Auspex with the whole Metamorphosist angle of the Clan and the mystical aspect of Auspex. At most, I could see is using their mind to dominate their flesh or that of others.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://youtu.be/_yBS2EZFduI?t=2m13s\" target=\"_blank\">Homo sapiens. What an inventive, invincible species. It's only a few million years since they crawled up out of the mud and learned to walk. Puny, defenceless bipeds. They've survived flood, famine and plague. They've survived cosmic wars and holocausts. And now, here they are, out among the stars, waiting to begin a new life. Ready to outsit eternity. They're indomitable. Indomitable.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/420-akatsukileader13","name":"AkatsukiLeader13","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar420_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1637"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-16T10:47:18-08:00","id":1428619,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AkatsukiLeader13</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1428599-v5-vampire-companion?p=1428617#post1428617\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, I too must chime in on the whole replacing Auspex with Dominate, especially with Vicissitude being a combo-Discipline with Dominate instead of a branch of Protean. I have ask, what was the thought process behind that? I could see an argument for Vicissitude being Protean/Auspex with the whole Metamorphosist angle of the Clan and the mystical aspect of Auspex. At most, I could see is using their mind to dominate their flesh or that of others.</div> </div> </div> </div>Tzimisce spent millennia cultivating a legacy of fear and a mastery of blood bonds. They have no need for Dominate. In fact, Dominate feels counter-intuitive.<br /> <br /> Otherworldly insight, preternatural senses and psychic projections, however, feel very much in keeping with the \u201cknow it all\u201d feel of the clan, especially for the more notoriously territorial ones. Auspex will always be in-clan for Tzimisce at my tables...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24351-garygeneric","name":"Garygeneric","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24351_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"108"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-16T10:53:53-08:00","id":1428620,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1428599-v5-vampire-companion?p=1428615#post1428615\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Merged these two threads. </span></div> </div> </div> </div>the other thread got nuked","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>-</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10998-pleiades","name":"Pleiades","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10998_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1844"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-16T11:23:17-08:00","id":1428622,"title":"","content":"Overall very impressed with this, especially given the price.<br /> <br /> Love the new clan banes and compulsions, love the clan based coterie merits, ghoul and mortal merits and flaws, and the errata. Two things stood out that I found puzzling:<br /> <br /> As with others, I'm a bit of two minds on Tzimisce and Dominate. This decision seemed more about differentiating them from the other clans in this companion, and heavily reinforcing their thematic focus than on maintaining what they have been in the past lore of the game. I love the discipline powers and think Viccissitude is handeled extremely well, but I may swap Auspex for Dominate both as a clan spec and the discipline prerequisite.<br /> <br /> The other point I found odd was that mortals and ghouls were given the same attribute spread as vampires, which was not the case in prior editions nor really in keeping with the mortals present within the backgrounds of the core rulebook. Given that this makes for a somewhat more level field of play for mixed stories, I'm not sure I like that for extended play, even though it's what I did for my group's embrace session.<br /> <br /> What do you all think of the mortals and ghouls section?<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24680-jrrparker","name":"JRRParker","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"24"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-16T11:29:52-08:00","id":1428623,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Pleiades</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1428599-v5-vampire-companion?p=1428620#post1428620\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> the other thread got nuked</div> </div> </div> </div>Click the link in the second post of this thread. <br /> <br /> Well I like most of it, but I can already hear the complaints about the ravnos bane from some corners of the internet","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3953-dwight","name":"Dwight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3953_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-16T11:33:04-08:00","id":1428624,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>IllithidActivity</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1428599-v5-vampire-companion?p=1428606#post1428606\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Tzimisce I'm so-so about. I like them as being avaricious dragons, but I feel like they've lost some of the &quot;old country nobility&quot; style that they used to have.</div> </div> </div> </div>I have to disagree. I think they might be both the hungry dragon and the old country nobility. By comparison,the way Smaug is written (in the book the Hobbit, not the movies) is almost a parody of British landed gentry and the noble class.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","name":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1208_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-16T11:34:37-08:00","id":1428625,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dwight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1428599-v5-vampire-companion?p=1428623#post1428623\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Click the link in the second post of this thread</div> </div> </div> </div>That\u2019s not the thread they were referring to. The other \u201cmerged\u201d thread was 9 pages long.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24351-garygeneric","name":"Garygeneric","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24351_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"108"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-16T11:35:36-08:00","id":1428626,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JRRParker</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1428599-v5-vampire-companion?p=1428622#post1428622\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The other point I found odd was that mortals and ghouls were given the same attribute spread as vampires, which was not the case in prior editions nor really in keeping with the mortals present within the backgrounds of the core rulebook. Given that this makes for a somewhat more level field of play for mixed stories, I'm not sure I like that for extended play, even though it's what I did for my group's embrace session.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>That makes sense. In V5, you need more dice just to be a functioning character, so any spread weaker than the starting vampire spread is... pretty brutal. If you wanted weaker mortals, you'd either need to reduce the required successes by one, or perhaps two in general, or you could buff vampires more.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-16T12:08:12-08:00","id":1428630,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dwight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1428599-v5-vampire-companion?p=1428623#post1428623\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well I like most of it, but I can already hear the complaints about the ravnos bane from some corners of the internet</div> </div> </div> </div>It does seem a bit strict, but it's also not far from my guess earlier.<br /> <br /> I like the writeup for sure.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-16T12:23:49-08:00","id":1428632,"title":"","content":"It is an interesting Companion but I was hoping for more merits and flaws. <br /> Just sad that Caitiff and Salubri do not get any coterie merits.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>This space for rent.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25995-ethryo","name":"Ethryo","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"67"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-16T12:29:58-08:00","id":1428633,"title":"","content":"How does the Ravnos ability work with torpor? Is Torpor basically just Ravnos death?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3901-radiofreedeath","name":"RadioFreeDeath","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-16T12:39:53-08:00","id":1428635,"title":"","content":"That definitely needs clarification<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-16T12:43:41-08:00","id":1428637,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>RadioFreeDeath</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1428599-v5-vampire-companion?p=1428633#post1428633\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How does the Ravnos ability work with torpor? Is Torpor basically just Ravnos death?</div> </div> </div> </div>While it's not at all described, if I were the ST I would rule that being in Torpor counts as one single &quot;sleep&quot; and so you haven't slept in the same place more than once. You slept for a very long time, once. It's fiddly but I think a better option than all Ravnos burning up while they're out for a month.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25972-illithidactivity","name":"IllithidActivity","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25972_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"103"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-16T12:44:22-08:00","id":1428639,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>IllithidActivity</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1428599-v5-vampire-companion?p=1428637#post1428637\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> While it's not at all described, if I were the ST I would rule that being in Torpor counts as one single &quot;sleep&quot; and so you haven't slept in the same place more than once. You slept for a very long time, once. It's fiddly but I think a better option than all Ravnos burning up while they're out for a month.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would too, and was thinking similar.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-16T12:44:48-08:00","id":1428640,"title":"","content":"Kind of sad that the Salubri write up was focused on the Seven rather than the Antitribu. After about two decades I'd have expected them to now have an established, if minor, place in the setting. Probably helping organise the rtemnants of the Sabbat considering that the vast majority of them were far too young to feel the Beckoning. I just felt like there was this great concept for a Clan of fallen knights/bandits that was ignored for the same ting again.<br /> <br /> Also not a fan of the new Bane, enforced concentualism just clicked for me whereas this doesn't.<br /> <br /> As for the rest I have no real feelings one way or the other. I'm not on board with the Tzimisce having dominate, but I wasn't really attached to the Clan and can ignore it. For the rest I'll have to wait until I can do more than skim it, which due to work will be in a few days.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:blue\">Blue is sarcasm.</span><br /> <br /> If I suggestion I make contradicts in-setting metaphysics please ignore me, I probably brought in scientific ideas.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4507-twodsix","name":"TwoDSix","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-16T13:11:10-08:00","id":1428650,"title":"","content":"Looking at it again, the Lasombra Clan Merit seems ripe for exploitation. Once per session a coterie-mate can add two successes to a roll, and then call the roll a messy critical. Adding two successes in exchange for some kind of bestial act is probably worth it in times of need, but more importantly a messy critical is still a critical, which means you can guarantee the triggering of certain crit-only effects like ending a frenzy with Quell the Beast or creating a perfect memory with The Forgetful Mind.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25972-illithidactivity","name":"IllithidActivity","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25972_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"103"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-16T13:35:50-08:00","id":1428653,"title":"","content":"Chimestry has always been abit speed bumpy The only real loss is a &quot;do damage with illusions&quot; power which I'd probably house rule in. I'm also thinking of house ruling Ravnos as Fortitude, Presence, Obfuscate since I am not sure how well Animalism matches with them.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Salubri-I think EVERYONE wants to murder you makes more sense for their fallen state than the &quot;Everyone listened to the tremere&quot;<br /> <br /> <br /> Tzim as full dragons I like maybe some future Dragon themed amalgams","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-16T13:48:49-08:00","id":1428656,"title":"","content":"Animalism is pretty great for Ravnos. Those who develop the power can get a ton of mileage out of it, especially given they can't sleep in one place.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-16T13:55:38-08:00","id":1428658,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TwoDSix</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1428599-v5-vampire-companion?p=1428640#post1428640\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Kind of sad that the Salubri write up was focused on the Seven rather than the Antitribu. After about two decades I'd have expected them to now have an established, if minor, place in the setting. Probably helping organise the rtemnants of the Sabbat considering that the vast majority of them were far too young to feel the Beckoning. I just felt like there was this great concept for a Clan of fallen knights/bandits that was ignored for the same ting again.<br /> <br /> Also not a fan of the new Bane, enforced concentualism just clicked for me whereas this doesn't.</div> </div> </div> </div>You do realize that there's more Healers than just the Seven, right? For years now there have been scattered Salubri Healers around the world because much like the Cappadocians, word of their death has been quite exaggerated. The Seven are merely the famous ones that everyone knows about, letting the rest hide in the shadows as those crazy oddballs take all the attention.<br /> <br /> In fact, the Crimson Wedding that sealed the alliance between the Cam and the Ashirra was officiated by a Salubri Healer as the Ashirra protected the Healers for centuries.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://youtu.be/_yBS2EZFduI?t=2m13s\" target=\"_blank\">Homo sapiens. What an inventive, invincible species. It's only a few million years since they crawled up out of the mud and learned to walk. Puny, defenceless bipeds. They've survived flood, famine and plague. They've survived cosmic wars and holocausts. And now, here they are, out among the stars, waiting to begin a new life. Ready to outsit eternity. They're indomitable. Indomitable.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/420-akatsukileader13","name":"AkatsukiLeader13","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar420_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1637"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-16T13:56:47-08:00","id":1428659,"title":"","content":"Also if the Salubri antitribu get coverage I'd expect it to be in the Sabbat book.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-16T14:09:56-08:00","id":1428662,"title":"","content":"Ah so just as I suspected.. Vicissitude got merged as an &quot;Amalgam&quot; into Protean... lol...<br /> <br /> Also its an Amalgam paired with Dominate? WTF.<br /> <br /> Welp, there goes the Tzimisce.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Jade Kingdom Warrior","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","name":"Shakanaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"951"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-16T14:15:30-08:00","id":1428663,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>IllithidActivity</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1428599-v5-vampire-companion?p=1428637#post1428637\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> While it's not at all described, if I were the ST I would rule that being in Torpor counts as one single &quot;sleep&quot; and so you haven't slept in the same place more than once. You slept for a very long time, once. It's fiddly but I think a better option than all Ravnos burning up while they're out for a month.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmm, not looking good for the Ravnos<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://twitter.com/jachilli/status/1339256495800799235\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://abs.twimg.com/x-web/assets/og/default-og.a2e144f0cf66.jpg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div 