ifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-17T08:19:57-08:00","id":1428761,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>adambeyoncelowe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1428599-v5-vampire-companion?p=1428755#post1428755\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I believe they're separate things. At least, the press releases seemed to suggest so.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't see what else you could put in there at this point that would have any substance that isn't covered by any other book. Loresheets only get you so far.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3953-dwight","name":"Dwight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3953_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-17T08:24:54-08:00","id":1428762,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dwight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1428599-v5-vampire-companion?p=1428750#post1428750\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think this *was* the players guide Modiphius had planned to put out.</div> </div> </div> </div>The book is nice, very nice given it is free. But it feels rather slim for a full Players Guide. There are no lore sheets, no new blood sorcery rituals, a minimum of new amalgams, and no sections on advice for various issues. So there is still room for a PG - particularly if it should provide information on bloodlines, or guidance on designing a bloodline.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","name":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1208_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-17T10:53:13-08:00","id":1428776,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Grumpy RPG Reviews</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1428599-v5-vampire-companion?p=1428762#post1428762\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The book is nice, very nice given it is free. But it feels rather slim for a full Players Guide. There are no lore sheets, no new blood sorcery rituals, a minimum of new amalgams, and no sections on advice for various issues. So there is still room for a PG - particularly if it should provide information on bloodlines, or guidance on designing a bloodline.</div> </div> </div> </div>My impression is that this is probably half or a third of the book that they planned to do. However, it's all that they managed to get done and that may be related to why WOD severed their contract.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-17T11:18:04-08:00","id":1428779,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1428599-v5-vampire-companion?p=1428744#post1428744\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you need dominate to be a leader, you're a shitty leader.</div> </div> </div> </div>that's definitely what v5 is selling, with their 12th gen neonate princes, thinblooded primogen and whatnot,<br /> <br /> and I'm surprised you, of all people, would be the one echoing the v5 ideal<br /> <br /> so, what's next for the sabbat in your opinion? revenant Archbishops? thinblooded Regent?<br /> <br /> no thanks, I like my (sabbat) Tzimisce as powerful leaders,<br /> maybe &quot;shitty&quot; leaders, but still powerful leaders,<br /> <br /> previously, they had koldunism for power, but that wasn't very accessible to player characters,<br /> now they have dominate and protean in clan, which is more player friendly<br /> <br /> it might be one of the few v5 decision I wholeheartedly agree with","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>-</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10998-pleiades","name":"Pleiades","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10998_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1844"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-17T11:56:42-08:00","id":1428783,"title":"","content":"Tzmisce aren't meant to be 'powerful leaders', they're meant to be Lords of the Land. Tzmisce leadership sucks, they're fuedal; organizing Tzmisce is like herding stray cats. It's why they couldn't wreck the nascent Tremere despite the home-field advantage; they never left their homes when the collective wanted them to. They're a clan of individualists. Auspex let them survey their lands and Animalism had their faithful hounds guard them. Vicissitude is a resource. They're too anti-social to be a Dominate clan.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":11}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-17T12:08:53-08:00","id":1428784,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1428599-v5-vampire-companion?p=1428783#post1428783\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Tzmisce aren't meant to be 'powerful leaders', they're meant to be Lords of the Land. Tzmisce leadership sucks, they're fuedal; organizing Tzmisce is like herding stray cats. It's why they couldn't wreck the nascent Tremere despite the home-field advantage; they never left their homes when the collective wanted them to. They're a clan of individualists. Auspex let them survey their lands and Animalism had their faithful hounds guard them. Vicissitude is a resource. They're too anti-social to be a Dominate clan.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would also add that it was their overconfidence in, and over-reliance on, their perceived iron-clad control through fear and blood bonds that led to their downfall in the Anarch revolt. A clan-wide mastery of Dominate changes the entire dynamic of the clan\u2019s history and lore, not just their role in the Sabbat.<br /> <br /> I wouldn\u2019t be against Dominate as an option, but definitely not status quo.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24351-garygeneric","name":"Garygeneric","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24351_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"108"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-17T12:10:28-08:00","id":1428785,"title":"","content":"So if bloodlines 2 is supposed to mirror V5 does that mean if you play a ravnos you can't use the same save location twice in a row?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3953-dwight","name":"Dwight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3953_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-17T12:26:28-08:00","id":1428786,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dwight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1428599-v5-vampire-companion?p=1428785#post1428785\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So if bloodlines 2 is supposed to mirror V5 does that mean if you play a ravnos you can't use the same save location twice in a row?</div> </div> </div> </div>you can, you just risk getting a few burns if you do so,<br /> not sure how often that happens though,<br /> my brain isn't very good with statistics<br /> <br /> well, regardless of statistics, I have to say I love the Ravnos this time around,<br /> they're definitely the most improved clan,<br /> I just hope they don't make them into an anarch clan<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1428599-v5-vampire-companion?p=1428783#post1428783\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Auspex let them survey their lands and Animalism had their faithful hounds guard them.</div> </div> </div> </div>no, koldunism allowed them to survey their land,<br /> they had faithful spirits (+hounds, +ghouls, +revenants, +whatever) to guard them","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>-</b>","edited":{"userid":10998,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10998-pleiades","user":"Pleiades","date":". 12-17-2020, 03:29 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10998-pleiades","name":"Pleiades","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10998_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1844"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-17T12:27:46-08:00","id":1428787,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Garygeneric</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1428599-v5-vampire-companion?p=1428784#post1428784\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I would also add that it was their overconfidence in, and over-reliance on, their perceived iron-clad control through fear and blood bonds that led to their downfall in the Anarch revolt. A clan-wide mastery of Dominate changes the entire dynamic of the clan\u2019s history and lore, not just their role in the Sabbat.<br /> <br /> I wouldn\u2019t be against Dominate as an option, but definitely not status quo.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> It also makes the development of Revenant Families and the over reliance on Ghouls a thing that there was never any need for if they had Dominate. <br /> <br /> I wonder if perhaps they're just erasing the clan schism between Old Clan and Main Clan as never happening.<br /> <br /> Eh, not my problem. Its not like I'm going to play V5 again anyway its definetely going to confuse folks though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-17T12:31:43-08:00","id":1428788,"title":"","content":"Impressions:<br /> <br /> * Ravnos. Swapping &quot;Ravnos are compulsive thieves because being thieves is a Roma stereotype&quot; for &quot;Ravnos are nomadic because being nomadic is a Roma stereotype&quot; sure was a move. I guess the saving throw here is that &quot;Ravnos are associated with the Roma&quot; is being retconned, because neither Roma nor India are ever mentioned and the two art pieces are a Japanese woman and an African Man.<br /> ** Chimerstry seems mostly useless to me, compared to existing powerful Presence powers you can take at 2. Fata Morgana is fine, though kinda steep difficulty-wise.<br /> <br /> * Salubri. You'd think with the fall of the Pyramid would bring the clan to resurgence, but no. The new Bane is really bad. It's bad thematically because it's basically victim-blaming the Salubri genocide on the Salubri just being too delicious. It's bad mechanically because any time you use any of your vampire powers, your coterie mates frenzy and kill you.<br /> ** Obeah isn't great at chargen, but if you do get your dicepool to 10 you can pretty reliably throw around Willpower. So it's kinda like Blood Surge with extra steps. The limitation on the number of people healed is really dumb and doesn't need to be there.<br /> ** Valeren is real bad. You can only use it on vampires, and vampires can already heal themselves. To heal aggravated wounds you need 5 successes, and you are not doing that any time soon.<br /> ** Unburdening the Bestial Soul is a fine concept, but it should really be against 10-Humanity. Low Humanity vampires don't need a shield against Stains, they can already eat up a boatload of Stains and be fine. As is Unburdening helps the most the people who need it the least.<br /> <br /> * Tzimisce. No particular thoughts. It's fine. They are fine.<br /> ** Fleshcrafting RAW takes the <i>Tzimisce's</i> attribute points to apply changes to someone else, and there's no mention if you ever get them back as you do with Vicissitude.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12892-kammerer","name":"Kammerer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12892_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-17T13:20:06-08:00","id":1428791,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1428599-v5-vampire-companion?p=1428725#post1428725\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">it's a pitty that now one has to choose between their own invisibility or Masks and illusions due to the 5-power limit.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's one of the things I dislike about V5. I don't mourn the demise of 6+ Disciplines and demigod Methuselahs - I disliked both - but allowing elder characters to trade great versatility for power would be better than forcing their Discipline development to a screeching halt <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/100-jezmiller","name":"JezMiller","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"437"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-17T13:21:46-08:00","id":1428792,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Pleiades</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1428599-v5-vampire-companion?p=1428786#post1428786\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">my brain isn't very good with statistics</div> </div> </div> </div>Now that the Bane Severity for Blood Potency 1 has increased to 2, there's a 19% chance of getting an Aggravated Damage for revisiting a sleeping space within a week. Those are some pretty harsh odds.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kammerer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1428599-v5-vampire-companion?p=1428788#post1428788\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">** Fleshcrafting RAW takes the <i>Tzimisce's</i> attribute points to apply changes to someone else, and there's no mention if you ever get them back as you do with Vicissitude.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, that was just some outright sloppy writing. To say &quot;Each change causes the loss of a single Physical Attribute dot of the user&quot; under plain Vicissitude, which makes sense since you can only do it to yourself, but then just referring back to Vicissitude and not changing the phrasing for Fleshcrafting. If they had said &quot;Each change causes the loss of a single Physical Attribute dot of the recipient&quot; or something like that (which I imagine is what they must have intended) then that would have solved that.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25972-illithidactivity","name":"IllithidActivity","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25972_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"103"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-17T13:23:53-08:00","id":1428793,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1428599-v5-vampire-companion?p=1428783#post1428783\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Tzmisce aren't meant to be 'powerful leaders', they're meant to be Lords of the Land. Tzmisce leadership sucks, they're fuedal; organizing Tzmisce is like herding stray cats. It's why they couldn't wreck the nascent Tremere despite the home-field advantage; they never left their homes when the collective wanted them to. They're a clan of individualists. Auspex let them survey their lands and Animalism had their faithful hounds guard them. Vicissitude is a resource. They're too anti-social to be a Dominate clan.</div> </div> </div> </div>I feel the need to state that, of course, I am ecstatic with the more Dark Ages-esque Tzimisce in Modern Nights.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-17T13:25:25-08:00","id":1428794,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Grumpy RPG Reviews</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1428599-v5-vampire-companion?p=1428697#post1428697\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I like the temperamental, or maybe thematic, change to the Tzimisce. That is them moving from an alien spiritually to greedy dragons.</div> </div> </div> </div>There was always a division between the alien-spirituality types like Yorak and the warlords like Rustovitch. I suspect that this change is the first part of formalizing that, with the warlords becoming the clan's dominant faction and the kolduns either being a bloodline or just interested in studying Blood Sorcery and Auspex as out-of-clan Disciplines - but a minority faction in either case.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/100-jezmiller","name":"JezMiller","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"437"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-17T13:29:42-08:00","id":1428795,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>IllithidActivity</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1428599-v5-vampire-companion?p=1428792#post1428792\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Now that the Bane Severity for Blood Potency 1 has increased to 2, there's a 19% chance of getting an Aggravated Damage for revisiting a sleeping space within a week. Those are some pretty harsh odds.</div> </div> </div> </div>ouch<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JezMiller</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1428599-v5-vampire-companion?p=1428791#post1428791\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's one of the things I dislike about V5. I don't mourn the demise of 6+ Disciplines and demigod Methuselahs - I disliked both - but allowing elder characters to trade great versatility for power would be better than forcing their Discipline development to a screeching halt</div> </div> </div> </div>surprised they didn't mention that in the errata, I was certain they were gonna retcon it","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>-</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10998-pleiades","name":"Pleiades","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10998_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1844"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-17T13:38:12-08:00","id":1428797,"title":"","content":"I like it for the most part. Where I don't know how I feel about it jet, it is easily fixed by houserules. (Playing Tzimisce with Auspex for example)<br /> <br /> The Ravnos write up is fitting, but I was always rather fond of the Indian Ravnos. (It's just to bad that they got their best incarnation after they were nuked)<br /> The Bane applying to in Torpor seems fitting. After all most of them are supposed to be dead.<br /> <br /> All in all, great for a free product. Particularly the Art.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1428599-v5-vampire-companion?p=1428776#post1428776\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> My impression is that this is probably half or a third of the book that they planned to do. However, it's all that they managed to get done and that may be related to why WOD severed their contract.</div> </div> </div> </div> Mhm, I think a players guide that takes what is here, maybe improves upon things after they have been out and tested for a while and then collects all the Clan write ups, new rules, Loresheets etc. that are currently spread out across too many books, adds some more and maybe one or two extra chapters would be fine with me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25507,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25507-nobby","user":"nobby","date":". 12-18-2020, 03:39 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25507-nobby","name":"nobby","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25507_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"66"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-17T13:45:02-08:00","id":1428800,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1428599-v5-vampire-companion?p=1428783#post1428783\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Tzmisce aren't meant to be 'powerful leaders', they're meant to be Lords of the Land. Tzmisce leadership sucks, they're fuedal; organizing Tzmisce is like herding stray cats. It's why they couldn't wreck the nascent Tremere despite the home-field advantage; they never left their homes when the collective wanted them to. They're a clan of individualists. Auspex let them survey their lands and Animalism had their faithful hounds guard them. Vicissitude is a resource. They're too anti-social to be a Dominate clan.</div> </div> </div> </div>Their slogan in this Companion is:<br /> <br /> &quot;Not to lead, not to triumph, but to rule \u2014 to own utterly&quot;<br /> <br /> Half of the archetypes are leaders, but that leadership is incidental. They are described as bad leaders; their domains can show severe neglect and they don't feel obligated to do anything for their subjects. All that that matters is that their domain remains theirs or grows. Leadership serves as a socially acceptable front for ownership. Dominate as written may not be ideal for that because it they still need to roll social attributes*, but it can allow them to ignore social <i>skills</i>. Clans without Dominate have to negotiate.<br /> <br /> *Although the same attributes are needed for Animalism.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3523,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3523-spencer-from-the-hills","user":"Spencer from The Hills","date":". 12-17-2020, 05:59 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3523-spencer-from-the-hills","name":"Spencer from The Hills","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"546"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-17T13:58:22-08:00","id":1428802,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JezMiller</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1428599-v5-vampire-companion?p=1428791#post1428791\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's one of the things I dislike about V5. I don't mourn the demise of 6+ Disciplines and demigod Methuselahs - I disliked both - but allowing elder characters to trade great versatility for power would be better than forcing their Discipline development to a screeching halt</div> </div> </div> </div>Wait.. what? You dislike 6+ Elder Disciplines, but then say you don't like that their development now has been borked with how V5 is working it with Caps and limited power slots per dot? Sorry, I'm not really understanding your logic here.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Jade Kingdom Warrior","edited":{"userid":25523,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","user":"Shakanaka","date":". 12-17-2020, 05:02 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","name":"Shakanaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"951"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-17T14:08:40-08:00","id":1428803,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Pleiades</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1428599-v5-vampire-companion?p=1428795#post1428795\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">surprised they didn't mention that in the errata, I was certain they were gonna retcon it</div> </div> </div> </div>Me too. I wonder if an &quot;Elders&quot; book is in the works?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/100-jezmiller","name":"JezMiller","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"437"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-17T14:28:40-08:00","id":1428805,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shakanaka</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1428599-v5-vampire-companion?p=1428802#post1428802\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Wait.. what? You dislike 6+ Elder Disciplines, but then say you don't like that their development now has been borked with how V5 is working it with Caps and limited power slots per dot? Sorry, I'm not really understanding your logic here.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I'm not interested in elders with level 9 Presence powers that can affect entire cities<br /> I don't see why an elder character should have to sacrifice Earth Meld if they want the wolf, bat and mist forms<br /> <br /> As I said - power and versatility","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/100-jezmiller","name":"JezMiller","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"437"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-17T14:52:57-08:00","id":1428806,"title":"","content":"Well that's the thing. 6+ Powers allowed Elders to have all their abilities without anything having to be nonsensically slotted out for gameplay reasons. V5 is anti-versatility in this regard and is not made for Elder playstyles in mind. Also a level 9 Discipline is basically Antediluvian level of Discipline or in the ballpark of 8000+ year old Methuselahs having them (such as Baba Yaga). Elders as we know it shouldn't and don't have that range at all so your perceived complaint is nonsensical.<br /> <br /> (EDIT: And even then, Baba Yaga herself doesn't even HAVE a 9+ Discipline. The only ability she has in 9 via her stat sheet is Thaumaturgy and that's not an inherent Discipline Cainites possess, you have to learn it all yourself (it also helped that the Baba Yaga was already a Shaman pre-Embrace already). All of her &quot;natural&quot; Disciplines that are non-Thaumaturgy are 8 or 7 at the highest)<br /> <br /> Most of the complaints against 6+ Disciplines are just aggreaved theoretics on scenarios that have never happened in their chronicles or fiats of just having a bad ST than good arguments against 6+ Disciplines; especially concerning with what we're left with in V5 as of now.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Jade Kingdom Warrior","edited":{"userid":25523,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","user":"Shakanaka","date":". 12-17-2020, 06:04 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","name":"Shakanaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"951"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-17T18:14:00-08:00","id":1428818,"title":"","content":"You don't need to be 8000+ years old to have a Discipline at nine dots. Children of the Night suggests giving vampires a number of Discipline dots equal to the square root of their age, but offers no guidelines other than what works for your chronicle. When you say that a Discipline level is basically Antediluvian, that's 10 dots. The number you can have when you're 3rd generation.<br /> <br /> Most methuselahs in VtM aren't written with nine dots, but that's not a rule that anyone set. That's just the way they were written. If Menele and Helena can have at least one eight dot discipline at 3,000 years you're not looking at waiting another 5,000 for that last dot.<br /> <br /> Thaumaturgy is absolutely a discipline and as such yes it does count as a nine dot discipline.<br /> <br /> It's fine to have opinions, and &quot;it takes a long time to get nine dots&quot; is a fine opinion, but it's not a book rule. If it were, you wouldn't have to look at methuselah character sheets to cite all the 8s (and handwave a 9 away) as evidence.<br /> <br /> Limiting Disciplines to 5 dots is fine. It's a valid game design choice with its own consequences, In this case it means not having elders and methuselahs who can, I don't know, view a distant location and dominate everyone there telepathically or whatever. It's not game breaking, and there are a lot of reasons for making such a choice as Justin Achilli did when developing Vampire: The Requiem, which worked out fairly well for that game. People do have good reasons for preferring it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2367,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","user":"Resplendent Fire","date":". 12-17-2020, 09:34 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-17T18:28:47-08:00","id":1428819,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shakanaka</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1428599-v5-vampire-companion?p=1428712#post1428712\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Eh, its just some simple Inductive Reasoning with how everything in this edition has been panning out so far. Though I am certainly hopeful my prediction isn't right, but again, that's just really hopeful.</div> </div> </div> </div>V5 is under new management, and Justin has treated the Sabbat well in the past.<br /> <br /> I do understand your feelings about how everything's panned out so far. I've been pretty turned off due to several storyline/metaplot decisions.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-17T20:40:19-08:00","id":1428826,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Damian May</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1428599-v5-vampire-companion?p=1428787#post1428787\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> It also makes the development of Revenant Families and the over reliance on Ghouls a thing that there was never any need for if they had Dominate.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I assumed they overelied on ghouls and Revenant Families because they're a bunch of flesh-crafting mad scientists.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-17T21:16:23-08:00","id":1428829,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1428599-v5-vampire-companion?p=1428826#post1428826\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I assumed they overelied on ghouls and Revenant Families because they're a bunch of flesh-crafting mad scientists.</div> </div> </div> </div>When centuries of breeding won't get you the perfect servants drastic measures need to be taken for the desired results","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3953-dwight","name":"Dwight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3953_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-17T21:33:41-08:00","id":1428830,"title":"","content":"I think people are exaggerating the impact of Tzimisce having Dominate. That's usually a one-on-one power, not a group power like Presence can be. I don't think it can just eliminate the need for other methods.<br /> <br /> Plus, it's not as if there's ever been a firewall between Kindred and the common out of clan disciplines (Animalism, Auspex, Celerity, Dominate, Fortitude, Obfuscate, Potence, Presence). Tzimisce with dominate aren't a new thing, just having it as a clan discipline.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2367,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","user":"Resplendent Fire","date":". 12-18-2020, 12:37 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-17T21:47:11-08:00","id":1428831,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Resplendent Fire</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Most methuselahs in VtM aren't written with nine dots, but that's not a rule that anyone set. That's just the way they were written. If Menele and Helena can have at least one eight dot discipline at 3,000 years you're not looking at waiting another 5,000 for that last dot.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, the rules didn't say anything explicitly, so I simply observe from the few instances of precedent to take from (i.e how they were written in the first place). Baba Yaga who's 7000+ years old (much more than Menele and Helena) doesn't have any &quot;natural&quot; Disciplines in 9 at all. Thaumaturgy is a not a &quot;natural&quot; Discipline that is in-built from among the spread of Cainites, nowhere did I say Thaumaturgy was NOT a Discipline. And further, Thaumaturgy is something you have to especially get out on your own to learn.<br /> <br /> The fact Baba Yaga has a 9 in Thaum is easily tied to the fact of her pre-Embrace background (because y'know, she was literally a Shaman). If Baba Yaga hasn't gotten 1 natural Cainite Discipline to 9 and she's 7000+ years old.. It basically blows the notion that &quot;Menele and Helena can have at least one eight dot discipline at 3,000 years you're not looking at waiting another 5,000 for that last dot&quot; (and Baba Yaga isn't getting any of that anytime soon because Final Death).<br /> <br /> The main meat of what I was speaking about was Elders primarily, extrapolated on what Discipline range they should realistically have from written material; so yes, that's why I'm looking how Elders should contrast from Methuselahs and Antediluvians because there aren't outright written rules. If his ST (since they dictate the story, taking into account what to put in and what not) is bringing in Elders with a 9 Discipline, that's on his ST doing something iffy than any valid argument against 6+ Disciplines. I just find his argument funny because 6+ Disciplines has what he desires of having everything being intact and not slotted out, while still having versatility in the fact powers don't have to be have to be left out for a certain one and 6+ Disciplines having more &quot;omph&quot;.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Resplendent Fire</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Limiting Disciplines to 5 dots is fine. It's a valid game design choice with its own consequences, In this case it means not having elders and methuselahs who can, I don't know, view a distant location and dominate everyone there telepathically or whatever.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah so its perfectly valid that now STs (or *gasp* PLAYERS xxxxD) don't have no resources at all to work with if they every want an Elder playstyle or emulation. Its perfectly valid that in Tabletop games that is supposed to have infinite avenues on how it can be taken, more advanced Disciplines are completely capped off and locked away for some nonsensical reason and a major part of the VTM setting (Elders) just up and left... Funny.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Resplendent Fire</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's not game breaking, and there are a lot of reasons for making such a choice as Justin Achilli did when developing Vampire: The Requiem, which worked out fairly well for that game.</div> </div> </div> </div>VTR is its own game. Its good, but its not VTM and the lines are different for reason catering for different things. To have VTR shoved in VTM?.... no, just no.<br /> <br /> Also with V5 Mechanic logic, things that were done before it came out just isn't possible anymore or just as wonky logics to attempt to justify them in (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1417738-how-do-i-explain-sleeping-methuselah-powers-in-v5\">How do I explain sleeping methuselah powers in V5? - Onyx Path Forums (theonyxpath.com)</a>) regards to Elders or other higher level Vampires.. It's pretty on the nose to say it's not game breaking..<br /> <br /> EDIT: And actually its bizarre. That example the poster gave was like a reference to Michael.. but what are the odds of that character ever being in a chronicle they'd run at all? lol. Again, aggreaved theoretics.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Jade Kingdom Warrior","edited":{"userid":25523,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","user":"Shakanaka","date":". 12-18-2020, 01:09 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","name":"Shakanaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"951"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-18T04:57:51-08:00","id":1428843,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Resplendent Fire</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1428599-v5-vampire-companion?p=1428830#post1428830\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think people are exaggerating the impact of Tzimisce having Dominate. That's usually a one-on-one power, not a group power like Presence can be. I don't think it can just eliminate the need for other methods.<br /> <br /> Plus, it's not as if there's ever been a firewall between Kindred and the common out of clan disciplines (Animalism, Auspex, Celerity, Dominate, Fortitude, Obfuscate, Potence, Presence). Tzimisce with dominate aren't a new thing, just having it as a clan discipline.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean, what Tzimisce has Dominate!<br /> <br /> You know...aside from DRACULA.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-18T05:08:56-08:00","id":1428844,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1428599-v5-vampire-companion?p=1428843#post1428843\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I mean, what Tzimisce has Dominate!<br /> <br /> You know...aside from DRACULA.</div> </div> </div> </div>a tzimisce on power and the inner voice or cathari is gonna want some dominate or presence","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>-</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10998-pleiades","name":"Pleiades","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10998_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1844"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-18T05:09:39-08:00","id":1428845,"title":"","content":"As much as I would like to throw in my Opinion on Elders in V5, I\u00b4ve seen this tango danced before, so lets not get back to the old back and forth here but maybe make a new Thread so we wont derail another Thead...<br /> <br /> For the Companion:<br /> I like the Salubri write-up the most, Obeah and Valeren seem to me like a &quot;downtime activity&quot; with an O-Shit-Button Potential.<br /> I am a little confused why they would include Armor in Vicissitude and the Horrid Form, since it does basicly nothing for Vampires...<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26305-takeochan","name":"TakeoChan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26305_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"39"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-18T05:43:31-08:00","id":1428849,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1428599-v5-vampire-companion?p=1428843#post1428843\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I mean, what Tzimisce has Dominate!<br /> <br /> You know...aside from DRACULA.</div> </div> </div> </div>Dracula could mesmerize, sure (Animalism 3?), but Van Helsing was the superior hypnotist and he was just some old dude.<br /> <br /> Dracula also had the strength of 20 men, so Potence is arguably the better In Clan option over Dominate, by that logic.<br /> <br /> I\u2019m not even as much against them having Dominate as I\u2019m angry they\u2019ve lost their heightened senses, telepathy, far sight, prognostication, oracular abilities, psychic/spirit vision, etc, etc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24351-garygeneric","name":"Garygeneric","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24351_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"108"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-18T06:02:12-08:00","id":1428852,"title":"","content":"If we want to dig real deep into the discussions of Dracula, then the majority of Dracula's supernatural powers don't come from being a vampire. They come from him being a sorcerer taught by the Devil at Scholomance.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The Draculas were, says Arminius, a great and noble race, though now and again were scions who were held by their coevals to have had dealings with the Evil One. They learned his secrets in the Scholomance, amongst the mountains over Lake Hermanstadt, where the devil claims the tenth scholar as his due. In the records are such words as 'stregoica' witch, 'ordog' and 'pokol' Satan and hell, and in one manuscript this very Dracula is spoken of as 'wampyr,' which we all understand too well. </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12892-kammerer","name":"Kammerer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12892_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-18T07:11:03-08:00","id":1428856,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Damian May</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1428599-v5-vampire-companion?p=1428787#post1428787\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It also makes the development of Revenant Families and the over reliance on Ghouls a thing that there was never any need for if they had Dominate.</div> </div> </div> </div>Just because the Fiends want to own everything doesn't mean they are competent managers or that they might want to do all the busy work of actual leadership. They probably designate authority and actual management responsibilities to some ghoul or servant while they (they Tzimisce) go and see how many arms they can add to the newest prisoner and still have the prisoner capable of walking across the room.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","name":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1208_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-18T08:09:57-08:00","id":1428863,"title":"","content":"My pick for them was:<br /> <br /> * Animalism<br /> * Blood Sorcery<br /> * Protean<br /> <br /> I also would have Vicissitude effects on other people as Blood Sorcery rituals.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-18T08:37:16-08:00","id":1428865,"title":"","content":"My Pick for them was<br /> <br /> Animalism<br /> Auspex<br /> Vicissitude. <br /> <br /> The perfect combination, the summary of who this clan are. Why fix what was perfect?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":12}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-18T09:13:16-08:00","id":1428870,"title":"","content":"The new One With The Land power was clearly written to give Tzimisce (and Gangrel?) an option to have intel-gathering in a wide range around their territory, so it seems that the writers knew that the Tzimisce were supposed to be able to know what's going on in their domain. With that in mind it feels weird that they'd remove Auspex, the discipline that lets you do exactly that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25972-illithidactivity","name":"IllithidActivity","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25972_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"103"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-18T09:16:52-08:00","id":1428871,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>IllithidActivity</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1428599-v5-vampire-companion?p=1428870#post1428870\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> With that in mind it feels weird that they'd remove Auspex, the discipline that lets you do exactly that.</div> </div> </div> </div>because they already have animalism for that","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>-</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10998-pleiades","name":"Pleiades","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10998_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1844"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-18T09:29:36-08:00","id":1428872,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>IllithidActivity</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1428599-v5-vampire-companion?p=1428870#post1428870\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The new One With The Land power was clearly written to give Tzimisce (and Gangrel?) an option to have intel-gathering in a wide range around their territory, so it seems that the writers knew that the Tzimisce were supposed to be able to know what's going on in their domain. With that in mind it feels weird that they'd remove Auspex, the discipline that lets you do exactly that.</div> </div> </div> </div>The flavor definitely fits the clan, but there is a lot (too much?) of exclusivity with Protean and Vicissitude powers now, in my opinion. To get OWtL, you also need Earthmeld. As much as I love Earthmeld for Tzimisce characters, it now means bumping off a traditional Vicissitude power. Two actually, if you also want OWtL.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24351-garygeneric","name":"Garygeneric","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24351_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"108"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-18T10:00:35-08:00","id":1428875,"title":"","content":"IMO, Tzimisce are just narrower than before. That seems to be the design intent in V5, but you do lose those other variations at the edges of the broader concept this way.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-18T10:31:34-08:00","id":1428879,"title":"","content":"So who's making a Tzimisce with a collection of anime wafiu body pillows as their thing?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3953-dwight","name":"Dwight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3953_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-18T10:54:00-08:00","id":1428882,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1428599-v5-vampire-companion?p=1428865#post1428865\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My Pick for them was<br /> <br /> Animalism<br /> Auspex<br /> Vicissitude.<br /> <br /> The perfect combination, the summary of who this clan are. Why fix what was perfect?</div> </div> </div> </div>How exactly does that reflect Dracula?<br /> <br /> Seriously.<br /> <br /> Mind you, I've never really felt Auspex was a good fit for the Tzimisce. Nothing about them screams &quot;Oracle&quot;, &quot;Super-Senses&quot;, or &quot;Psychic.&quot; It was just the random Discipline they could give them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 12-18-2020, 01:56 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-18T11:34:09-08:00","id":1428887,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1428599-v5-vampire-companion?p=1428882#post1428882\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> How exactly does that reflect Dracula?</div> </div> </div> </div>Dracula is a Tzmisce, Tzmisce are not Dracula. <br /> <br /> <br /> Also, Auspex is a -OF FUCKING COURSE THEY HAVE AUSPEX- Discipline for Tzmisce. They're an immensely territorial clan, probably THE most territorial clan, and they need to keep an eye out. They're surgeons, messing with the absurdly complicated human body with their <i>Fingers</i> , they need to sense a level of detail. They also get off on weirdly sussing out guests, looking for mistakes they're making, trying to find an excuse to go YOU ARE A BAD GUEST and turn people into research materials. <br /> Finally, as a clan of surgeons, if not wizards, they value mental attributes far beyond social and physical attributes. That might not be such an issue with v5's system, but Auspex is <i>The </i>discipline for clans of clever people. Malkavians? Auspex. Tremere? Auspex. Capadocians? Auspex. Assamite Viziers? Auspex. Toreador.... erm.... generalists, but some of them are very clever; Auspex. Tzmisce are the clever people.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":10}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-18T11:39:47-08:00","id":1428889,"title":"","content":"Fortunately, my ST agrees with my sentiments. He just sent me this:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> &quot;Tzimisce are a clan of metamorphosis and this has become expressed not just in individuals, but the clan itself. Within the Tzimisce family are varying bloodlines which focus on different aspects of their nature. Historically, Tzimisce produced its share seers and Koldunic sorcerers. Tzimisce characters can substitute Auspex or (at storyteller discretion) Blood Sorcerery for Dominate.<br /> <br /> There is more than one way to flay a cat, and the Tzimisce know them all. The clan infamously taps deep into their Protean abilities finding methods to fine tune their appearance or even alter the appearances of others. Through various methods, whether by tapping into the essence of the blood or reaching into the very mind and soul, Tzimisce have discovered many paths to Vicissitude. Tzimisce can replace the Dominate requirement in Vicissitude Amalgams with Auspex or Blood Sorcery if either of those have been taken as one of their clan disciplines.&quot; </div> </div> </div>Not sure if that helps inspire anyone else, but I thought I\u2019d share, see how it landed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24351-garygeneric","name":"Garygeneric","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24351_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"108"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-18T12:25:55-08:00","id":1428895,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1428599-v5-vampire-companion?p=1428863#post1428863\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My pick for them was:<br /> <br /> * Animalism<br /> * Blood Sorcery<br /> * Protean<br /> <br /> I also would have Vicissitude effects on other people as Blood Sorcery rituals.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I thought Justin had stated that Viscittitude was back. Because what ever those...things are they are not Tzimisce, Also, They mention a Tzim having Feral weapons and Viscittitude, that isn't possible, they are both protean 2, so only one can be picked.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25011,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","user":"Taggie","date":". 12-18-2020, 03:32 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","name":"Taggie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1047"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-18T12:26:18-08:00","id":1428896,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1428599-v5-vampire-companion?p=1428863#post1428863\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My pick for them was:<br /> <br /> * Animalism<br /> * Blood Sorcery<br /> * Protean<br /> <br /> I also would have Vicissitude effects on other people as Blood Sorcery rituals.</div> </div> </div> </div>I like that, but would have replaced Animalism with Presence.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","name":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1208_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-18T12:29:11-08:00","id":1428898,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1428599-v5-vampire-companion?p=1428882#post1428882\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> How exactly does that reflect Dracula?<br /> <br /> Seriously.<br /> <br /> Mind you, I've never really felt Auspex was a good fit for the Tzimisce. Nothing about them screams &quot;Oracle&quot;, &quot;Super-Senses&quot;, or &quot;Psychic.&quot; It was just the random Discipline they could give them.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Stop talking about Dracula, he was made a Tzim because he was a fictional Slavic character and all slavs had to be Tzim. He should have been a Ventrue, and left Tzim to have actually interesting characters and good stories. Dracula is not interesting, he is not fun, and he should never be used to state what Tzim should be, he is a racist stereotype made even worse by WW, nothing more.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25011,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","user":"Taggie","date":". 12-18-2020, 03:36 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","name":"Taggie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1047"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-18T12:43:42-08:00","id":1428902,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Grumpy RPG Reviews</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1428599-v5-vampire-companion?p=1428896#post1428896\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I like that, but would have replaced Animalism with Presence.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's starting to sound like more Telyavelic Tremere. I don't dislike the concept, but I wouldn't give up a load of sentry owls, enhanced Bratovitch dogs and an armoured bear for it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3523-spencer-from-the-hills","name":"Spencer from The Hills","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"546"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-18T12:57:11-08:00","id":1428904,"title":"","content":"The old clan tzimize had dominate instead of vissitude. So it shouldn't be that strange that they have it.<br /> I'm surprised ravnos lost fortitude and chimerstry and got obfuscate and presence. Although their new spread of disciplines looks pretty good","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/19506-killtron","name":"Killtron","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar19506_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"38"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-18T13:41:54-08:00","id":1428909,"title":"","content":"If anything, I'd expect the Ravnos who specialized in Fortitude to be disproportionately represented in survivors of the Week of Nightmares. Oh well, overall I like what's been done with the clan.<br /> <br /> I'm not so thrilled by the Salubri, but then again I never have been except for the <i>antitubu</i> in the 3rd Ed. Sabbat book.<br /> <br /> I like the back to basics approach to the Tzimisce, more of traditional folkloric vampires and less of body mod obsession for shock value. Vicissitude has been de-emphasized into a useful tool rather than a raison d'etre. Looks like the Old Clan has been folded back into the main body, with the division between the two being a matter of location and attitude rather than some fundamental difference of the blood. Good.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-18T13:54:01-08:00","id":1428910,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taggie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1428599-v5-vampire-companion?p=1428898#post1428898\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Stop talking about Dracula, he was made a Tzim because he was a fictional Slavic character and all slavs had to be Tzim. He should have been a Ventrue, and left Tzim to have actually interesting characters and good stories. Dracula is not interesting, he is not fun, and he should never be used to state what Tzim should be, he is a racist stereotype made even worse by WW, nothing more.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Honestly the obsession with Dracula in regard to the Tzimisce has now made unequivalently hate everything Dracula with a passion. The only thing Tzimisce have with Dracula as a broad theme is that they're both slavic. Beyond that the main themes of the Tzimisce have been literally akin to the Wamphyri/Necroscope thematics with their Flesh-Crafting and like. They're meant to be weird and obsessed with biology, crafting flesh and bone.. With V5 just Amalgamming Vicissitude into Protean and it being a splice of Dominate ontop of it... Its completely crap on a crapsicle-stick.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Jade Kingdom Warrior","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","name":"Shakanaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"951"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-18T13:58:53-08:00","id":1428911,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taggie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1428599-v5-vampire-companion?p=1428895#post1428895\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I thought Justin had stated that Viscittitude was back. Because what ever those...things are they are not Tzimisce, Also, They mention a Tzim having Feral weapons and Viscittitude, that isn't possible, they are both protean 2, so only one can be picked.</div> </div> </div> </div>Wrong. They are VERY Tzimisce. I shall in fact assume the status of &quot;Best Tzimisce Fan&quot; and claim you are not a fan because I am gateekeeping. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shakanaka</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1428599-v5-vampire-companion?p=1428910#post1428910\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Honestly the obsession with Dracula in regard to the Tzimisce has now made unequivalently hate everything Dracula with a passion. The only thing Tzimisce have with Dracula as a broad theme is that they're both slavic. Beyond that the main themes of the Tzimisce have been literally akin to the Wamphyri/Necroscope thematics with their Flesh-Crafting and like. They're meant to be weird and obsessed with biology, crafting flesh and bone.. With V5 just Amalgamming Vicissitude into Protean and it being a splice of Dominate ontop of it... Its completely crap on a crapsicle-stick.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well I know that Dracula and Old Clan Tzimisce are awesome so maybe you should adjust your perceptions.<br /> <br /> The Tzimisce deserve to be more than a rip off of Brian Lumley's work.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-18T14:19:29-08:00","id":1428912,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1428599-v5-vampire-companion?p=1428911#post1428911\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Wrong. They are VERY Tzimisce. I shall in fact assume the status of &quot;Best Tzimisce Fan&quot; and claim you are not a fan because I am gateekeeping. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Well I know that Dracula and Old Clan Tzimisce are awesome so maybe you should adjust your perceptions.<br /> <br /> The Tzimisce deserve to be more than a rip off of Brian Lumley's work.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> The Tzismice deserve MORE than being just centered around Dracula. Dracula should've just been a Gangrel and get it over with. Nothing about the Old Clan was ever interesting compared to the main Tzimisce. They're basic as all fuck. Now I wonder with this dumb edition how they're going to explain the [Tzimisce] antediluvian since he's always more or less had Vicissitude as a Discipline, not some garbage subsidiary of Protean (the Tzimisce literally liken him as a visible manifestation of Vicissitude when it is rumored through Vampiric lore that Enoch spat him out). <br /> <br /> Like jesus christ, I thought V5 had the emphasis of being deleterious to bloodlines and keeping intact with the main ones, but why is the reverse happening to the Tzimisce? Is it because they're trying to remove or press-step out the Sabbat? How can V5 keep being touted as personal &quot;horror&quot; when one of the most fear-inducing Sects (sabbat) and Tzimisce (in lieu of Vicissitude) have been completely gutted? I really wish this Dracula garbage in terms with the Tzimisce never happened, its just trash.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Jade Kingdom Warrior","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","name":"Shakanaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"951"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-18T14:22:44-08:00","id":1428913,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shakanaka</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1428599-v5-vampire-companion?p=1428831#post1428831\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yes, the rules didn't say anything explicitly, so I simply observe from the few instances of precedent to take from (i.e how they were written in the first place). Baba Yaga who's 7000+ years old (much more than Menele and Helena) doesn't have any &quot;natural&quot; Disciplines in 9 at all. Thaumaturgy is a not a &quot;natural&quot; Discipline that is in-built from among the spread of Cainites, nowhere did I say Thaumaturgy was NOT a Discipline. And further, Thaumaturgy is something you have to especially get out on your own to learn.</div> </div> </div> </div>There are outright written rules. Children of the Night has guidelines for creating older vampire NPCs and the generation chart shows you each generation's trait maximum. You know any given vampire's potential as well as how many dots are suggested depending upon age. A 3,600 year old methuselah has, by CotN guidelines, 60 dots in disciplines. A 2,500 year old methuselah has 50 dots. A 1,600 year old methuselah has 40. It's easy to justify with numbers like that one or two nine dot disciplines (well maybe not two at 1600, not enough other stuff). If the intent was that no vampire under 8000 years of age would have nine dot disciplines, you'd think it'd merit at least a passing mention.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shakanaka</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1428599-v5-vampire-companion?p=1428831#post1428831\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The fact Baba Yaga has a 9 in Thaum is easily tied to the fact of her pre-Embrace background (because y'know, she was literally a Shaman). If Baba Yaga hasn't gotten 1 natural Cainite Discipline to 9 and she's 7000+ years old.. It basically blows the notion that &quot;Menele and Helena can have at least one eight dot discipline at 3,000 years you're not looking at waiting another 5,000 for that last dot&quot; (and Baba Yaga isn't getting any of that anytime soon because Final Death).</div> </div> </div> </div>The idea of a distinction between &quot;natural&quot; and &quot;unnatural&quot; vampire disciplines doesn't make sense. Thaumaturgy is, and always has been, presented as a discipline vampires can learn. Also, your argument contradicts itself. If Thaumaturgy is actually harder to learn than other disciplines, then it underlines the fact that 4th generation vampires can learn nine dot disciplines before they're 8.000 years old.<br /> <br /> But that's beside the point, because Michael has nine dots of Presence and was destroyed after 3,353 years as a vampire.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shakanaka</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1428599-v5-vampire-companion?p=1428831#post1428831\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The main meat of what I was speaking about was Elders primarily, extrapolated on what Discipline range they should realistically have from written material; so yes, that's why I'm looking how Elders should contrast from Methuselahs and Antediluvians because there aren't outright written rules. If his ST (since they dictate the story, taking into account what to put in and what not) is bringing in Elders with a 9 Discipline, that's on his ST doing something iffy than any valid argument against 6+ Disciplines. I just find his argument funny because 6+ Disciplines has what he desires of having everything being intact and not slotted out, while still having versatility in the fact powers don't have to be have to be left out for a certain one and 6+ Disciplines having more &quot;omph&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, it's fine to argue what one thinks should make an elder or methuselah. It's just when it slides into &quot;this is the design intent even though it's never explicitly stated as such, and contradicted at least a few times&quot; that it becomes problematic, as you can't divine sweeping design intent from the number of dots on a character sheet. Since VRev clearly states what 10 dot disciplines are (whatever you want whenever you want within the discipline's theme), it seems as if it'd be mentioned if 9 dot disciplines were restricted to antediluvians or 8000+ year old methuselahs. Seems to be a huge omission to never mention it once and slightly hint at it with character sheets under 8 or more different line developers in two separate game lines with seven different editions combined, plus Baba Yaga in a Werewolf book.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shakanaka</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1428599-v5-vampire-companion?p=1428831#post1428831\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ah so its perfectly valid that now STs (or *gasp* PLAYERS xxxxD) don't have no resources at all to work with if they every want an Elder playstyle or emulation. Its perfectly valid that in Tabletop games that is supposed to have infinite avenues on how it can be taken, more advanced Disciplines are completely capped off and locked away for some nonsensical reason and a major part of the VTM setting (Elders) just up and left... Funny.</div> </div> </div> </div>You do have resources for disciplines above 5. It's called Vampire: The Masquerade first, second, revised, and V20 editions + Vampire: The Dark Ages, Dark Ages: Vampire, and Vampire: The Dark Ages 20th Anniversary edition.<br /> <br /> No RPG in the history of the hobby has ever purported to support every playstyle or emulation of anything. RPGs set out to define a particular range of playstyles, and V5 is intended to be lower powered than previous editions. No one has to like it or even play it.<br /> <br /> You may not like the reason something was done, but that doesn't make it nonsense. I loathe the Second Inquisition for a variety of reasons, but that doesn't mean there's no justification for something like that in V5. I just wish it had been different and more plausible. There's nothing wrong with disliking the 5 dot limit. It's just the reach to &quot;therefore no good arguments exist for it&quot; that's questionable. I'm not a fan of the one power per dot you take limit, after all.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shakanaka</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1428599-v5-vampire-companion?p=1428831#post1428831\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">VTR is its own game. Its good, but its not VTM and the lines are different for reason catering for different things. To have VTR shoved in VTM?.... no, just no.</div> </div> </div> </div>VtR wasn't shoved into V5. Yes, they did use a lot of VtR ideas in V5. Some done well, some less well. I think the Disciplines are about 2/3 of the way to being where I'd want them to be if we're limited to five dots. But the rest of that distance would be even more like VtR, so take that as you will.<br /> <br /> This is another one of those instances where it's hard to see how RPGs are written and developed if you're not writing and developing RPGs or haven't in the past. In the case of V5, they decided what they wanted to do with V5, came up with ideas on how to achieve that, and borrowed material from Vampire: The Requiem in the process. The result is, in my opinion, a fairly good RPG in which to play vampires. It's fair to criticize V5 for moving too far from where it started for any given person's taste. It's just not necessarily wrong.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shakanaka</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1428599-v5-vampire-companion?p=1428831#post1428831\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also with V5 Mechanic logic, things that were done before it came out just isn't possible anymore or just as wonky logics to attempt to justify them in (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1417738-how-do-i-explain-sleeping-methuselah-powers-in-v5\">How do I explain sleeping methuselah powers in V5? - Onyx Path Forums (theonyxpath.com)</a>) regards to Elders or other higher level Vampires.. It's pretty on the nose to say it's not game breaking..[/quote[<br /> <br /> EDIT: And actually its bizarre. That example the poster gave was like a reference to Michael.. but what are the odds of that character ever being in a chronicle they'd run at all? lol. Again, aggreaved theoretics.</div> </div> </div> </div>If you play in a Dark Ages Constantinople chronicle, you can very well meet Michael. He's right there and actively doing stuff. And if you could meet Michael you could meet others of similar power level. Personally I tend to prefer 5th gen as the highest PCs are likely to interact with unless the chronicle demands otherwise.<br /> <br /> I'm not sure how V5 could or would address that stuff that used to be possible is no longer. It might just get handwaved away, or they might have a reason, or they might retcon stuff. IDK. It is a big shift with big consequences with the in-game history as it exists now, and it couldn't hurt to resolve the apparent contradiction.<br /> <br /> I don't think something like a form of the withering making them all weaker is wonky logic, especially since the withering itself exists in the Gehenna sourcebook and this is explicitly post/during Gehenna.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-18T14:26:51-08:00","id":1428914,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taggie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1428599-v5-vampire-companion?p=1428895#post1428895\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I thought Justin had stated that Viscittitude was back. Because what ever those...things are they are not Tzimisce, Also, They mention a Tzim having Feral weapons and Viscittitude, that isn't possible, they are both protean 2, so only one can be picked.</div> </div> </div> </div>You can pick lower dot powers when you purchase higher dots. You could take Feral Weapons as Protean 3.<br /> <br /> That's not ideal, but it can be done.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-18T14:31:18-08:00","id":1428915,"title":"","content":"With the changes in V5, Tzimisce are even more Dracula.<br /> <br /> Gangrel do not really fit Dracula, and never really did. They got the wolf, bat, and mist as well as commanding animal stuff, but powers aren't the archetype and the new Tzimisce actually fits Dracula really well both in terms of powers and archetype.<br /> <br /> And honestly I don't think Dracula was shoehorned into Tzimisce, I think the Tzimisce were always intended to be the &quot;Dracula&quot; clan in the same way Toreador are the &quot;Lestat&quot; clan, the Brujah are the &quot;Near Dark&quot; clan, and so on.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-18T14:37:59-08:00","id":1428917,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Resplendent Fire</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1428599-v5-vampire-companion?p=1428915#post1428915\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">With the changes in V5, Tzimisce are even more Dracula.<br /> <br /> Gangrel do not really fit Dracula, and never really did. They got the wolf, bat, and mist as well as commanding animal stuff, but powers aren't the archetype and the new Tzimisce actually fits Dracula really well both in terms of powers and archetype.<br /> <br /> And honestly I don't think Dracula was shoehorned into Tzimisce, I think the Tzimisce were always intended to be the &quot;Dracula&quot; clan in the same way Toreador are the &quot;Lestat&quot; clan, the Brujah are the &quot;Near Dark&quot; clan, and so on.</div> </div> </div> </div>So they were meant to only be Victorian slavic panic racist memes. Great. Here was me thinking lazy racism was being removed this edition, not doubled down on. Fitting Dracula better is like being proud of wod Gypsies.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25011,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","user":"Taggie","date":". 12-18-2020, 05:41 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","name":"Taggie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1047"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-18T14:44:26-08:00","id":1428918,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shakanaka</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1428599-v5-vampire-companion?p=1428912#post1428912\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Tzismice deserve MORE than being just centered around Dracula. Dracula should've just been a Gangrel and get it over with. Nothing about the Old Clan was ever interesting compared to the main Tzimisce. They're basic as all fuck.</div> </div> </div> </div>You know my opinion: The Modern Tzimisce are just a bunch of pathetic edgelords with none of the class, style, or lore of the Old Clan.<br /> <br /> I don't begrudge people who like them but the Old Clan?<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://i.pinimg.com/736x/b2/94/54/b29454a96bbc8d3b336b662a6d00e15b.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-18T14:45:47-08:00","id":1428919,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Resplendent Fire</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">VtR wasn't shoved into V5. Yes, they did use a lot of VtR ideas in V5. Some done well, some less well. I think the Disciplines are about 2/3 of the way to being where I'd want them to be if we're limited to five dots. But the rest of that distance would be even more like VtR, so take that as you will.</div> </div> </div> </div>It very is clear and feels that 5th feels or is basically VtR. Touchstones, adopting the Attribute system from it, depowering everything, less emphasis on interesting grand conspiracy and some metaplot, narrowing the game down to one avenue of play of &quot;&quot;&quot;&quot;street-level&quot;&quot;&quot;&quot; stuff, Blood Potency (seriously, this is the biggest tell many of VtR stuff has been shoved into VTM... Blood Potency with Generation..? WTF!), curbing and absorbing Disciplines into eachother, capping Disciplines to 5 only, etcetera... VTM and VtR are separate gamelines that are supposed to cater to different audiences.<br /> <br /> Imagine in a parallel universe where new Developers came along and started shoving all the stuff from VTM into VtR willy-nilly.. and take out stuff that are intrinsic to what people take like VtR, VtR. Wouldn't be fair and assholey, right? This is exactly is what's happening with VTM and to shrug it off like it ISN'T happening is hilarious.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Jade Kingdom Warrior","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","name":"Shakanaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"951"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-18T14:46:57-08:00","id":1428920,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1428599-v5-vampire-companion?p=1428918#post1428918\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You know my opinion: The Modern Tzimisce are just a bunch of pathetic edgelords with none of the class, style, or lore of the Old Clan.<br /> <br /> I don't begrudge people who like them but the Old Clan?<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://i.pinimg.com/736x/b2/94/54/b29454a96bbc8d3b336b662a6d00e15b.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/></div> </div> </div> </div>Well, congrats, companion just destroyed them. You win, the interesting Tzim are gone. Oh an fthe hunger changes have made the game even less playable, so theirs that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","name":"Taggie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1047"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-18T14:47:19-08:00","id":1428921,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taggie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1428599-v5-vampire-companion?p=1428917#post1428917\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So they were meant to only be Victorian slavic panic racist memes. Great. Here was me thinking lazy racism was being removed this edition, not doubled down on. Fitting Dracula better is like being proud of wod Gypsies.</div> </div> </div> </div>If you know anything about Bram Stoker, in fact Dracula was actually used as a critique of the aristocracy of Britain rather than the aristocracy of Romania. POWERS OF DARKNESS was the original novel by Bram Stoker that was eventually published elsewhere and makes his original idea for the character more clear. His publishers made him remove a large portion of the text that was political in nature and attacked Anti-Semitism, the rising eugenics movement, and colonialism.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/dp/B07MW9H8FP/ref=dp-kindle-redirect?_encoding=UTF8&amp;btkr=1\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.amazon.com/dp/B07MW9H8FP...ng=UTF8&amp;btkr=1</a><br /> <br /> Which fits perfectly with the Tzimisce who are colonialist, racist, eugenicist, and probably not fond of Jews either.<br /> <br /> The Tzimisce should really be the fascist heart of the Sabbat with a handful of the Old Clan resisting in the Anarchs, Independents, Blood Cults, and maybe even the Camarilla.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-18T14:55:34-08:00","id":1428922,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1428599-v5-vampire-companion?p=1428921#post1428921\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If you know anything about Bram Stoker, in fact Dracula was actually used as a critique of the aristocracy of Britain rather than the aristocracy of Romania. POWERS OF DARKNESS was the original novel by Bram Stoker that was eventually published elsewhere and makes his original idea for the character more clear. His publishers made him remove a large portion of the text that was political in nature and attacked Anti-Semitism, the rising eugenics movement, and colonialism.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://&quot;https://www.amazon.com/dp/B07MW9H8FP/ref=dp-kindle-redirect?_encoding=UTF8&amp;btkr=1&quot;\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.amazon.com/dp/B07MW9H8FP...ng=UTF8&amp;btkr=1</a><br /> <br /> Which fits perfectly with the Tzimisce who are colonialist, racist, eugenicist, and probably not fond of Jews either.<br /> <br /> The Tzimisce should really be the fascist heart of the Sabbat with a handful of the Old Clan resisting in the Anarchs, Independents, Blood Cults, and maybe even the Camarilla.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well those edits turned it into one of the slavic panic novels soo..gj I guess? Also Fascism is a human ideology, and should not motivate the Sabbat, they are not human, and should not have human motives, fascism is an anarch and cam thing (mostly cam, certain groups would make great enforcers), as should be communism, anarchism etc. If I can easily map Sabbat schemes onto human movements then it has messed up, they don't have Humanity, they aren't human, and it should take effort to get into that headspace, not reading 8chan and modifying memes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","name":"Taggie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1047"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-18T15:01:36-08:00","id":1428923,"title":"","content":"I liked V5 Vampire Companion overall. I especially liked the portrayals of the Ravnos, Salubri and Tzimisce. I thought it was cool that they made Vicissitude a subset of Protean cause it made the Tzimisce seem somehow more human and less alien in nature. I would like to see a full Sabbat book though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-18T15:01:50-08:00","id":1428924,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taggie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1428599-v5-vampire-companion?p=1428922#post1428922\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well those edits turned it into one of the slavic panic novels soo..gj I guess? Also Fascism is a human ideology, and should not motivate the Sabbat, they are not human, and should not have human motives, fascism is an anarch and cam thing (mostly cam, certain groups would make great enforcers), as should be communism, anarchism etc. If I can easily map Sabbat schemes onto human movements then it has messed up, they don't have Humanity, they aren't human, and it should take effort to get into that headspace, not reading 8chan and modifying memes.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sabbat is everything evil and supervillain-like.<br /> <br /> Which is why they're awesome.<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> (Sabbat is my second favorite sect--I just think the Tzimisce should be in charge and RULE AS FEUDAL GODS!)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-18T15:04:05-08:00","id":1428925,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Matt the Bruins fan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1428599-v5-vampire-companion?p=1428909#post1428909\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If anything, I'd expect the Ravnos who specialized in Fortitude to be disproportionately represented in survivors of the Week of Nightmares. Oh well, overall I like what's been done with the clan.<br /> <br /> I'm not so thrilled by the Salubri, but then again I never have been except for the <i>antitubu</i> in the 3rd Ed. Sabbat book.<br /> <br /> I like the back to basics approach to the Tzimisce, more of traditional folkloric vampires and less of body mod obsession for shock value. Vicissitude has been de-emphasized into a useful tool rather than a raison d'etre. Looks like the Old Clan has been folded back into the main body, with the division between the two being a matter of location and attitude rather than some fundamental difference of the blood. Good.</div> </div> </div> </div>I totally agree with your last paragraph.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-18T15:10:38-08:00","id":1428926,"title":"","content":"Salubri deserved to die. <br /> Tremere did nothing wrong.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-18T15:10:56-08:00","id":1428927,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shakanaka</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1428599-v5-vampire-companion?p=1428919#post1428919\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It very is clear and feels that 5th feels or is basically VtR. Touchstones, adopting the Attribute system from it, depowering everything, less emphasis on interesting grand conspiracy and some metaplot, narrowing the game down to one avenue of play of &quot;&quot;&quot;&quot;street-level&quot;&quot;&quot;&quot; stuff, Blood Potency (seriously, this is the biggest tell many of VtR stuff has been shoved into VTM... Blood Potency with Generation..? WTF!), curbing and absorbing Disciplines into eachother, capping Disciplines to 5 only, etcetera... VTM and VtR are separate gamelines that are supposed to cater to different audiences.<br /> <br /> Imagine in a parallel universe where new Developers came along and started shoving all the stuff from VTM into VtR willy-nilly.. and take out stuff that are intrinsic to what people take like VtR, VtR. Wouldn't be fair and assholey, right? This is exactly is what's happening with VTM and to shrug it off like it ISN'T happening is hilarious.</div> </div> </div> </div>I literally acknowledged that VtR inspired multiple mechanics in V5, but I think ascribing insidious motives to the decision is nonsensical. The thing is that touchstones, blood potency, and the five dot limit all work fine in VtM. I would argue VtM needed such a mechanic from the beginning.<br /> <br /> I don't think generation would fit in VtR at all, as it's built around no known origin point for vampires, whether per clan or as a whole.<br /> <br /> I don't have any issue with adding new discipline powers to existing disciplines to accommodate Chimerstry, Vicissitude, etc.<br /> <br /> I really have no issue with limiting disciplines to five dots.<br /> <br /> I like touchstones, but I'd like them to have more carrot to them than they currently do. Right now they're all stick.<br /> <br /> I don't think &quot;this is supposed to be this way&quot; is necessarily a convincing argument. V5 wasn't even really intended to appeal to long-term VtM fans, it was meant to bring in new fans. Now, whether that was successful or not is another matter and I have no data on it, but I think all the things you listed are actually improvements over older editions of VtM.<br /> <br /> If I were this annoyed about V5 I'd stick to V20... which, actually, I <i>did</i> until I learned that Justin Achilli was running things. Except for a couple discussions about SI and concern about &quot;You are what you eat&quot; coming out badly, which it did not.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-18T15:12:48-08:00","id":1428928,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penelope</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1428599-v5-vampire-companion?p=1428923#post1428923\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I liked V5 Vampire Companion overall. I especially liked the portrayals of the Ravnos, Salubri and Tzimisce. I thought it was cool that they made Vicissitude a subset of Protean cause it made the Tzimisce seem somehow more human and less alien in nature. I would like to see a full Sabbat book though.</div> </div> </div> </div>The 'less alien' is what I dislike about it, the Tzim were the poster monster for the Sabbat and post human horror in the WoD, now they are weird Gangrel.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","name":"Taggie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1047"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-18T15:17:30-08:00","id":1428929,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Resplendent Fire</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1428599-v5-vampire-companion?p=1428927#post1428927\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I literally acknowledged that VtR inspired multiple mechanics in V5, but I think ascribing insidious motives to the decision is nonsensical. The thing is that touchstones, blood potency, and the five dot limit all work fine in VtM. I would argue VtM needed such a mechanic from the beginning.<br /> <br /> I don't think generation would fit in VtR at all, as it's built around no known origin point for vampires, whether per clan or as a whole.<br /> <br /> I don't have any issue with adding new discipline powers to existing disciplines to accommodate Chimerstry, Vicissitude, etc.<br /> <br /> I really have no issue with limiting disciplines to five dots.<br /> <br /> I like touchstones, but I'd like them to have more carrot to them than they currently do. Right now they're all stick.<br /> .</div> </div> </div> </div>Hard disagree on all those points, I like none of them. Which does mean I don't get to play VtM at the moment, because I can't find a V20 or earlier group, and the companion just took away all hope that something of what I loved would make it to this edition , it has all been replaced with VtR ideas, the very idea that meant I never enjoyed that system or setting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","name":"Taggie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1047"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-18T15:17:55-08:00","id":1428931,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penelope</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1428599-v5-vampire-companion?p=1428923#post1428923\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I liked V5 Vampire Companion overall. I especially liked the portrayals of the Ravnos, Salubri and Tzimisce. I thought it was cool that they made Vicissitude a subset of Protean cause it made the Tzimisce seem somehow more human and less alien in nature. I would like to see a full Sabbat book though.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot; I thought it was cool that they made Vicissitude a subset of Protean cause it made the Tzimisce seem somehow more human and less alien in nature.&quot;<br /> <br /> And this is why how the Tzimisce being done in V5 is complete idiot-ball. They're MEANT to be inhuman and the Clan most removed from humanity, alien of them all. Not some low-effort Dracula wringing non-sense and on-the-nose &quot;dragon tropes&quot;. To have Vicissitude side-lined into Protean is foolish. <br /> <br /> It makes me wonder how the Sabbat is going to be handled at all. Bad, probably, with how they've been trying to scrunge it as much as they can so far. If the fan demand for the Sabbat wasn't so high, they'd just kill off the Sabbat outright instead of subtly like they're doing now.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Jade Kingdom Warrior","edited":{"userid":25523,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","user":"Shakanaka","date":". 12-18-2020, 06:58 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","name":"Shakanaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"951"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-18T15:20:10-08:00","id":1428932,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taggie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1428599-v5-vampire-companion?p=1428928#post1428928\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The 'less alien' is what I dislike about it, the Tzim were the poster monster for the Sabbat and post human horror in the WoD, now they are weird Gangrel.</div> </div> </div> </div>I guess I like my Tzimisce less alien and more Dracula. Though I did run a pretty cool Metamorphosist girl named Caprice once. She wore really thick glasses and had cornflower blue eyes and lived in like a weird science/ alchemy lab in the Roman catacombs where she did experiments on the local Kindred (this was in Ancient Rome around the time of Julius Caesar).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-18T15:22:51-08:00","id":1428933,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taggie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1428599-v5-vampire-companion?p=1428929#post1428929\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Hard disagree on all those points, I like none of them. Which does mean I don't get to play VtM at the moment, because I can't find a V20 or earlier group, and the companion just took away all hope that something of what I loved would make it to this edition , it has all been replaced with VtR ideas, the very idea that meant I never enjoyed that system or setting.</div> </div> </div> </div>Join the official WoD discord server. There are two channels for people to post about looking for players and looking for groups. I've seen several people advertise for V20 groups.<br /> <br /> The link is toward the bottom (but not at the bottom) on this webpage. <a href=\"https://www.worldofdarkness.com/community\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.worldofdarkness.com/community</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-18T15:25:28-08:00","id":1428935,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penelope</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1428599-v5-vampire-companion?p=1428932#post1428932\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I guess I like my Tzimisce less alien and more Dracula. Though I did run a pretty cool Metamorphosist girl named Caprice once. She wore really thick glasses and had cornflower blue eyes and lived in like a weird science/alchemy lab in the Roman catacombs where she did experiments on the local Kindred (this was in Ancient Rome around the time of Julius Caesar).</div> </div> </div> </div>As can be seen by my previous comments in this thread, I loathe Dracula, and really like the post humanist, cosmic horror tinged monstrosity that the Tzim ( and in a different way) the Lasombra used to have, both have lost that now, their is no room for those themes in the setting anymore (btw I didn't like Viscititude as a disease), but as this transformative, experimental nightmare? Sign me up, now it is just weird protean, like onbtenebration is a branch of necromancy, and they both lose menace and mystery because of that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","name":"Taggie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1047"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-18T15:26:26-08:00","id":1428936,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Resplendent Fire</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1428599-v5-vampire-companion?p=1428933#post1428933\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Join the official WoD discord server. There are two channels for people to post about looking for players and looking for groups. I've seen several people advertise for V20 groups.<br /> <br /> The link is toward the bottom (but not at the bottom) on this webpage. <a href=\"https://www.worldofdarkness.com/community\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.worldofdarkness.com/community</a></div> </div> </div> </div>I have, wrong TZ.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","name":"Taggie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1047"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-18T15:28:38-08:00","id":1428937,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taggie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1428599-v5-vampire-companion?p=1428935#post1428935\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> As can be seen by my previous comments in this thread, I loathe Dracula, and really like the post humanist, cosmic horror tinged monstrosity that the Tzim ( and in a different way) the Lasombra used to have, both have lost that now, their is no room for those themes in the setting anymore (btw I didn't like Viscititude as a disease), but as this transformative, experimental nightmare? Sign me up, now it is just weird protean, like onbtenebration is a branch of necromancy, and they both lose menace and mystery because of that.</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay. Idk what post humanism is but I don\u2019t think I would like it. But thanks for listening.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-18T15:31:39-08:00","id":1428938,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shakanaka</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1428599-v5-vampire-companion?p=1428931#post1428931\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> &quot; I thought it was cool that they made Vicissitude a subset of Protean cause it made the Tzimisce seem somehow more human and less alien in nature.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Which is silly. There's nothing about Vicissitude which is alien or weird. It's BODY SCULPTING. Its like saying the Progenitors are somehow the most alien and weird Technocracy clan.<br /> <br /> Pretending that trans people or tattoos are somehow weird.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And this is why hiw the Tzimisce being done in V5 is complete idiot-ball. They're MEANT to be inhuman and the Clan most removed from humanity, alien of them all. Not some low-effort Dracula wringing non-sense and on-the-nose &quot;dragon tropes&quot;. To have Vicissitude side-lined into Protean is foolish. </div> </div> </div>Except they're not alien. They never have been alien. They're sadistic serial killers and Buffalo Bill types. There's nothing alien about them and pretending so has always been lame. It also acts like other vampires are MORE human.<br /> <br /> Which is silly.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It makes me wonder how the Sabbat is going to be handled at all. Bad, probably, with how they've been trying to scrunge it as much as they can so far. If the fan demand for the Sabbat wasn't so high, they'd just kill off the Sabbat outright instead of subtly like they're doing now. </div> </div> </div>I feel the Tzimisce are their cruel, evil, and very monstrous [but no less human] selves in this.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-18T15:33:23-08:00","id":1428939,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Resplendent Fire</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think &quot;this is supposed to be this way&quot; is necessarily a convincing argument. V5 wasn't even really intended to appeal to long-term VtM fans, it was meant to bring in new fans. Now, whether that was successful or not is another matter.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's not about &quot;old&quot; or &quot;new&quot; fans. I only got into the tabletop aspect of VTM in 2018. I'm not a &quot;old head&quot;. These design choices are appealing to people who like aspects of VtR, not VTM. It's not fair for VTM to have VtR shoved into our line. VTM is supposed to have its own themes and mechanics, while VtR having different stuff. It's not fair to have this tack-on to be happening.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Jade Kingdom Warrior","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","name":"Shakanaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"951"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-18T15:34:26-08:00","id":1428940,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taggie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1428599-v5-vampire-companion?p=1428936#post1428936\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I have, wrong TZ.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't know how many time zones are represented, but the channels do get a lot of traffic. Some seem to be for RP servers, akin to MUSHes maybe? I don't know. Anyway, I hope you can find a V20 group.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-18T15:35:48-08:00","id":1428942,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shakanaka</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1428599-v5-vampire-companion?p=1428939#post1428939\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's not about &quot;old&quot; or &quot;new&quot; fans. I only got into the tabletop aspect of VTM in 2018. I'm not a &quot;old head&quot;. These design choices are appealing to people who like aspects of VtR, not VTM. It's not fair for VTM to have VtR shoved into our line. VTM is supposed to have its own themes and mechanics, while VtR having different stuff. It's not fair to have this tack-on to be happening.</div> </div> </div> </div>Re-Damn Diculous.<br /> <br /> Name the fans you know personally who are V:TR fans who are appealed to by these V5 changes. I've been playing since 1995 and I NEVER liked V:TR.<br /> <br /> It's not my bag.<br /> <br /> I like V5 because it's a return to classic Vampire: The Masquerade, 1st and 2nd Edition. A move away from the big globe trotting sect wars to the personal intimate city-based stories like Chicago and Milwaukee by Night.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-18T15:36:03-08:00","id":1428943,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penelope</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1428599-v5-vampire-companion?p=1428937#post1428937\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Okay. Idk what post humanism is but I don\u2019t think I would like it. But thanks for listening.</div> </div> </div> </div>Post humanist thought is a big subject, and a real thing, but as it applies to horror, it is casting aside humanity, as a larval stage of something greater (this is a big simplification, but hey) in the case of the Tzim, that greater is in Viscititude, animalism and auspex (and for some in Koldun), this super predator with utter mastery over flesh, with senses to see the world as it truly is, and the animals bending to dominion, I could have a lot of fun with that basis, and it's now gone, entirely. A good portion of the fun was actually from not having Dominate, as it happens.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","name":"Taggie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1047"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-18T15:38:37-08:00","id":1428944,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1428599-v5-vampire-companion?p=1428942#post1428942\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Re-Damn Diculous.<br /> <br /> Name the fans you know personally who are V:TR fans who are appealed to by these V5 changes. I've been playing since 1995 and I NEVER liked V:TR.<br /> <br /> It's not my bag.<br /> <br /> I like V5 because it's a return to classic Vampire: The Masquerade, 1st and 2nd Edition. A move away from the big globe trotting sect wars to the personal intimate city-based stories like Chicago and Milwaukee by Night.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't know what of second ed you see in the mechanics of v5, but what ever it is has sailed by me, and without those mechanics, the story can't be told, it isn't supported. The systems coming over from VtR, and the hunger mechanics both fundamentally change the universe the game is in, in a way that feels and plays nothing like previous editions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","name":"Taggie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1047"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-18T15:41:50-08:00","id":1428945,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shakanaka</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1428599-v5-vampire-companion?p=1428939#post1428939\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's not about &quot;old&quot; or &quot;new&quot; fans. I only got into the tabletop aspect of VTM in 2018. I'm not a &quot;old head&quot;. These design choices are appealing to people who like aspects of VtR, not VTM. It's not fair for VTM to have VtR shoved into our line. VTM is supposed to have its own themes and mechanics, while VtR having different stuff. It's not fair to have this tack-on to be happening.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think it is about old and new fans, mostly. Obviously not everyone will neatly fit into those categories, and I've been a fan since 1991 and I like a lot of the new stuff. But the intent (and it's arguable whether or not it succeeded, I grant that) was to present a modern RPG with the WoD setting.<br /> <br /> I again do not think it's fair to categorize it as &quot;shoved into&quot; anything. That implies a degree of carelessness and ensuing damage that just isn't present. Even I don't think the SI were included quite so thoughtlessly, no matter how I feel about how they're implemented. I just don't see them as tacked on.<br /> <br /> I'm also not sure &quot;it's not fair&quot; is a convincing argument against new rules.<br /> <br /> I also don't think VtM was specifically intended to be marketed to VtR fans.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2367,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","user":"Resplendent Fire","date":". 12-18-2020, 06:46 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-18T15:44:58-08:00","id":1428946,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1428599-v5-vampire-companion?p=1428942#post1428942\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Re-Damn Diculous.<br /> <br /> Name the fans you know personally who are V:TR fans who are appealed to by these V5 changes. I've been playing since 1995 and I NEVER liked V:TR.<br /> <br /> It's not my bag.<br /> <br /> I like V5 because it's a return to classic Vampire: The Masquerade, 1st and 2nd Edition. A move away from the big globe trotting sect wars to the personal intimate city-based stories like Chicago and Milwaukee by Night.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's me. I'm the VtR fan, but I like this stuff in V5 for reasons other than &quot;Cool, V5 is more like VtR now.&quot; I always wanted VtM to have something like blood potency, I feel like discipline proliferation became a problem over time, and I like that vampires have to maintain connections to mortals, even really old ones.<br /> <br /> I also like taking things back down to the local level emphasis that VtM had in its first edition.<br /> <br /> I like hunger although I would like it to be a bit different and less punishing at high blood potencies. I think it's more thematic than blood pools, and requires so much less bookkeeping.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-18T15:51:22-08:00","id":1428947,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Resplendent Fire</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1428599-v5-vampire-companion?p=1428946#post1428946\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's me. I'm the VtR fan, but I like this stuff in V5 for reasons other than &amp;quot;Cool, V5 is more like VtR now.&amp;quot; I always wanted VtM to have something like blood potency, I feel like discipline proliferation became a problem over time, and I like that vampires have to maintain connections to mortals, even really old ones.<br /> <br /> I also like taking things back down to the local level emphasis that VtM had in its first edition.<br /> <br /> I like hunger although I would like it to be a bit different and less punishing at high blood potencies. I think it's more thematic than blood pools, and requires so much less bookkeeping.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, so you're literally a VtR fan and you're happy that VTM now has VtR mechanics and themes boom-shoed into it... Proving what I was claiming in the first place. Then you bullshit and gaslight me saying that the new developers forcing VtR paradigm into VTM isn't a problem or no one who liked pre-V5 shouldn't be outraged.. <br /> <br /> *claps*<br /> <br /> Tell me, if new developers came to VtR, put in all the stuff you hate from VTM into it... Tell me, would you still like it and not hate it?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Jade Kingdom Warrior","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","name":"Shakanaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"951"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-18T16:17:09-08:00","id":1428949,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shakanaka</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1428599-v5-vampire-companion?p=1428947#post1428947\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Ah, so you're literally a VtR fan and you're happy that VTM now has VtR mechanics and themes boom-shoed into it... Proving what I was claiming in the first place. Then you bullshit and gaslight me saying that the new developers forcing VtR paradigm into VTM isn't a problem or no one who liked pre-V5 shouldn't be outraged..<br /> <br /> *claps*<br /> <br /> Tell me, if new developers came to VtR, put in all the stuff you hate from VTM into it... Tell me, would you still like it and not hate it?</div> </div> </div> </div>If my VtM hobby were a person, it'd be a millennial by now. I wanted something like blood potency in 1991, and tried to write some house rules for it (that I ended up never using). I'm not someone who got into VtR in the past decade and craved VtM being more like it because I can just play VtR. And vice versa.<br /> <br /> <i>However,</i> I think you're so focused on the appearance of similarities to VtR that you're ignoring the substance and as with other topics we've both discussed, you've leavened your criticism with personal attacks on the developers, accusing them of &quot;forcing the mechanics&quot; and ruining the game.<br /> <br /> I don't think anybody should be outraged over mechanical changes in RPGs. I don't think everyone should like those changes, however, and I have said so.<br /> <br /> When I say that I don't think it's a problem, it's my honest opinion. It's not bullshit and it's definitely not gaslighting. Asking you to make a distinction between &quot;I don't like these mechanics&quot; and &quot;The developers who wrote these mechanics did so out of spite for my favorite game&quot; is not gaslighting.<br /> <br /> If you don't like V5, just play older editions. It's really that simply. No one's forcing anyone to have to discuss how much they hate this game they're not going to play. It strikes me as a huge waste of time to spend this much effort on something you don't like.<br /> <br /> Also, ad hominem is a fallacy for a reason. You've just built this huge mischaracterization of my arguments on the admission that I like VtR. Everything you've said in your post about me there is something you made up so you can be angry. So you can be &quot;outraged&quot; over a goddamned elfgame. What you've not done is actually responded to the substance of my arguments, which is that the game is fine, no one is required to like it, and there are viable alternatives that people still play.<br /> <br /> A lot of RPG fans actually play and like multiple RPGs, and don't just devote themselves to a single line or publisher. I also like D&amp;D, Champions, GURPS, Fate, PbtA, M&amp;M, Shadowrun, Cyberpunk 2020, Amber Diceless, Lords of Gossamer and Shadow, Nobilis, and Feng Shui in case you want to psychoanalyze me based on the fact that I play more than two RPGs from more than one publisher.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2367,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","user":"Resplendent Fire","date":". 12-18-2020, 07:21 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-18T16:21:11-08:00","id":1428951,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1428599-v5-vampire-companion?p=1428942#post1428942\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Re-Damn Diculous.<br /> <br /> Name the fans you know personally who are V:TR fans who are appealed to by these V5 changes. I've been playing since 1995 and I NEVER liked V:TR.<br /> <br /> It's not my bag.<br /> <br /> I like V5 because it's a return to classic Vampire: The Masquerade, 1st and 2nd Edition. A move away from the big globe trotting sect wars to the personal intimate city-based stories like Chicago and Milwaukee by Night.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> I guess this is also me. I switched over to VTR and never looked back until V5 came out. I still have an internal battle in my mind over which system I prefer. However I really enjoy the hunger die mechanic and I'm a sucker for metaplot. I strongly dislike the globe trotting and world spanning conspiracies and I am not a huge crossover fan. I would prefer better elder rules though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3901-radiofreedeath","name":"RadioFreeDeath","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-18T16:45:50-08:00","id":1428952,"title":"","content":"To say the similarities of VtR and V5 is merely &quot;appearance&quot; is laughable. The way VTM is being directed is to deliberately make it more like VtR. If they're AREN'T forcing mechanics from VtR into VTM to be more like it, why are they doing that EXACT thing for? Why couldn't they just leave the pre-V5 mechanics and just touch-up and update things? Because this update isn't a new &quot;edition&quot;, it's a complete reboot and basically VtR 3rd Edition. <br /> <br /> To also just shrug off and say, &quot;play and older version&quot; is also ridiculous because now VTM is unrecognizable and the versions that are palpable to play will no longer get developer support of new things. If my main gaming hobby is WoD or general stuff is oWoD... And then I see things from nWoD overtaking it and will soon be the main cusp of my hobby and no longer aspects of oWoD... Why the fuck WOULDN'T I be not discussing why it's wrong? You're argument makes no freaking sense. <br /> <br /> Let's go to VtR. Let's put Generations into that game. Let's just take the basic 5 clans it has and let's make 13 new main ones. Let's retcon VtR having loose &quot;lore and setting&quot; and let's scale it up to be more grand-conspiracy. Let's remove Touchstones because they flat don't make any sense and let's put in Humanity along with Paths. Let's remove Covenants for warring Sects. Let's give the Clans more lore instead of loose origins.. Oh and let's put Appearance, Charisma, Wits, and Perception as Attributes for VtR too aswell. <br /> <br /> Now let's slap it to the VtR audience and say it's VtR still.... Yeah, bullshit for that group, right?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Resplendent Fire</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I feel like discipline proliferation became a problem over time</div> </div> </div> </div>WTF, are you kidding me? Have you even seen all the Disciplines VtR even HAS between the numerous Bloodlines in that game? But you say you dislike the &quot;Discipline&quot; proliferation in pre-V5 VTM? What does this exactly mean?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Jade Kingdom Warrior","edited":{"userid":25523,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","user":"Shakanaka","date":". 12-18-2020, 08:05 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","name":"Shakanaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"951"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-18T16:51:12-08:00","id":1428953,"title":"","content":"I'm not going to argue with someone who turns &quot;which RPGs someone likes&quot; into an us vs them situation","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-18T16:58:46-08:00","id":1428955,"title":"","content":"So you won't answer my clear question on whether or not VtR audiences would like their game being flipped over to aspects they don't like from VTM.. but expect I'm supposed to heed your claim that what is going on in V5 isn't particularly &quot;wrong&quot; and not understanding that fans of pre-V5 have different things they don't like from VtR not be in VTM..? Very quaint of you and basically confirms what I've been saying previously.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Jade Kingdom Warrior","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","name":"Shakanaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"951"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-18T17:01:11-08:00","