\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-18T17:05:20-08:00","id":1428958,"title":"","content":"I forgot to address one thing:<br /> <br /> If WW or Onyx Path decided to put what I hate about VtM into VtR I'd probably just ignore it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-18T17:08:37-08:00","id":1428959,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shakanaka</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1428599-v5-vampire-companion?p=1428955#post1428955\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So you won't answer my clear question on whether or not VtR audiences would like their game being flipped over to aspects they don't like from VTM.. but expect I'm supposed to heed your claim that what is going on in V5 isn't particularly &quot;wrong&quot; and not understanding that fans of pre-V5 have different things they don't like from VtR not be in VTM..? Very quaint of you and basically confirms what I've been saying previously.</div> </div> </div> </div>I said what I said:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Resplendent Fire</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1428599-v5-vampire-companion?p=1428953#post1428953\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not going to argue with someone who turns &quot;which RPGs someone likes&quot; into an us vs them situation</div> </div> </div> </div>But just so you know:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Resplendent Fire</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1428599-v5-vampire-companion?p=1428958#post1428958\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I forgot to address one thing:<br /> <br /> If WW or Onyx Path decided to put what I hate about VtM into VtR I'd probably just ignore it.</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-18T17:09:17-08:00","id":1428960,"title":"","content":"Yes and all they would put into VtR that would make it unrecognizable would be how the gameline for all new supplements and further development would be entirely for the rest of the gameline.... How very ignorable are you talking about here? Because that's really nonsensical. Basically everything you've said toward supporting VtR stuff in VTM, but not vice versa in a scenario into VtR if the shoe was on the other foot pings why your arguments are disingenuous and why you won't answer whether or not a VtR audience would like such changes. It's trite.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Jade Kingdom Warrior","edited":{"userid":25523,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","user":"Shakanaka","date":". 12-18-2020, 08:55 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","name":"Shakanaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"951"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-18T17:25:54-08:00","id":1428962,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taggie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1428599-v5-vampire-companion?p=1428943#post1428943\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Post humanist thought is a big subject, and a real thing, but as it applies to horror, it is casting aside humanity, as a larval stage of something greater (this is a big simplification, but hey) in the case of the Tzim, that greater is in Viscititude, animalism and auspex (and for some in Koldun), this super predator with utter mastery over flesh, with senses to see the world as it truly is, and the animals bending to dominion, I could have a lot of fun with that basis, and it's now gone, entirely. A good portion of the fun was actually from not having Dominate, as it happens.</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay. I definitely don\u2019t think this is my thing, especially since I like them having Dominate. But thanks for telling me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-18T17:33:05-08:00","id":1428963,"title":"","content":"I like humanizing the Tzimisce. I also like them having a transhumanist contingent, and with their own somewhat alien take on posthumanism. I'm fine with the entire clan not being alien, and many of them still being somewhat human. Body modification is a very human thing to do, whether out of need or desire.<br /> <br /> I also don't really read all that much into clan disciplines. Mostly it's just &quot;yeah, that supports the clan theme&quot; and I think in this case it supports the clan theme.<br /> <br /> Or perhaps I should say this is my favorite take on the Tzimisce since they were first introduced in the Player's Guide to the Sabbat in 1992.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-18T18:32:12-08:00","id":1428966,"title":"","content":"Here's the thing about the Tzimisce, they were &quot;Inhuman&quot; as a way of making them scarier than regular vampires because they were part of the designated Bad GuysTM.<br /> <br /> 5th Edition has made it clear all vampires are assholes and monsters.<br /> <br /> So, it becomes less of a really valid take on the subject. Besides, if you don't buy that &quot;murderous mad scientists and serial killers&quot; are inhuman since, well, those things exist among humans then it kind of undermines the point.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-18T18:44:59-08:00","id":1428967,"title":"","content":"Yeah, I much prefer this broader flesh catherdral now, and I love that a nickname is &quot;Dragons.&quot;<br /> I never really wanted to play Tzimisce before but I'd play one of the V5 Tzimisce.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-18T19:30:48-08:00","id":1428970,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1428599-v5-vampire-companion?p=1428966#post1428966\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Here's the thing about the Tzimisce, they were &quot;Inhuman&quot; as a way of making them scarier than regular vampires because they were part of the designated Bad GuysTM.<br /> <br /> 5th Edition has made it clear all vampires are assholes and monsters.<br /> <br /> So, it becomes less of a really valid take on the subject. Besides, if you don't buy that &quot;murderous mad scientists and serial killers&quot; are inhuman since, well, those things exist among humans then it kind of undermines the point.</div> </div> </div> </div>With everyone being on humanity, and the touchstone system and by the looks no replacement path system in sight, they have done the opposite of making it clear all vampires are monsters, the mechanics, again, do not support monsters at all, assholes yea, but not monsters. This is the most friendly neighborhood blood sucker the system has been, maybe ever, I half.expect Angelus and Spike to turn up at any second....","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25011,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","user":"Taggie","date":". 12-18-2020, 10:41 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","name":"Taggie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1047"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-18T19:42:21-08:00","id":1428972,"title":"","content":"&quot;I'm Peter Varper, just your friendly neighborhood Vampire!!!&quot;<br /> <br /> or better yet<br /> <br /> &quot;I'm totally madly in love with this human girl and that'll drive the whole plot all successive movies (Touchstones = Twilight). Also I'm totally a &quot;Vampire&quot; except I can go in the sun and only sparkle and I'm completely an angsty teen!!&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Jade Kingdom Warrior","edited":{"userid":25523,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","user":"Shakanaka","date":". 12-18-2020, 10:53 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","name":"Shakanaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"951"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-18T20:30:08-08:00","id":1428975,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1428599-v5-vampire-companion?p=1428926#post1428926\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Salubri deserved to die. <br /> Tremere did nothing wrong.</div> </div> </div> </div>If they didn't want to get eaten then maybe they shouldn't taste so delicious","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3953-dwight","name":"Dwight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3953_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-18T20:44:23-08:00","id":1428976,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taggie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1428599-v5-vampire-companion?p=1428970#post1428970\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> With everyone being on humanity, and the touchstone system and by the looks no replacement path system in sight, they have done the opposite of making it clear all vampires are monsters, the mechanics, again, do not support monsters at all, assholes yea, but not monsters. This is the most friendly neighborhood blood sucker the system has been, maybe ever, I half.expect Angelus and Spike to turn up at any second....</div> </div> </div> </div>Do you intend to say that being on humanity means not being a monster? Because from first edition onward that was always the point - that being a vampire pushes you to do monstrous things. &quot;A beast I am, lest a beast I become.&quot; V5 continues that, although humanity is quite different. Having a touchstone doesn't mean you can't do monstrous things.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-18T20:54:53-08:00","id":1428978,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Resplendent Fire</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1428599-v5-vampire-companion?p=1428976#post1428976\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Do you intend to say that being on humanity means not being a monster? Because from first edition onward that was always the point - that being a vampire pushes you to do monstrous things. &quot;A beast I am, lest a beast I become.&quot; V5 continues that, although humanity is quite different. Having a touchstone doesn't mean you can't do monstrous things.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> He's talking about in relation to the Tzimisce. The whole point of them and their sect was completely absconding Humanity and dispelling the notion of pretending to be Human or holding its facets. The Tzimisce were versed in a completely different verse of thought and way of dealing with their eternal unlife. They were monsters and they recognized that instead of chaining it from the surface. Now with V5 that's undoable or unrepresentable without Paths, which is the complaint.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Jade Kingdom Warrior","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","name":"Shakanaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"951"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-18T21:38:01-08:00","id":1428984,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Resplendent Fire</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1428599-v5-vampire-companion?p=1428976#post1428976\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Do you intend to say that being on humanity means not being a monster? Because from first edition onward that was always the point - that being a vampire pushes you to do monstrous things. &amp;quot;A beast I am, lest a beast I become.&amp;quot; V5 continues that, although humanity is quite different. Having a touchstone doesn't mean you can't do monstrous things.</div> </div> </div> </div>See the Paths as to their position on Touchstone (hint: interaction with humans beyond lunch or toy can cause degeneration on some of.them. Certainly having one be a touchstone would cause wassail","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","name":"Taggie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1047"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-18T22:49:38-08:00","id":1428987,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taggie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1428599-v5-vampire-companion?p=1428984#post1428984\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> See the Paths as to their position on Touchstone (hint: interaction with humans beyond lunch or toy can cause degeneration on some of.them. Certainly having one be a touchstone would cause wassail</div> </div> </div> </div>That doesn't answer my question.<br /> <br /> I remember when the Path of Harmonious Accord was a thing, I know what they do and what they're for. I'm asking what it is about humanity that prevents vampires from being monstrous, or how having a touchstone prevents it.<br /> <br /> We do not know what we're going to get with the Sabbat so it seems premature to imagine elaborate scenarios about how bad it'll be.<br /> <br /> Also, I may be missing something in V5, but heirarchy of sins seems to be out the door entirely. Instead you have convictions and chronicle tenets (pg 172) which do not work like a hierarchy of sins. I have no reason to assume such hierarchies will be needed for the Sabbat, either.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2367,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","user":"Resplendent Fire","date":". 12-19-2020, 02:07 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-18T23:14:44-08:00","id":1428990,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Resplendent Fire</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1428599-v5-vampire-companion?p=1428987#post1428987\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That doesn't answer my question.<br /> <br /> I remember when the Path of Harmonious Accord was a thing, I know what they do and what they're for. I'm asking what it is about humanity that prevents vampires from being monstrous, or how having a touchstone prevents it.<br /> <br /> We do not know what we're going to get with the Sabbat so it seems premature to imagine elaborate scenarios about how bad it'll be.<br /> <br /> Also, I may be missing something in V5, but heirarchy of sins seems to be out the door entirely. Instead you have convictions and chronicle tenets (pg 172) which do not work like a hierarchy of sins. I have no reason to assume such hierarchies will be needed for the Sabbat, either.</div> </div> </div> </div>On humanity you can be cruel, sadistic etc etc, do heinous things, but you are on Humanity, you aren't a monster, you are a human. Maybe an evil one, but still at core, a human.<br /> <br /> Having playtested, Paths do not work with tenets and convictions, this argument has been done to death, but that system does not work to translate the played experience of Paths, especially it does not work if pack members are on different paths, as what should stain Honourable Accord, should not stain Caine, or Inner Voice, but tenets are one size fits all..which breaks things.<br /> <br /> Basically the Paths need the Hierarchies or they aren't Paths and aren't interesting, like an F1 car needs an engine, I mean sure, technically you could race pedal cars and call it F1, but it isn't the same.<br /> <br /> As an aside humanity score does things Sabbat don't want anyway, appearing human having sex etc","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25011,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","user":"Taggie","date":". 12-19-2020, 02:23 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","name":"Taggie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1047"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-18T23:24:09-08:00","id":1428992,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taggie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1428599-v5-vampire-companion?p=1428990#post1428990\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> On humanity you can be cruel, sadistic etc etc, do heinous things, but you are on Humanity, you aren't a monster, you are a human. Maybe an evil one, but still at core, a human.</div> </div> </div> </div>A human who burns in the sun, drinks blood to survive, can be routed with true faith, and has supernatural predator powers like mind control and superhuman strength? Not a human. Humanity doesn't reflect <i>being a human</i> in Vampire, it reflects the conflict between vampiric urges and human morals and ethics. But the character is most definitely <i>not</i> a human.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taggie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1428599-v5-vampire-companion?p=1428990#post1428990\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Having playtested, Paths do not work with tenets and convictions, this argument has been done to death, but that system does not work to translate the played experience of Paths, especially it does not work if pack members are on different paths, as what should stain Honourable Accord, should not stain Caine, or Inner Voice, but tenets are one size fits all..which breaks things.<br /> <br /> <br /> Basically the Paths need the Hierarchies or they aren't Paths and aren't interesting, like an F1 car needs an engine, I mean sure, technically you could race pedal cars and call it F1, but it isn't the same.</div> </div> </div> </div>So you don't know what might be in the works either, huh? Cool. Justin's worked on a few Vampire books here and there, one having Sabbat in the title. I think he can come up with something or hire someone else who can come up with something that maybe hasn't been thought of yet.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2367,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","user":"Resplendent Fire","date":". 12-19-2020, 02:59 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-18T23:42:32-08:00","id":1428998,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Resplendent Fire</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1428599-v5-vampire-companion?p=1428992#post1428992\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> A human who burns in the sun, drinks blood to survive, can be routed with true faith, and has supernatural predator powers like mind control and superhuman strength? Not a human. Humanity doesn't reflect <i>being a human</i> in Vampire, it reflects the conflict between vampiric urges and human morals and ethics. But the character is most definitely <i>not</i> a human.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> So you don't know what might be in the works either, huh? Cool. Justin's worked on a few Vampire books here and there, one having Sabbat in the title. I think he can come up with something or hire someone else who can that maybe hasn't been thought of yet.</div> </div> </div> </div>You said it your self HUMAN morals and ethics. Literally that, and having a high score in it gives you human urges, and human appearance.....makes the human more important and obvious, and keeping that score is tied to human morality pets. Fine for Anne Rice's Vampire Chronicles, not great for 30 Days of Night, Sub Species, The Strain etc (also The Thing makes a great Tzim Methuselah, while The Flesh That Hates and Sarkism in general are near perfect Metamorphosis inspiration)<br /> <br /> No I don't know what is coming, my point was what we have now doesn't work, as a counter to your statement about it not being necessary, and what we have seen of Tzimisce in companion is not encouraging at all, as what I liked about them has been retconned, or downplayed. Also given that the Revised Sabbat is my least liked version (2e doom cultist for unlife!) His name brings mixed feelings, yes he is a change, but it doesn't bring confidence that he likes the aspects of the setting I do.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25011,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","user":"Taggie","date":". 12-19-2020, 03:11 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","name":"Taggie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1047"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-19T01:14:17-08:00","id":1429000,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taggie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1428599-v5-vampire-companion?p=1428998#post1428998\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Fine for Anne Rice's Vampire Chronicles, not great for 30 Days of Night, Sub Species, The Strain etc (also The Thing makes a great Tzim Methuselah, while The Flesh That Hates and Sarkism in general are near perfect Metamorphosis inspiration)</div> </div> </div> </div>I hear you.<br /> \u200b<br /> I've said before that I don't like metaplot as the reason for publishing sourcebooks because it forces people to play in one particular chronicle style. I prefer an approach where sourcebooks are toolkits that allow people to play the game they wanted. I think one of the beauties of the original V1/V2 sourcebooks is that they did that. The concepts of the Camarilla and Sabbat (and other concepts) allowed people to roleplay a wide variety of vampire types.<br /> <br /> Whatever its merits, it seems V5 does not. And its a weakness.<br /> <br /> And I say this as someone who has never liked Necroscope style Vampires and eliminate Vicissitude entirely in the chronicles I ST around 20 years ago, and thus changed the Tzimisce into something I suspect is very much like V5's version. But that doesn't mean I don't understand that others do like the Discipline and the Clan's portrayal for decades, and they don't like how the game no longer supports that.<br /> <br /> The game's setting is breaking as a result of these metaplots. Each time they introduce retroactive continuity, and there are just too many retroactive continuity changes required to make it work. The setting is increasingly being damaged. It would not surprise me in some future V6 or V7 that the next group of developers decide the original seven clans of the Camarilla should rejoin, the Tzimisce (and other clans) be restored to what they were, and a \u201cback to the basics\u201d attempt is made to restore the setting; or that the merry-go-round approach to sects continues and we get yet another selection of clans of the Camarilla or even more bizarre changes.<br /> <br /> I think a better approach is to define the &quot;core&quot; elements of the Vampire setting, and realize there are now (at least) 3 different versions of it. Those different versions are simply examples of what one can do with the core setting, but shouldn't define them. Players, of course, have had even more variations in their home chronicles. In my opinion, it would be better of the game company to divide their published material into a core book dealing with mechanics and the core setting, and then a variety of approved &quot;metaplot/edition/variations&quot; sourcebooks that explore the different ways to approach it. Each of those visions can still be supported - especially now in a world with PDFs and print on demand versions don't require game stores to physically stock everything.<br /> <br /> Canon Elements of Vampire: the Masquerade (that is present in all incarnations; this is what V20 attempted to provide at least in its corebook)<ul><li>13 clans divided into the Camarilla, Sabbat, and Independents with individuals also belonging to Anarchs and other minor sects</li> <li>Camarilla as the dominant faction</li> <li>Jyhad / Manipulation by Methusalehs</li> <li>\u200bAntedeluvians are a mystery</li> </ul>Elements of the first era of Metaplot (Greenberg \u2013 V1/V2)<ul><li>Multi-layered Jyhad \u2013 Anarchs vs Prince, Prince vs Primogen, Prince vs Camarilla, some Anarchs against the Camarilla as an institution, Camarilla vs Sabbat, True Hand versus False Hand, Gehenna Cults; elder Vampires remaining in contact with past friends in rival sects</li> <li>Lots of unknown secrets \u2013 True Brujah, fate of the Cappadocians, nature of the Salubri</li> <li>Vicissitude as an Umbral Disease</li> <li>Lots of Bloodlines with mysterious origins</li> <li>Sympathetic vampires struggling with their condition a common element (perhaps too much)</li> <li>Encouragement of crossover with the rest of the WoD</li> <li>Often prone to gonzo elements at the highest level</li> </ul>Elements of the second era of Metaplot (Achilli - Rev)<ul><li>Sect politics most important element</li> <li>Sect conflicts along the lines of a military campaign</li> <li>Gehenna imminent so there are major changes to the setting to reflect that countdown</li> <li>Golconda is a lie or at least a disappointing reality</li> <li>Stronger emphasis that deviating from Humanity feeds the beast combined with belief vampires can't really follow Humanity to any large degree over time</li> <li>The events that happen in the metaplot essentially destroys the Masquerade, but the setting refuses to admit it</li> <li>Vicissitude now just an ordinary Discipline</li> <li>Clans have many sub-clans with separate mechanics</li> <li>Elimination of the elements of previous metaplots that conflict with the new style</li> <li>No crossover with the rest of the WoD</li> </ul>Elements of the third era of Metaplot (V5) / I admit this is my impression from hearsay as I've never read any V5 material<ul><li>Worldwide Wrestling/Soap Opera script-based approach to vampire politics - Clans change sect; clans split up; bloodlines join up to become one clan</li> <li>Very event driven in the sense that changes to the core setting are done just previous to Players playing in the game; these aren't events players participate in</li> <li>More humane vampires an option again, but generally most vampires depicted as evil</li> <li>Streamlining of mechanics while allowing more options, and these mechanical changes impact the setting accordingly</li> <li>Nostalgia for certain characters and ideas found in earlier editions that show again in more profound ways</li> <li>Elimination of the elements of previous metaplots that conflict with the new style</li> </ul>I'm sure others would articulate a different set of bullet points, but I think there is general agreement that these are very different styles of play, and that each subsequent version applied retroactive continuity changes to eliminate certain things in the previous edition and to set up unique things in their version.<br /> <br /> These are really three separate incarnations of the game's core setting. They're not really continuations of the prior version even though they make reference to many of the same characters and concepts. It's like the old Earth-1, Earth-2, Earth-3 and so on of DC's Pre-Crisis superhero comics. Each one has its own version of &quot;Superman&quot; (or whatever character) with its own lore and continuity, but they are not the same character.<br /> <br /> While I have my preferences, I have to admit that I'd probably have fun playing in any of these kind of chronicles once. But I find it distasteful that I'm told this is the way the setting will be going forward permanently (until, of course, another version comes around that invalidates this version).<br /> <br /> Of course, my own version played at my tables has elements from all of these as well as many things uniquely derived just from me. And the same goes for many other home chronicles of other players. They're compatible with the &quot;core&quot; setting - just not these metaplot separate interpretations.<br /> <br /> What I am looking for our tools that allow me to run the kind of vampire chronicle I want, as well as the occasional look at how others run their games so I can be inspired and steal new ideas. I don't want to be told to radically change my chronicle in order to accommodate the new metaplot setting - no matter how cool or interesting I may find it as a whole or as parts. I don't like the idea that new material seems to invalidate my own ideas.<br /> <br /> Game companies love metaplot because it's an easy way to get the fanbase to buy new sourcebooks that provides the revenue treadmill. However, I think that's an illusion. Because what ultimately happens is that fans of the game's previous incarnations simply stop supporting the game line at all and retreat back to their already purchased books. So after the initial rush of sold material, the company now has a much smaller fanbase buying materials than it did before.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3046,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","user":"Black Fox","date":". 12-21-2020, 03:18 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-19T02:12:17-08:00","id":1429001,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1428599-v5-vampire-companion?p=1429000#post1429000\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I hear you.<br /> \u200b<br /> I've said before that I don't like metaplot as the reason for publishing sourcebooks because it forces people to play in one particular chronicle style. I prefer an approach where sourcebooks are toolkits that allow people to play the game they wanted. I think one of the beauties of the original V1/V2 sourcebooks is that they did that. The concepts of the Camarilla and Sabbat (and other concepts) allowed people to roleplay a wide variety of vampire types.<br /> <br /> Whatever its merits, it seems V5 does not. And its a weakness. <br /> <br /> And I say this as someone who has never liked Necroscope style Vampires and eliminate Vicissitude entirely in the chronicles I ST around 20 years ago, and thus changed the Tzimisce into something I suspect is very much like V5's version. But that doesn't mean I don't understand that others do like the Discipline and the Clan's portrayal for decades, and they don't like how the game no longer supports that.<br /> <br /> The game's setting is breaking as a result of these metaplots. Each time they introduce retroactive continuity, and there are just too many retroactive continuity changes required to make it work. The setting is increasingly being damaged. It would not surprise me in some future V6 or V7 that the next group of developers decide the original seven clans of the Camarilla should rejoin, the Tzimisce (and other clans) be restored to what they were, and a \u201cback to the basics\u201d attempt is made to restore the setting; or that the merry-go-round approach to sects continues and we get yet another selection of clans of the Camarilla or even more bizarre changes.<br /> <br /> I think a better approach is to define the &quot;core&quot; elements of the Vampire setting, and realize there are now (at least) 3 different versions of it. Those different versions are simply examples of what one can do with the core setting, but shouldn't define them. Players, of course, have had even more variations in their home chronicles. In my opinion, it would be better of the game company to divide their published material into a core book dealing with mechanics and the core setting, and then a variety of approved &quot;metaplot/edition/variations&quot; sourcebooks that explore the different ways to approach it. Each of those visions can still be supported - especially now in a world with PDFs and print on demand versions don't require game stores to physically stock everything. Canon Elements of Vampire: the Masquerade (that is present in all incarnations; this is what V20 attempted to provide at least in its corebook)<ul><li>13 clans divided into the Camarilla, Sabbat, and Independents with individuals also belonging to Anarchs and other minor sects</li> <li>Camarilla as the dominant faction</li> <li>Jyhad / Manipulation by Methusalehs</li> <li>\u200bAntedeluvians are a mystery</li> </ul>Elements of the first era of Metaplot (Greenberg \u2013 V1/V2)<ul><li>Multi-layered Jyhad \u2013 Anarchs vs Prince, Prince vs Primogen, Prince vs Camarilla, some Anarchs against the Camarilla as an institution, Camarilla vs Sabbat, True Hand versus False Hand, Gehenna Cults; elder Vampires remaining in contact with past friends in rival sects</li> <li>Lots of unknown secrets \u2013 True Brujah, fate of the Cappadocians, nature of the Salubri</li> <li>Vicissitude as an Umbral Disease</li> <li>Lots of Bloodlines with mysterious origins</li> <li>Sympathetic vampires struggling with their condition a common element (perhaps too much)</li> <li>Encouragement of crossover with the rest of the WoD</li> <li>Often prone to gonzo elements at the highest level</li> </ul>Elements of the second era of Metaplot (Achilli - Rev)<ul><li>Sect politics most important element</li> <li>Sect conflicts along the lines of a military campaign</li> <li>Gehenna imminent so there are major changes to the setting to reflect that countdown</li> <li>Golconda is a lie or at least a disappointing reality</li> <li>Stronger emphasis that deviating from Humanity feeds the beast combined with belief vampires can't really follow Humanity to any large degree over time</li> <li>The events that happen in the metaplot essentially destroys the Masquerade, but the setting refuses to admit it</li> <li>Vicissitude now just an ordinary Discipline</li> <li>Clans have many sub-clans with separate mechanics</li> <li>Elimination of the elements of previous metaplots that conflict with the new style</li> <li>No crossover with the rest of the WoD</li> </ul>Elements of the third era of Metaplot (V5) / I admit this is my impression from hearsay as I've never read any V5 material<ul><li>Worldwide Wrestling/Soap Opera script-based approach to vampire politics - Clans change sect; clans split up; bloodlines join up to become one clan</li> <li>Very event driven in the sense that changes to the core setting are done just previous to Players playing in the game; these aren't events players participate in</li> <li>More humane vampires an option again, but generally most vampires depicted as evil</li> <li>Streamlining of mechanics while allowing more options, and these mechanical changes impact the setting accordingly</li> <li>Nostalgia for certain characters and ideas found in earlier editions that show again in more profound ways</li> <li>Elimination of the elements of previous metaplots that conflict with the new style</li> </ul>I'm sure others would articulate a different set of bullet points, but I think there is general agreement that these are very different styles of play, and that each subsequent version applied retroactive continuity changes to eliminate certain things in the previous edition and to set up unique things in their version.<br /> <br /> These are really three separate incarnations of the game's core setting. They're not really continuations of the prior version even though they make reference to many of the same characters and concepts. It's like the old Earth-1, Earth-2, Earth-3 and so on of DC's Pre-Crisis superhero comics. Each one has its own version of &quot;Superman&quot; (or whatever character) with its own lore and continuity, but they are not the same character.<br /> <br /> While I have my preferences, I have to admit that I'd probably have fun playing in any of these kind of chronicles once. But I find it distasteful that I'm told this is the way the setting will be going forward permanently (until, of course, another version comes around that invalidates this version).<br /> <br /> Of course, my own version played at my tables has elements from all of these as well as many things uniquely derived just from me. And the same goes for many other home chronicles of other players. They're compatible with the &quot;core&quot; setting - just not these metaplot separate interpretations.<br /> <br /> What I am looking for our tools that allow me to run the kind of vampire chronicle I want, as well as the occasional look at how others run their games so I can be inspired and steal new ideas. I don't want to be told to radically change my chronicle in order to accommodate the new metaplot setting - no matter how cool or interesting I may find it as a whole or as parts. I don't like the idea that new material seems to invalidate my own ideas.<br /> <br /> Game companies love metaplot because it's an easy way to get the fanbase to buy new sourcebooks that provides the revenue treadmill. However, I think that's an illusion. Because what ultimately happens is that fans of the game's previous incarnations simply stop supporting the game line at all and retreat back to their already purchased books. So after the initial rush of sold material, the company now has a much smaller fanbase buying materials than it did before.</div> </div> </div> </div>This broadly reflects my view, too. I liked how M20 presented conflicting metaplots as Future Fates, for example, giving us more, rather than less, choice. V5 definitely gives us less choice than V20.<br /> <br /> I like the Dragons as Old Clan Tzimisce. But it is reductive to make that the whole experience, rather than allowing for the breadth that was there before. Dracula is fine, and all, but Vykos is the signature Tzimisce character and should, therefore, be represented as a more viable choice than they are presently. Vykos was always more central to the game than Dracula.<br /> <br /> Discipline-wise, I'd give traditional Tzimisce:<br /> <br /> Animalism<br /> Auspex<br /> Blood Sorcery (optional swap: Protean)<br /> <br /> The Old Clan would swap Blood Sorcery for Dominate. Now you have all the different options again.<br /> <br /> But the more I engage with V5 as it is, the more I keep thinking I should finish my homebrew 'classic' VTM ruleset. V20 was very close to where the ideal VTM Classic would be, but still needed some fixes that only started to be hinted at late in the V20 line (e.g., V20DA's simplified combat).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-19T02:43:50-08:00","id":1429002,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taggie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1428599-v5-vampire-companion?p=1428970#post1428970\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> With everyone being on humanity, and the touchstone system and by the looks no replacement path system in sight, they have done the opposite of making it clear all vampires are monsters, the mechanics, again, do not support monsters at all, assholes yea, but not monsters. This is the most friendly neighborhood blood sucker the system has been, maybe ever, I half.expect Angelus and Spike to turn up at any second....</div> </div> </div> </div>You know 5th edition Humanity doesn't work that way anymore, right? It doesn't work like Paths but you can kill hundreds of people a year and not lose a single point of it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-19T04:03:04-08:00","id":1429006,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1428599-v5-vampire-companion?p=1429002#post1429002\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You know 5th edition Humanity doesn't work that way anymore, right? It doesn't work like Paths but you can kill hundreds of people a year and not lose a single point of it.</div> </div> </div> </div>We had this whole argument in another Thread already. As far as I remember even with the same Users on the same sides. Quite franky, I fail to see the benefit of having this conversation again.<br /> <br /> But to get at least a little bit on Topic again: to the 'V5 sucks' fraction, what exactly is missing in the Vicissitude write-up to make it viable? Is it 'just' the fact that its an amalgam now? Or would you say there are important parts of the old mechanics missing? (not a rhetorical question btw. I am realy interested in your Opinion <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> )","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26305-takeochan","name":"TakeoChan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26305_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"39"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-19T05:13:51-08:00","id":1429011,"title":"","content":"late to the party as usual.<br /> <br /> i've got mixed feelings about the new clans, i think this new direction for the ravnos is what the clan needed and i'm pleased with it but the devil's in the details, mostly the disciplines but regardless.<br /> <br /> my issues are mainly: that the banes of the ravnos and the salubri are a bit too harsh, the saubri specifically are being openly hunted by one of the clans, they have a massive target on their forehead, (which is also a masquerade breach let's be fair here) on top of that they bleed from it when using a discipline (so they can't try to use disciplines subtly and can potentially trigger hunger frenzies) and on top of that their blood is extra tasty, that just seems a bit like overkill to me.<br /> <br /> the new disciplines also leave somewhat to be desired (besides the tzimisce getting dominate) because up until now i was under the impression that amalgams where meant to keep previously class specific abilities mostly in clan but 2 out of 3 of the salubri specific abilities can be learned by the hecata and chimerstry can now be learned by the ministry while the ravnos now can host a insect swarm inside their body with the unliving hive amalgam which i thought was meant for the nosferatu. this is either a massive oversight or they've given up on amalgams to keep clan specific abilities mostly in clan which i'm most definitely not ok with.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25992,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25992-archderd","user":"archderd","date":".  i'm stupid: dementation is dominate/obfuscate, not dominate/auspex 12-19-2020, 09:22 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25992-archderd","name":"archderd","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25992_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-19T05:25:09-08:00","id":1429012,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1428599-v5-vampire-companion?p=1429002#post1429002\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You know 5th edition Humanity doesn't work that way anymore, right? It doesn't work like Paths but you can kill hundreds of people a year and not lose a single point of it.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> That is not the point, it is a stat that fives you a sex drive, makes you look human etc, how on earth following the Path of Caine properly should be tied in anyway to being a blushing horndog serial rapist (like most anarch vamps I have ever seen) is beyond me, yet you need to have a decent score in it for it's morality and mechanical effects beyond that. IT matters that you have human on your sheet at all, should all cam vamps have a paedophilia rating, to reflect the paedophile primogen? Ofc you'd have a low score in it to begin, but it would put unwanted effects on your character, and have some role in resisting certain effects...I know this is absurd, but I have tried at great length to make clear how much NO I feel about sabbat having humanity at all, and this is the only comparison I feel I can make to explain it, that has a chance of breaking through cycle of explaining to me yet again that v5 morality does not work that way, so I don't need to worry, I know it fails to function as paths, that is not the point. So will you launch yet another patronising attack? Or will you actually process what I am saying, finally?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25011,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","user":"Taggie","date":". 12-19-2020, 08:32 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","name":"Taggie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1047"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-19T05:45:44-08:00","id":1429013,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TakeoChan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1428599-v5-vampire-companion?p=1429006#post1429006\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is it 'just' the fact that its an amalgam now? Or would you say there are important parts of the old mechanics missing? (not a rhetorical question btw. I am realy interested in your Opinion <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> )</div> </div> </div> </div>Without reading the book itself to go into detail, yeah, that's a whole bunch of problems. <br /> <br /> First off, mechanically, Amalgams suck shit. They're normal disciplines but with an extra chore of getting another discipline to a certain level before you invest in them, which gets into further issue when you want a few amalgams or want to cross amalgams or you've got 5 in a discipline and now you can never learn another power when you totally could in V20. They're the worst of all worlds, mechanically speaking. <br /> <br /> Second, thematically, it basically undermines everything. Tzmisce are freaks and the camarilla elders can't fucking abide vicissitude. It's a discipline made from all the evil of some second gen, or it's a disease, or it's space aliens, or it came from lilith or kupala. For it to just be the lovechild of protean and... DOMINATE of all the fucking changes to give the Tzmisce... that's just... That's some serious stolen thunder right there. <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-19T06:02:05-08:00","id":1429014,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>archderd</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1428599-v5-vampire-companion?p=1429011#post1429011\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">the new disciplines also leave somewhat to be desired (besides the tzimisce getting dominate) because up until now i was under the impression that amalgams where meant to keep previously class specific abilities mostly in clan but the salubri have acces to dementation and 2 out of 3 of their specific abilities can be learned by the hecata and chimerstry can now be learned by the ministry while the ravnos now can host a insect swarm inside their body with the unliving hive amalgam which i thought was meant for the nosferatu. this is either a massive oversight or they've given up on amalgams to keep clan specific abilities mostly in clan which i'm most definitely not ok with.</div> </div> </div> </div>For me, the purpose of amalgams are mostly two. At first, you can lock specific powers from most of the Clans (true, there are some overlapses). This applies especialy to Character creation. I think, making these Powers more accessible is a 'good' thing. Players that have at least one Discipline in Clan and want to learn them now dont have to hunt down and potentialy diablerize lets say a Malkavian. They just need access to Obfu/Domi (whichever they dont already have) and can get dementation. This point applies to Players the most, since they would have the most desire to 'break out' of the boundries.<br /> The second benefit (at least in my eyes) is more variety in playstyles. So as a Tzim for example, you dont have to overcommit to Vicissitude now, you can get maybe the level 2 Power and decide that you dont need Fleshcraft but get other Protean Powers that suit your Character.<br /> For NPC Characters a ST should think about what is appropriate for them. Your Cam Prince despises Fleshcrafting? Dont give it to him just because he can.<br /> If you would want a more in-clan aspekt of certain powers, houserule a clan blood prequisite. That way Players could learn them with the right blood in their hands.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26305-takeochan","name":"TakeoChan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26305_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"39"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-19T06:49:38-08:00","id":1429019,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TakeoChan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1428599-v5-vampire-companion?p=1429014#post1429014\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> For me, the purpose of amalgams are mostly two. At first, you can lock specific powers from most of the Clans (true, there are some overlapses). This applies especialy to Character creation. I think, making these Powers more accessible is a 'good' thing. Players that have at least one Discipline in Clan and want to learn them now dont have to hunt down and potentialy diablerize lets say a Malkavian. They just need access to Obfu/Domi (whichever they dont already have) and can get dementation. This point applies to Players the most, since they would have the most desire to 'break out' of the boundries.<br /> The second benefit (at least in my eyes) is more variety in playstyles. So as a Tzim for example, you dont have to overcommit to Vicissitude now, you can get maybe the level 2 Power and decide that you dont need Fleshcraft but get other Protean Powers that suit your Character.<br /> For NPC Characters a ST should think about what is appropriate for them. Your Cam Prince despises Fleshcrafting? Dont give it to him just because he can.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>i'm was talking about in clan disciplines, i was misremebering some things about dementation but otherwise me point still stands. i don't mind that abilities have become more accessible but when previously clan specific abilities become accessible to other clans purely with in clan disciplines they're a bit too accessble.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <br /> If you would want a more in-clan aspekt of certain powers, houserule a clan blood prequisite. That way Players could learn them with the right blood in their hands.<br /> </div> </div> </div>i'm not going into it because i don't wanna risk the ire of the mods here but holy shit ma dude does that line fucking annoy me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25992-archderd","name":"archderd","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25992_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-19T06:52:34-08:00","id":1429021,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taggie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1428599-v5-vampire-companion?p=1429012#post1429012\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That is not the point, it is a stat that fives you a sex drive, makes you look human etc, how on earth following the Path of Caine properly should be tied in anyway to being a blushing horndog serial rapist (like most anarch vamps I have ever seen) is beyond me, yet you need to have a decent score in it for it's morality and mechanical effects beyond that. IT matters that you have human on your sheet at all, should all cam vamps have a paedophilia rating, to reflect the paedophile primogen? Ofc you'd have a low score in it to begin, but it would put unwanted effects on your character, and have some role in resisting certain effects...I know this is absurd, but I have tried at great length to make clear how much NO I feel about sabbat having humanity at all, and this is the only comparison I feel I can make to explain it, that has a chance of breaking through cycle of explaining to me yet again that v5 morality does not work that way, so I don't need to worry, I know it fails to function as paths, that is not the point. So will you launch yet another patronising attack? Or will you actually process what I am saying, finally?</div> </div> </div> </div>This actually makes sense to me because it's showing how much you control your Beast.<br /> <br /> It's no longer about how GOOD you are, which is ridiculous anyway.<br /> <br /> No, it's about how much self-control you have over the monster.<br /> <br /> It never made sense to me that a bunch of orgy-having decadent Path of Cathar members couldn't get it up (or lubricate to be technical) because they are assholes.<br /> <br /> Having sex is not a function of how ethical you are.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-19T07:02:52-08:00","id":1429023,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TakeoChan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1428599-v5-vampire-companion?p=1429006#post1429006\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> We had this whole argument in another Thread already. As far as I remember even with the same Users on the same sides. Quite franky, I fail to see the benefit of having this conversation again.<br /> <br /> But to get at least a little bit on Topic again: to the 'V5 sucks' fraction, what exactly is missing in the Vicissitude write-up to make it viable? Is it 'just' the fact that its an amalgam now? Or would you say there are important parts of the old mechanics missing? (not a rhetorical question btw. I am realy interested in your Opinion <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> )</div> </div> </div> </div>Not a V5 hater here, but admittedly a V5-struggling-to-love-er. I haven't seen anyone here or any other forum complain about the mechanics of Vicissitude being unacceptable apart from the strange Dominate amalgam. Historically, having Dominate as In Clan for the small population of Old Clan Tzimisce was exclusive with having Vicissitude. Now Vicissitude suddenly <i>depends</i> on Dominate? For the entire Clan?! <br /> <br /> And the rationale is absurd: you command your own flesh to obey. If you have any artistic, crafting or medical experience under your belt, you would link Vicissitude's molding, sculpting and invasive surgeries to Auspex (heightened senses, mental acuity, insight, awareness) before any other Discipline...and that's if it needed and amalgam at all, which it really doesn't. (Most amalgams requirements feel arbitrary, if not counter-intuitive.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24351-garygeneric","name":"Garygeneric","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24351_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"108"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-19T08:25:17-08:00","id":1429027,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1428599-v5-vampire-companion?p=1429021#post1429021\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It never made sense to me that a bunch of orgy-having decadent Path of Cathar members couldn't get it up (or lubricate to be technical) because they are assholes.<br /> <br /> Having sex is not a function of how ethical you are.</div> </div> </div> </div>To quote the musician Peaches &quot;Fuck the pain away&quot; or Depesh Mode &quot;Give me a pain that I'm used to&quot;. Cathars use over indulgence to keep the beast at bay, it was never about the sex or coke or extreme body mods. It's about taking away the pain of being inhuman.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3953-dwight","name":"Dwight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3953_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-19T08:31:38-08:00","id":1429028,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dwight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1428599-v5-vampire-companion?p=1429027#post1429027\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> To quote the musician Peaches &quot;Fuck the pain away&quot; or Depesh Mode &quot;Give me a pain that I'm used to&quot;. Cathars use over indulgence to keep the beast at bay, it was never about the sex or coke or extreme body mods. It's about taking away the pain of being inhuman.</div> </div> </div> </div>In my Sabbat games, one of the players had a very salient point. &quot;Some people hold the Beast down by suppressing it. Others glut it with sex, blood, and rock and roll.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-19T12:14:16-08:00","id":1429045,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1428599-v5-vampire-companion?p=1429021#post1429021\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This actually makes sense to me because it's showing how much you control your Beast.<br /> <br /> It's no longer about how GOOD you are, which is ridiculous anyway.<br /> <br /> No, it's about how much self-control you have over the monster.<br /> <br /> It never made sense to me that a bunch of orgy-having decadent Path of Cathar members couldn't get it up (or lubricate to be technical) because they are assholes.<br /> <br /> Having sex is not a function of how ethical you are.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> yet again you miss the point. If you really, truly cannot acknowledge the point I am making again, and again, and again, then why the hell respond? Seriously you just respond exactly the same every time, like I don't get your 'but vampires actually are just funny humans and Taggie is a complete idiot for wanting anything else and shouldn't play, Dracula is the perfect model and if you don't like him don't play' insinuations. in before you claim to love the sabbat while shitting on everything they are.<br /> <br /> In short, stop insulting my intelligence, stop implying I am an idiot, and stop you general, malicious insults.<br /> <br /> <br /> I don't want 'control over the monster' I want to, as the sabbat always have been to BE the monster.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25011,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","user":"Taggie","date":". 12-19-2020, 03:24 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","name":"Taggie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1047"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-19T12:34:10-08:00","id":1429048,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taggie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1428599-v5-vampire-companion?p=1429045#post1429045\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I want to, as the sabbat always have been to BE the monster.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's just not what the game is about, though. Never has been. There's no gothic horror in unflappably accepting &quot;oh I'm a bloodthirsty murderous monster, sweet.&quot; It's kind of like how Dungeons and Dragons is at its heart a combat game where 90% of the rules are about how to fight, and it goes against the spirit of the system to try to make it a medieval world simulator by statting out the economy. Or how Call of Cthulhu is about investigators getting way in over their heads and eventually getting killed or going mad as they fight things way above their capability - if you overhauled it to give the PCs a good shot at fighting minions of Elder Gods then the game stops being what it is. So too with VtM, it's not meant to be a game where your vampire toon specs out into a synergistic skill tree and stomps all his enemies, it's meant to be a game in which you play as a figure pretending to be human and trying to combat the beast within. Ignoring that ignores the core concept of the game.<br /> <br /> Obviously you can play anything however you want, but don't act like everyone in the world around you is wrong because they and the core rulebook are in agreement and you disagree with both.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25972-illithidactivity","name":"IllithidActivity","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25972_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"103"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-19T12:35:52-08:00","id":1429049,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>IllithidActivity</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1428599-v5-vampire-companion?p=1429048#post1429048\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's just not what the game is about, though. Never has been. There's no gothic horror in unflappably accepting &quot;oh I'm a bloodthirsty murderous monster, sweet.&quot; It's kind of like how Dungeons and Dragons is at its heart a combat game where 90% of the rules are about how to fight, and it goes against the spirit of the system to try to make it a medieval world simulator by statting out the economy. Or how Call of Cthulhu is about investigators getting way in over their heads and eventually getting killed or going mad as they fight things way above their capability - if you overhauled it to give the PCs a good shot at fighting minions of Elder Gods then the game stops being what it is. So too with VtM, it's not meant to be a game where your vampire toon specs out into a synergistic skill tree and stomps all his enemies, it's meant to be a game in which you play as a figure pretending to be human and trying to combat the beast within. Ignoring that ignores the core concept of the game.<br /> <br /> Obviously you can play anything however you want, but don't act like everyone in the world around you is wrong because they and the core rulebook are in agreement and you disagree with both.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Then tell that to 2e Sabbat, and to an extent Revised. I wasn't kidding about the Sabbat always having been that. (Oh and a fair chunk of the Roads in DA [all editions])","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","name":"Taggie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1047"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-19T12:42:53-08:00","id":1429050,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taggie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1428599-v5-vampire-companion?p=1429049#post1429049\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Then tell that to 2e Sabbat, and to an extent Revised. I wasn't kidding about the Sabbat always having been that. (Oh and a fair chunk of the Roads in DA [all editions])</div> </div> </div> </div>It takes just one look at the Lasombra and Tzimisce to recognize that they weren't in their conception meant to be playable. They're very obvious Bad Guys. Then players whined about not having access to every option imaginable, so they became playable, despite how overpowered they would be in comparison. Now V5 is keeping them playable, but scaling back both the mentality and the capabilities of those clans in order to bring them more in-line with all the others. Because obviously there <i>shouldn't</i> be two clans that are far and away stronger than all the others. But people are mad that their toys are being taken away.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25972-illithidactivity","name":"IllithidActivity","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25972_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"103"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-19T13:11:09-08:00","id":1429052,"title":"","content":"For me, I think that all the new Clans in the Companion will make for antagonists more than PCs.<br /> <br /> I like how they have completely removed any \u2018Gypsie\u2019 references from Ravnos, and while some players will like playing a Loki-like trickster, I think the constant nomadic aspect will stop them from being used in a long term city campaign. They will make an excellent, short term, Loki-like disrupter though, and you could get them involved with the PCs with the travel agent concept. Basically, if the PCs need to travel anywhere, you could make them an awkward NPC to make a deal with...<br /> <br /> I like that Salubri have been clarified as a historical ex-Clan (usurped by the Tremere - which means that the mystical 13 Clans total remains in tact) and they are so rare they are basically a plot hook. I can see a scenario like Children of Men, where the PCs are involved in smuggling a hunted Salubri in order to make some sort of gambit towards Golconda.....or just undermining the Tremere in some way. If they have to travel, it may mean they have to deal with the aforementioned Ravnos travel agent....<br /> <br /> I like that the Tzmisce is one of the most archetypal types of monstrous vampire, and actually combines the Dracula myth with Dr. Frankenstein in a way. Their limited movement - contrasted against the Ravnos actually - would still make them more of an NPC antagonist than a PC to me. But actually, they could be involved in the aforementioned conspiracy to smuggle the Salubri insofar that their experimentation could involve the blood of the Salubri to <i>reach</i> a state of Golconda. Maybe the PCs are, unbeknownst to them, surreptitiously smuggling the Salubri to a Tzmisce overlord....<br /> <br /> Good Anarch-based chronicle concept that! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2517-trippy","name":"Trippy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2517_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1018"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-19T13:13:13-08:00","id":1429053,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>IllithidActivity</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1428599-v5-vampire-companion?p=1429050#post1429050\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It takes just one look at the Lasombra and Tzimisce to recognize that they weren't in their conception meant to be playable. They're very obvious Bad Guys. Then players whined about not having access to every option imaginable, so they became playable, despite how overpowered they would be in comparison. Now V5 is keeping them playable, but scaling back both the mentality and the capabilities of those clans in order to bring them more in-line with all the others. Because obviously there <i>shouldn't</i> be two clans that are far and away stronger than all the others. But people are mad that their toys are being taken away.</div> </div> </div> </div>When have I mentioned power? I don't like merging disciplines for thematic reasons, but that is not a power issue. We had a glorious setting capable of telling many stories and genres..now we have Interview meets Lost boys with added mandatory abusive relationship simulator...<br /> <br /> If it was about power I would be celebrating the swapping of auspex for dominate not hacked off about it","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25011,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","user":"Taggie","date":". 12-19-2020, 04:27 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","name":"Taggie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1047"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-19T13:31:39-08:00","id":1429054,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taggie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1428599-v5-vampire-companion?p=1429045#post1429045\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">yet again you miss the point. If you really, truly cannot acknowledge the point I am making again, and again, and again, then why the hell respond? Seriously you just respond exactly the same every time, like I don't get your 'but vampires actually are just funny humans and Taggie is a complete idiot for wanting anything else and shouldn't play, Dracula is the perfect model and if you don't like him don't play' insinuations. in before you claim to love the sabbat while shitting on everything they are.<br /> <br /> In short, stop insulting my intelligence, stop implying I am an idiot, and stop you general, malicious insults.<br /> <br /> I don't want 'control over the monster' I want to, as the sabbat always have been to BE the monster.</div> </div> </div> </div>Allow me to clarify: <b>Taggie I'm not trying to insult your playstyle.</b><br /> <br /> Disagreement does not mean I don't think your way is valid.<br /> <br /> What matters is what's fun at your table. There's room for many different interpretations of Vampire: The Masquerade and I actually ENJOY discussing things with people who have a different take or outright disagree with me on things both fundamental.<br /> <br /> It's fun. I'm sorry if you're not having fun discussing these things. It is not my intention to frustrate you. I feel happy discussing V:TM's ins and outs with you.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-19T13:39:43-08:00","id":1429055,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1428599-v5-vampire-companion?p=1429054#post1429054\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Allow me to clarify: <b>Taggie I'm not trying to insult your playstyle.</b><br /> <br /> Disagreement does not mean I don't think your way is valid.<br /> <br /> What matters is what's fun at your table. There's room for many different interpretations of Vampire: The Masquerade and I actually ENJOY discussing things with people who have a different take or outright disagree with me on things both fundamental.<br /> <br /> It's fun. I'm sorry if you're not having fun discussing these things. It is not my intention to frustrate you. I feel happy discussing V:TM's ins and outs with you.</div> </div> </div> </div>That was not the impression I was getting. I was seeing you tell me, again,. That the Humanity system was perfect for what I wanted of only I would see that, when it isn't, I had explained, I thought at least, why it wasn't, in as many different ways I could think of, only to get the same response yet again. That is along side the issued I have with other aspects (how elders aren't scary any more, and meths are a joke, the discipline mergers breaking thematic parts of the setting, changes to discipline spread making aspects of the setting non sensical...and Hunger derailing everything with messy/bestial results.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25011,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","user":"Taggie","date":". 12-19-2020, 04:46 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","name":"Taggie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1047"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-19T13:49:06-08:00","id":1429057,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taggie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1428599-v5-vampire-companion?p=1429055#post1429055\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That was not the impression I was getting. I was seeing you tell me, again,. That the Humanity system was perfect for what I wanted of only I would see that, when it isn't, I had explained, I thought at least, why it wasn't, in as many different ways I could think of, only to get the same response yet again. That is along side the issued I have with other aspects (how elders aren't scary any more, and meths are a joke, the discipline mergers breaking thematic parts of the setting, changes to discipline spread making aspects of the setting non sensical...and Hunger derailing everything with messy/bestial results.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well it's not my intent. I was sharing why I felt that the addition of REVISED'S addition to the Humanity System, that the Sabbat get no sex drives and more corpse-looking so on was always weird. This is a 20 year old irritation of me.<br /> <br /> It's not a V5 defense.<br /> <br /> I think we actually agree more often than not that Revised shit on the Sabbat.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-19T13:56:47-08:00","id":1429061,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1428599-v5-vampire-companion?p=1429057#post1429057\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well it's not my intent. I was sharing why I felt that the addition of REVISED'S addition to the Humanity System, that the Sabbat get no sex drives and more corpse-looking so on was always weird. This is a 20 year old irritation of me.<br /> <br /> It's not a V5 defense.<br /> <br /> I think we actually agree more often than not that Revised shit on the Sabbat.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Sabbat looking more dead made perfect sense to me, like DAs resonance system, Path/Road mattered ( and yes DA did it better), Path walkers didn't look human because they weren't pretending to be human, they are the hungry dead and are fine with this (in general, YMMV with some Paths/Roads ) They are the children of Caine, not the children of Seth anymore ((doing that from memory mea culpa if it isn't Seth)). Plus looking like creepy walking corpses fit them very.well, it tore off the self righteous mask to expose the monster, in a way that instinctively unsettles people, in a way they can't explain. So they look like corpses not because the beast is in the ascendant, but because their paths don't even try to put on that mask.<br /> <br /> <br /> In contrast, a vampire walking humanity is weaving that illusion/delusion and his blood reflects that desire on his corpse, keeping it fresher.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25011,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","user":"Taggie","date":". 12-19-2020, 05:02 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","name":"Taggie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1047"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-19T14:01:34-08:00","id":1429062,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taggie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1428599-v5-vampire-companion?p=1429061#post1429061\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The Sabbat looking more dead made perfect sense to me, like DAs resonance system, Path/Road mattered ( and yes DA did it better), Path walkers didn't look human because they weren't pretending to be human, they are the hungry dead and are fine with this (in general, YMMV with some Paths/Roads ) They are the children of Caine, not the children of Seth anymore ((doing that from memory mea culpa if it isn't Seth)). Plus looking like creepy walking corpses fit them very.well, it tore off the self righteous mask to expose the monster, in a way that instinctively unsettles people, in a way they can't explain. So they look like corpses not because the beast is in the ascendant, but because their paths don't even try to put on that mask.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think the difference there is a Sabbat vampire isn't going to worry about getting new clothes, bathing, and trying to primp. I.e they'll look like 30 Days of Night vampires because they have abandoned human norms.<br /> <br /> Which is different from the system that says, &quot;your biology physically changes the Higher or Lower your Humanity is.&quot;<br /> <br /> Which I interpret as the Beast's power over you.<br /> <br /> But YMMV.<br /> <br /> It's just my interpretation and is not canon or supported by it. Your version is perfectly fine too.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-19T14:03:44-08:00","id":1429064,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1428599-v5-vampire-companion?p=1428942#post1428942\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Re-Damn Diculous.<br /> <br /> Name the fans you know personally who are V:TR fans who are appealed to by these V5 changes. I've been playing since 1995 and I NEVER liked V:TR.<br /> <br /> It's not my bag.<br /> <br /> I like V5 because it's a return to classic Vampire: The Masquerade, 1st and 2nd Edition. A move away from the big globe trotting sect wars to the personal intimate city-based stories like Chicago and Milwaukee by Night.</div> </div> </div> </div>I <i>did </i>rather like VtR and ran an online London game using it, and I mostly like the V5 changes. I prefer VtM, though.<br /> <br /> I started with VtM in '92 when I bought the 2nd edition book, and I agree with you - V5 feels like a return to the game's thematic roots.<br /> <br /> That said, my initial reaction was that they were over-Requiem-ing, over-year-zero-ising VtM, throwing out too much of the lore, too much of the backstory, too many of the established elder characters who provided a link to the setting's past. Power equalisation and the new, 5-max attributes could just as easily have been explained by changes wrought by the Red Star, without using the Beckoning to Blackadder the entire royal court.<br /> <br /> Fortunately there seems to have been some rowing back from the initial slash-and-burn enthusiasm. Fall of London and the Chicago trilogy of books were very strong on continuity and featured plenty of elder characters. It's feeling more like a cleanup than a purge now, and I do like most of the mechanics and a lot of the metaplot developments.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/100-jezmiller","name":"JezMiller","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"437"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-19T14:17:43-08:00","id":1429065,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1428599-v5-vampire-companion?p=1429062#post1429062\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think the difference there is a Sabbat vampire isn't going to worry about getting new clothes, bathing, and trying to primp. I.e they'll look like 30 Days of Night vampires because they have abandoned human norms.<br /> <br /> Which is different from the system that says, &amp;quot;your biology physically changes the Higher or Lower your Humanity is.&amp;quot;<br /> <br /> Which I interpret as the Beast's power over you.<br /> <br /> But YMMV.<br /> <br /> It's just my interpretation and is not canon or supported by it. Your version is perfectly fine too.</div> </div> </div> </div>The rules support your take, and it's a take that makes the Sabbat wrong at a RAW level, like the rules of the universe don't support their ideological rejection of Humanity.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","name":"Taggie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1047"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-19T14:22:13-08:00","id":1429066,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taggie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1428599-v5-vampire-companion?p=1429065#post1429065\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The rules support your take, and it's a take that makes the Sabbat wrong at a RAW level, like the rules of the universe don't support their ideological rejection of Humanity.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think I'm getting we're we ran into our problem.<br /> <br /> I think Humanity is arguably a dumb thing to have in the rules to begin with because humans are the worst people in the universe. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> I feel like it never should have been linked your self-control, your status as a human, and your ethics.<br /> <br /> But yes, the Sabbat reject being human. They are immortal gods.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://youtu.be/wiCTUbwWfCY\" data-code=\"wiCTUbwWfCY\" data-provider=\"youtube_share\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/wiCTUbwWfCY/hqdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-19T14:22:53-08:00","id":1429067,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taggie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1428599-v5-vampire-companion?p=1428998#post1428998\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You said it your self HUMAN morals and ethics. Literally that, and having a high score in it gives you human urges, and human appearance.....makes the human more important and obvious, and keeping that score is tied to human morality pets.</div> </div> </div> </div>You desperately need to read the entire thing I wrote and not just cherry pick the words you think support your argument. Vampires <i>used to be </i>human. But they're <i>not</i>. They're bloodsucking predators and they struggle with their vampiric instincts vs. their human morals and ethics. I need you to understand this, because you're not making any sense.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taggie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1428599-v5-vampire-companion?p=1428998#post1428998\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Fine for Anne Rice's Vampire Chronicles, not great for 30 Days of Night, Sub Species, The Strain etc (also The Thing makes a great Tzim Methuselah, while The Flesh That Hates and Sarkism in general are near perfect Metamorphosis inspiration)</div> </div> </div> </div>The only vampire in Anne Rice who even <i>approaches</i> anything like VtM's humanity in any edition but V5 is Louis in Interview With the Vampire. In The Vampire Lestat, we see Lestat exult in killing humans over and over and over and over again. And Gabrielle. And Armand. And Marius. And Claudia. And virtually all of them. They don't as a general struggle with their nature, and the one who <i>does</i> is seen as either a bit odd or a bit endearing for it.<br /> <br /> The Thing is a cosmic horror, and a terrible model for how to do Tzimisce, who like all other vampires, used to be human. Vampire: The Masquerade is certainly written around a lot of Vampire stories, I'm not sure that going full bore into some of those interpretations of vampirism is really actually a good way to handle this game.<br /> <br /> The whole &quot;vicissitude is aliens from elsewhere&quot; thing was a bad idea. The whole &quot;vicissitude is the Tzimisce founders' will&quot; thing was better, but a singular notion of what constitutes Tzimisce is utterly boring.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taggie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1428599-v5-vampire-companion?p=1428998#post1428998\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No I don't know what is coming, my point was what we have now doesn't work, as a counter to your statement about it not being necessary, and what we have seen of Tzimisce in companion is not encouraging at all, as what I liked about them has been retconned, or downplayed. Also given that the Revised Sabbat is my least liked version (2e doom cultist for unlife!) His name brings mixed feelings, yes he is a change, but it doesn't bring confidence that he likes the aspects of the setting I do.</div> </div> </div> </div>I can already think of at least one model that'd work fine. A Sabbat chronicle will have its own tenets, and individual characters will have their own relevant convictions. It's not going to be hard to derive some from any given path that exists in V20 or earlier. And V5 is clearly not bound to obey older books, meaning that whatever Sabbat do as a touchstone thing will be fine. You can do this with the humanity rules now.<br /> <br /> The new Tzimisce are miles better than the old. You can still do the older stuff as well as some newer stuff. Everyone doesn't have to be an alien murderer. Tzimisce do not have to by default be inhuman. It's great.<br /> <br /> Anyway, Justin was the best dev Vampire ever had and his take on the Sabbat was the best take. I'm happy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2367,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","user":"Resplendent Fire","date":". 12-19-2020, 05:28 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-19T14:36:51-08:00","id":1429069,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>IllithidActivity</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1428599-v5-vampire-companion?p=1429050#post1429050\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It takes just one look at the Lasombra and Tzimisce to recognize that they weren't in their conception meant to be playable. They're very obvious Bad Guys. Then players whined about not having access to every option imaginable, so they became playable, despite how overpowered they would be in comparison. Now V5 is keeping them playable, but scaling back both the mentality and the capabilities of those clans in order to bring them more in-line with all the others. Because obviously there <i>shouldn't</i> be two clans that are far and away stronger than all the others. But people are mad that their toys are being taken away.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is literally not what happened. The Player's Guide to the Sabbat was published in 1992 and the Storyteller's Handbook in 1993. The PGttS was the first book to feature the Lasombra and Tzimisce in full, as well as to explain the concept of antitribu as well as playing Sabbat characters and running Sabbat chronicles. Players didn't <i>whine</i> about anything, they were never set up as NPC only material, that's some kind of weird received wisdom that just floats around this forum because apparently either no one was there or they don't remember what happened.<br /> <br /> Also they weren't overpowered. Obtenebration and Vicissitude weren't all that power and each only had one power devoted directly to combat, and both were fairly blatant uses.<br /> <br /> There was no period during which Lasombra and Tzimisce were written up fully but were not explicitly presented as player options.<br /> <br /> Oh yeah, I wrote something about this last month as well:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Resplendent Fire</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1413085-obtenebration-or-oblivion?p=1425867#post1425867\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I keep seeing this and it bugs me, and I seem to recall this has come up on other occasions, but:<br /> <br /> The Lasombra, Tzimisce, etc. were introduced along with their disciplines in the Player's Guide to the Sabbat in 1992, an early supplement for V:tM second edition<br /> The Storyteller's Handbook to the Sabbat was a second edition sourcebook published in 1993, and was intended as a companion to the PGttS. It didn't repeat material from the PG, but added more stuff such as bloodlines, material on infernalists, and so on.<br /> <br /> They were never introduced as &quot;Storyteller only clans&quot; that needed correcting to make them viable for PCs, they were always intended to be playable.<br /> <br /> RPGGeek lists its publication date as 1993: <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/2300/Storytellers-Handbook-to-the-Sabbat-WW2225\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product...-Sabbat-WW2225</a><br /> <br /> And PGttS as 1992: <a href=\"https://rpggeek.com/rpgitem/44483/players-guide-sabbat\" target=\"_blank\">https://rpggeek.com/rpgitem/44483/players-guide-sabbat</a><br /> <br /> The preview for the STHttS on dtrpg also says copyright 1993, but the player's guide to the sabbat is from a later printing (1997) Steven Brown wrote both, however and his last work for Vampire was in 1994, Dirty Secrets of the Black Hand <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Steven_C._Brown\" target=\"_blank\">https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Steven_C._Brown</a><br /> <br /> That page dates Freak Legion at 1999 and that doesn't right to me, but the page for Freak Legion says 1995, which does.<br /> <br /> This leaves me trying to figure out who was developing Vampire between Dirty Secrets and Vampire Revised, as my impression was Greenberg's last developed product was that. Edit: Rob Hatch developed during the interim</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2367,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","user":"Resplendent Fire","date":". 12-19-2020, 05:41 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-19T15:04:42-08:00","id":1429074,"title":"","content":"Edit: Got confused.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26564,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26564-badfurryfanfic","user":"BadFurryFanFic","date":". 12-19-2020, 06:07 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26564-badfurryfanfic","name":"BadFurryFanFic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"93"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-19T15:23:30-08:00","id":1429077,"title":"","content":"Apropos of nothing from the last dozen pages or so, I'll just say that I am incredibly happy with the Companion because there's enough info in the Ghouls section to extrapolate a Dhampir as a ghoul who doesn't need to be fed monthly but otherwise follows all other rules for Ghoul PCs.<br /> <br /> Time to see what converting my Dhampir to V5 looks like.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1328-chris24601","name":"Chris24601","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-19T15:38:38-08:00","id":1429082,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Resplendent Fire</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1428599-v5-vampire-companion?p=1429069#post1429069\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There was no period during which Lasombra and Tzimisce were written up fully but were not explicitly presented as player options.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you for typing this post. Of all the bizarre claims about the history of the game that I've seen floating around, the idea that the Lasombra and Tzimisce powers were originally designed for NPC use only is among the strangest. I have no idea where this meme originates from -- there isn't enough text in all of 1st Edition about the Lasombra and Tzimisce (then called Tzimisces) for even one clan writeup, let alone any game mechanics for either clan.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1190-elphilm","name":"Elphilm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1190_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"763"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-19T15:39:54-08:00","id":1429083,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elphilm</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1428599-v5-vampire-companion?p=1429082#post1429082\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thank you for typing this post. Of all the bizarre claims about the history of the game that I've seen floating around, the idea that the Lasombra and Tzimisce powers were originally designed for NPC use only is among the strangest. I have no idea where this meme originates from -- there isn't enough text in all of 1st Edition about the Lasombra and Tzimisce (then called Tzimisces) for even one clan writeup, let alone any game mechanics for either clan.</div> </div> </div> </div>No problem. I don't know either? I don't think anyone's lying, I just think it sort of evolved out of the community at some point?<br /> <br /> I just wrote a longer post about it, though.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1429081-lasombra-and-tzimisce-were-never-introduced-as-npc-only-options\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/filedata/fetch?filedataid=1074\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1429081-lasombra-and-tzimisce-were-never-introduced-as-npc-only-options\"> Lasombra and Tzimisce were never introduced as NPC-only options - Onyx Path Forums </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1429081-lasombra-and-tzimisce-were-never-introduced-as-npc-only-options\"> http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1429081-lasombra-and-tzimisce-were-never-introduced-as-npc-only-options </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> Both received their first full writeup in the Player's Guide to the Sabbat in 1992, right after VtM2e came out and a bit over a year after VtM came out. They were </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-19T15:58:17-08:00","id":1429086,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taggie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1428599-v5-vampire-companion?p=1429061#post1429061\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The Sabbat looking more dead made perfect sense to me, like DAs resonance system, Path/Road mattered ( and yes DA did it better), Path walkers didn't look human because they weren't pretending to be human, they are the hungry dead and are fine with this (in general, YMMV with some Paths/Roads ) They are the children of Caine, not the children of Seth anymore ((doing that from memory mea culpa if it isn't Seth)). Plus looking like creepy walking corpses fit them very.well, it tore off the self righteous mask to expose the monster, in a way that instinctively unsettles people, in a way they can't explain. So they look like corpses not because the beast is in the ascendant, but because their paths don't even try to put on that mask.<br /> <br /> <br /> In contrast, a vampire walking humanity is weaving that illusion/delusion and his blood reflects that desire on his corpse, keeping it fresher.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Pre-V5, the only Sabbat that looked like corpses explicitly were the Harbingers. Other Sabbat on Paths (excluding Nosferatu antitribu who always look ugly) just seem to have a strange &quot;bearing&quot; to mortals, but nothing that'd key-in to be corpselike.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Jade Kingdom Warrior","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","name":"Shakanaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"951"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-19T20:19:49-08:00","id":1429106,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Resplendent Fire</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1428599-v5-vampire-companion?p=1429067#post1429067\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You desperately need to read the entire thing I wrote and not just cherry pick the words you think support your argument. Vampires <i>used to be </i>human. But they're <i>not</i>. They're bloodsucking predators and they struggle with their vampiric instincts vs. their human morals and ethics. I need you to understand this, because you're not making any sense.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> The only vampire in Anne Rice who even <i>approaches</i> anything like VtM's humanity in any edition but V5 is Louis in Interview With the Vampire. In The Vampire Lestat, we see Lestat exult in killing humans over and over and over and over again. And Gabrielle. And Armand. And Marius. And Claudia. And virtually all of them. They don't as a general struggle with their nature, and the one who <i>does</i> is seen as either a bit odd or a bit endearing for it.<br /> <br /> The Thing is a cosmic horror, and a terrible model for how to do Tzimisce, who like all other vampires, used to be human. Vampire: The Masquerade is certainly written around a lot of Vampire stories, I'm not sure that going full bore into some of those interpretations of vampirism is really actually a good way to handle this game.<br /> <br /> The whole &amp;quot;vicissitude is aliens from elsewhere&amp;quot; thing was a bad idea. The whole &amp;quot;vicissitude is the Tzimisce founders' will&amp;quot; thing was better, but a singular notion of what constitutes Tzimisce is utterly boring.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> I can already think of at least one model that'd work fine. A Sabbat chronicle will have its own tenets, and individual characters will have their own relevant convictions. It's not going to be hard to derive some from any given path that exists in V20 or earlier. And V5 is clearly not bound to obey older books, meaning that whatever Sabbat do as a touchstone thing will be fine. You can do this with the humanity rules now.<br /> <br /> The new Tzimisce are miles better than the old. You can still do the older stuff as well as some newer stuff. Everyone doesn't have to be an alien murderer. Tzimisce do not have to by default be inhuman. It's great.<br /> <br /> Anyway, Justin was the best dev Vampire ever had and his take on the Sabbat was the best take. I'm happy.</div> </div> </div> </div>I do understand that it's the beast Vs human ethics that indeed is the theme of camirilla and anarch games, it is not and never has been anything Todo with Sabbat games. Vampires are not human, human ethics do not apply to beings that aren't human.<br /> <br /> As to.Sabbat tenets and Path convictions, as I previously stated..I tried that, it doesn't work,.we play tested it (this was the last WoD game I could convince people to play) the paths don't care about the same things, their sins aren't the same so it's impossible to make Tenets for them, Inner Voice really doesn't care about the same things Cathari or Caine or Honourable Accord do, and they don't agree with each other.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","name":"Taggie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1047"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-19T20:22:22-08:00","id":1429107,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shakanaka</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1428599-v5-vampire-companion?p=1429086#post1429086\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Pre-V5, the only Sabbat that looked like corpses explicitly were the Harbingers. Other Sabbat on Paths (excluding Nosferatu antitribu who always look ugly) just seem to have a strange &amp;quot;bearing&amp;quot; to mortals, but nothing that'd key-in to be corpselike.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes and no, vamps on path could not use blush iirc, I'd have to double check tho.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","name":"Taggie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1047"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-19T21:08:30-08:00","id":1429113,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taggie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1428599-v5-vampire-companion?p=1429106#post1429106\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I do understand that it's the beast Vs human ethics that indeed is the theme of camirilla and anarch games, it is not and never has been anything Todo with Sabbat games. Vampires are not human, human ethics do not apply to beings that aren't human.<br /> <br /> As to.Sabbat tenets and Path convictions, as I previously stated..I tried that, it doesn't work,.we play tested it (this was the last WoD game I could convince people to play) the paths don't care about the same things, their sins aren't the same so it's impossible to make Tenets for them, Inner Voice really doesn't care about the same things Cathari or Caine or Honourable Accord do, and they don't agree with each other.</div> </div> </div> </div>You do realize that Humanity as done in previous editions doesn't work for 5th Edition either. Similar names aside.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-19T21:22:29-08:00","id":1429115,"title":"","content":"If human ethics don't apply to vampires then why have VtM in the first place? Why write stories about vampires who struggle with their human socialization vs. their undead predator instincts? Why even make them relatable?<br /> <br /> There are things the <i>Sabbat</i> cares about, and that's the sort of thing the chronicle tenets should be - or more specifically, what the players and ST decide are important for any given chronicle. Individual convictions would be about paths. You can't have the same path of enlightenment experience in V5 as you did in previous versions, and that's a feature of the system. It'll be fine. It's practically a new game, and if you don't respect the fact that it's a new game, you're going to run into trouble trying to convert older material. And if you want the old paths of enlightenment experience, it's still intact in earlier editions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-19T22:33:39-08:00","id":1429117,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Resplendent Fire</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1428599-v5-vampire-companion?p=1429115#post1429115\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If human ethics don't apply to vampires then why have VtM in the first place? Why write stories about vampires who struggle with their human socialization vs. their undead predator instincts? Why even make them relatable?</div> </div> </div> </div>I believe he's referring specifically to Sabbat Games ( and I would venture Dark Ages games) where those aspects are simply not integral to the chronicle in any way shape or form. So why would those aspects be of import in chronicles they do not feature in?<br /> <br /> I mean, my answer would be the same as yours, V5 is not really robust enough to handle chronicles outside a certain paradigm so you will need to got to older iterations in order to play them.<br /> <br /> I would not however call it a new game as that tends to get looked upon rather poorly by the management here.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26564,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26564-badfurryfanfic","user":"BadFurryFanFic","date":". 12-20-2020, 01:36 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26564-badfurryfanfic","name":"BadFurryFanFic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"93"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-19T22:35:05-08:00","id":1429118,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Resplendent Fire</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1428599-v5-vampire-companion?p=1429115#post1429115\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If human ethics don't apply to vampires then why have VtM in the first place? Why write stories about vampires who struggle with their human socialization vs. their undead predator instincts? Why even make them relatable?<br /> <br /> There are things the <i>Sabbat</i> cares about, and that's the sort of thing the chronicle tenets should be - or more specifically, what the players and ST decide are important for any given chronicle. Individual convictions would be about paths. You can't have the same path of enlightenment experience in V5 as you did in previous versions, and that's a feature of the system. It'll be fine. It's practically a new game, and if you don't respect the fact that it's a new game, you're going to run into trouble trying to convert older material. And if you want the old paths of enlightenment experience, it's still intact in earlier editions.</div> </div> </div> </div>Because.human ethics as applied to vampire is schtick of 2 of the 3 sects. For anarchs and cam.games it is a pillar of the chronicle, but the Sabbat are the ones who reject that idea they are the ones who went.looking for something else. It's why I enjoy Sabbat games, but not Anarch and Cam ones <br /> <br /> Oh and just.play old editions...great fantastic...with who? Right now my choices are v5 or nothing.<br /> <br /> If v5 is as changes as you claim why advertise it as a vtm game? I mean if they hated the previous editions that much why even use the name?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","name":"Taggie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1047"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-19T22:37:43-08:00","id":1429119,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BadFurryFanFic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1428599-v5-vampire-companion?p=1429117#post1429117\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I believe he's referring specifically to Sabbat Games ( and I would venture Dark Ages games) where those aspects are simply not integral to the chronicle in any way shape or form. So why would those aspects be of import in chronicles they do not feature in?</div> </div> </div> </div>Exactly. Humanity had never been a feature and I flat do not care about, and do not enjoy Chronicles where it is.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","name":"Taggie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1047"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-19T22:44:46-08:00","id":1429120,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BadFurryFanFic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1428599-v5-vampire-companion?p=1429117#post1429117\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I believe he's referring specifically to Sabbat Games ( and I would venture Dark Ages games) where those aspects are simply not integral to the chronicle in any way shape or form. So why would those aspects be of import in chronicles they do not feature in?<br /> <br /> I mean, my answer would be the same as yours, V5 is not really robust enough to handle chronicles outside a certain paradigm so you will need to got to older iterations in order to play them.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think V5 is robust enough to handle the Sabbat, but just as with Humanity it would not be handled the way it was in previous editions.<br /> <br /> I know he's talking about the Sabbat, but also has said stuff that vampires on Humanity are humans and I feel like there's a communication breakdown somewhere. More accurately, he said <i>I </i>said that Camarilla vampires are human.<br /> <br /> Anyway, it sounds like he wants a Sabbat game where everyone can just kill and be depraved without consequences and I don't know why he doesn't just go ahead and do that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-19T22:52:22-08:00","id":1429122,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Resplendent Fire</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1428599-v5-vampire-companion?p=1429120#post1429120\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think V5 is robust enough to handle the Sabbat, but just as with Humanity it would not be handled the way it was in previous editions.<br /> <br /> I know he's talking about the Sabbat, but also has said stuff that vampires on Humanity are humans and I feel like there's a communication breakdown somewhere. More accurately, he said <i>I </i>said that Camarilla vampires are human.<br /> <br /> Anyway, it sounds like he wants a Sabbat game where everyone can just kill and be depraved without consequences and I don't know why he doesn't just go ahead and do that.</div> </div> </div> </div>I want inhuman ethics, I don't want fanged humans, which is what V5 gives us. Human does not mean nice btw. It's not killing and being depraved I ma after.it.is being totally inhuman, alien and other. If it was about depravity, the mandatory abusive relationship system, aka touchstones has that covered.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25011,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","user":"Taggie","date":". 12-20-2020, 03:44 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","name":"Taggie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1047"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-20T05:25:10-08:00","id":1429134,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BadFurryFanFic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1428599-v5-vampire-companion?p=1429117#post1429117\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would not however call it a new game as that tends to get looked upon rather poorly by the management here.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would. Because it IS a new game in the same way that D&amp;D 5e is a new game compared to 4E, 3e and AD&amp;D. The mechanics ARE different. That's inarguable.<br /> <br /> What is supposed to be the same between editions of VtM is the SETTING and the new additions of late seem to be getting it more back onto that course. I may not like all the metaplot-y bits (the changes to the Ravnos bane basically make V5 impossible to convert to until the current chronicle is well and truly ended), but at least they're a bit more recognizable now.<br /> <br /> As this relates the Sabbat; it means there's still a bit of work to do... alternate mechanical options from the Humanity/Touchstone system primarily... before the Sabbat can be properly played as Taggie would like in V5. By the same token, they'd need to do some work on presenting some of the original clan banes before V5 would be very useful in presenting a historical campaign (ex. the new Ravnos bane specifically mentions it becoming such with the Antediluvian's death... so it shouldn't apply in the 1980's or 1780's).<br /> <br /> Those are only flaws in the system if no upcoming work (ex. the Sabbat book) is used to add those elements to the system. Until then we can just say the new system is incomplete.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1328-chris24601","name":"Chris24601","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-20T07:47:56-08:00","id":1429142,"title":"","content":"Found an interesting review of it.<br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=H2zYdujv_nk\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=H2zYdujv_nk\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=H2zYdujv_nk\" target=\"_blank\"> https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=H2zYdujv_nk </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3953-dwight","name":"Dwight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3953_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-20T08:01:17-08:00","id":1429143,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chris24601</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1428599-v5-vampire-companion?p=1429134#post1429134\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would. Because it IS a new game in the same way that D&amp;D 5e is a new game compared to 4E, 3e and AD&amp;D. The mechanics ARE different. That's inarguable.<br /> <br /> What is supposed to be the same between editions of VtM is the SETTING and the new additions of late seem to be getting it more back onto that course. I may not like all the metaplot-y bits (the changes to the Ravnos bane basically make V5 impossible to convert to until the current chronicle is well and truly ended), but at least they're a bit more recognizable now.<br /> <br /> As this relates the Sabbat; it means there's still a bit of work to do... alternate mechanical options from the Humanity/Touchstone system primarily... before the Sabbat can be properly played as Taggie would like in V5. By the same token, they'd need to do some work on presenting some of the original clan banes before V5 would be very useful in presenting a historical campaign (ex. the new Ravnos bane specifically mentions it becoming such with the Antediluvian's death... so it shouldn't apply in the 1980's or 1780's).<br /> <br /> Those are only flaws in the system if no upcoming work (ex. the Sabbat book) is used to add those elements to the system. Until then we can just say the new system is incomplete.</div> </div> </div> </div>It\u2019s not a new game. It is a new edition of the same game. Regardless of system changes, that is the fact and unlike D&amp;D which has only ever had an implied system with associated settings, the Vampire game is wedded to the Wold of Darkness as part of the core game experience. <br /> <br /> The system in V5 is not dependent on details about the Sabbat, in the same manner that the first two editions of the game didn\u2019t detail the Sabbat. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2517-trippy","name":"Trippy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2517_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1018"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-20T08:04:04-08:00","id":1429144,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Trippy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1428599-v5-vampire-companion?p=1429143#post1429143\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It\u2019s not a new game. It is a new edition of the same game. Regardless of system changes, that is the fact and unlike D&amp;D which has only ever had an implied system with associated settings, the Vampire game is wedded to the Wold of Darkness as part of the core game experience.<br /> <br /> The system in V5 is not dependent on details about the Sabbat, in the same manner that the first two editions of the game didn\u2019t detail the Sabbat.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Players Guide to the Sabbat came out for 2e, and so a little later did the ST guide, as well as Sabbat appearing in a basic form in Chicago by Night. They have been in the game from pretty much the start.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","name":"Taggie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1047"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-20T08:22:54-08:00","id":1429145,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taggie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1428599-v5-vampire-companion?p=1429144#post1429144\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Players Guide to the Sabbat came out for 2e, and so a little later did the ST guide, as well as Sabbat appearing in a basic form in Chicago by Night. They have been in the game from pretty much the start.</div> </div> </div> </div>As a <i>supplement</i> to the core game, and it was never a requirement for any ST to include the Sabbat as playable options (till maybe Vampire Revised which included them in the core). They were detailed in the first two editions of the core game as boogymen figures - much in line with how they are in V5. We now know that V5 has a supplement for the Sabbat coming, but it doesn\u2019t make the core system \u2018incomplete' for the waiting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2517-trippy","name":"Trippy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2517_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1018"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-20T08:40:20-08:00","id":1429147,"title":"","content":"Didn't the Tzmisce and Lasombra come in with <i><u>The Players Guide</u> to the Sabbat. ? </i><br /> <br /> Does V5 really have a sabbat book coming, in any recognizable form? If they say Sabbat but we get... Anarchs but Chaotic Evil or Baali but not really inferalist... is that really &quot;The Sabbat&quot;? With everyone in the middle east, what are we even dealing with? Remnants? Something entirely different? Vampires in an active armed conflict set in a place the majority of our pasty-faced players aren't familiar with and aren't likely to do justice? We gonna have some Morytania style city where vampires rule openly? I'd like to believe in a reconquista, but based off of current trends, it's doubtful they'd do something so... damage control based.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-20T08:51:38-08:00","id":1429151,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Trippy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1428599-v5-vampire-companion?p=1429143#post1429143\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It\u2019s not a new game. It is a new edition of the same game. Regardless of system changes, that is the fact and unlike D&amp;D which has only ever had an implied system with associated settings, the Vampire game is wedded to the Wold of Darkness as part of the core game experience.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks to D&amp;D (primarily WotC), tabletop RPGs are literally the only entertainment medium where edition doesn't mean &quot;new printing of the same material with some minor edits&quot; but can include &quot;completely new system with only the trappings of previous material attached.&quot;<br /> <br /> By this definition checkers and chess would be the same game because they both have the same setting (an 8x8 bi-colored board) even though their mechanics are entirely different.<br /> <br /> Similarly, D&amp;D has had the Forgotten Realms setting persist from AD&amp;D through the present and yet none of the D&amp;D fans have a problem acknowledging that different mechanics make each edition its own game system with similar fluff.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1328-chris24601","name":"Chris24601","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-20T08:52:11-08:00","id":1429152,"title":"","content":"Yes, there is a Sabbat book coming.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2517-trippy","name":"Trippy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2517_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1018"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-20T08:53:55-08:00","id":1429153,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chris24601</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1428599-v5-vampire-companion?p=1429151#post1429151\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thanks to D&amp;D (primarily WotC), tabletop RPGs are literally the only entertainment medium where edition doesn't mean &quot;new printing of the same material with some minor edits&quot; but can include &quot;completely new system with only the trappings of previous material attached.&quot;<br /> <br /> By this definition checkers and chess would be the same game because they both have the same setting (an 8x8 bi-colored board) even though their mechanics are entirely different.<br /> <br /> Similarly, D&amp;D has had the Forgotten Realms setting persist from AD&amp;D through the present and yet none of the D&amp;D fans have a problem acknowledging that different mechanics make each edition its own game system with similar fluff.</div> </div> </div> </div>I guess you\u2019ve never heard of Warhammer 40K?<br /> <br /> And no, checkers and chess are not the same game. Neither game has a setting. A playing board is not a setting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2517-trippy","name":"Trippy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2517_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1018"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-20T09:25:58-08:00","id":1429160,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dwight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1428599-v5-vampire-companion?p=1429142#post1429142\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Found an interesting review of it.<br /> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=H2zYdujv_nk\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v