dition. The first 'appearance\u2019 as a reference in the first edition were that of potential boogeyman antagonists.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2517-trippy","name":"Trippy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2517_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1018"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-20T10:26:47-08:00","id":1429179,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Trippy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1428599-v5-vampire-companion?p=1429177#post1429177\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> They were\u2019t playable from the beginning because they were weren\u2019t included in the core of the game. They came out as a supplement. Indeed, the 1st edition of the Player\u2019s Guide did not include them, yet included details on the other independent Clans (Assamites, etc). The Sabbat didn\u2019t actually make any supplement as a Clan write up till second edition. The first 'appearance\u2019 as a reference in the first edition were that of potential boogeyman antagonists.</div> </div> </div> </div>well then, you can't play camirilla either, anarchs only. That was 1e core.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","name":"Taggie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1047"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-20T10:33:39-08:00","id":1429180,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Trippy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1428599-v5-vampire-companion?p=1429152#post1429152\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, there is a Sabbat book coming.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> and given the companion (anarch Tzim..what the hell, why would they ever join the anarchs?, morality system and the Lasombra, give me zero confidence it will have anything to do with the sabbat, as anything but a name.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25011,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","user":"Taggie","date":". 12-20-2020, 01:37 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","name":"Taggie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1047"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-20T10:38:17-08:00","id":1429183,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taggie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1428599-v5-vampire-companion?p=1429179#post1429179\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> well then, you can't play camirilla either, anarchs only. That was 1e core.</div> </div> </div> </div>Er, no. Actually, in 1e it was only Camarilla by default. The anarchs were a rebellious class of vampire within the Camarilla - they weren\u2019t originally a distinct sect. I\u2019m beginning to wonder whether you have read these books....<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> and given the companion (anarch Tzim..what the hell, why would they ever join the anarchs?, morality system and the Lasombra, give me zero confidence it will have anything to do with the sabbat, as anything but a name. </div> </div> </div>....and on that basis, I don\u2019t think anybody needs to lose much sleep about whether any new book meets your approval.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2517,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2517-trippy","user":"Trippy","date":". 12-20-2020, 01:41 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2517-trippy","name":"Trippy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2517_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1018"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-20T10:48:10-08:00","id":1429184,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Trippy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1428599-v5-vampire-companion?p=1429183#post1429183\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Er, no. Actually, in 1e it was only Camarilla by default. The anarchs were a rebellious class of vampire within the Camarilla - they weren\u2019t originally a distinct sect. I\u2019m beginning to wonder whether you have read these books....<br /> <br /> ....and on that basis, I don\u2019t think anybody needs to lose much sleep about whether any new book meets your approval.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> You had to be an anarch in the cam tho, and yes I have read those books.<br /> <br /> No one had to loose sleep over my approval, ever, never claimed they did.<br /> <br /> Just wish they would be honest about the vast retcons going on. Every publication makes it clearer, so just admit it, and move forward, so the expectation that clans will be recognisable at all is gone, and you can explain how the world works, what the big events are, clearly, to give story tellers the world, where they can provide the player agency with that frame work.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25011,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","user":"Taggie","date":". 12-20-2020, 01:51 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","name":"Taggie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1047"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-20T10:57:46-08:00","id":1429185,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taggie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1428599-v5-vampire-companion?p=1429184#post1429184\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> You had to be an anarch in the cam tho, and yes I have read those books.<br /> <br /> No one had to loose sleep over my approval, ever, never claimed they did.<br /> <br /> Just wish they would be honest about the vast retcons going on. Every publication makes it clearer, so just admit it, and move forward, so the expectation that clans will be recognisable at all is gone, and you can explain how the world works, what the big events are, clearly, to give story tellers the world, where they can provide the player agency with that frame work.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not true. You could, as easily, play as Camarilla enforcers, or Caitiff refugees or play in a Camarilla based political game. There are a variety of different campaign suggestions in the core book and only one of them is explicitly about playing an anarch gang.<br /> <br /> I think you need to be honest about your own experience with the history of the game as your comments are showing it up anyway. I still have my 1st Edition books in front of me as I type. You are utterly wrong on several counts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2517,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2517-trippy","user":"Trippy","date":". 12-20-2020, 02:00 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2517-trippy","name":"Trippy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2517_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1018"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-20T11:06:04-08:00","id":1429186,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Trippy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1428599-v5-vampire-companion?p=1429185#post1429185\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Not true. You could, as easily, play as Camarilla enforcers, or Caitiff refugees or play in a Camarilla based political game. There are a variety of different campaign suggestions in the core book and only one of them is explicitly about playing an anarch gang.<br /> <br /> I think you need to be honest about your own experience with the history of the game as your comments are showing it up anyway. I still have my 1st Edition books in front of me as I type. You are utterly wrong on several counts.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I started playing in 1996, the first book I bought for myself, rather than clubbing together to buy the ST was a second hand copy of the Chicago Chronicles (I was 16, and didn't realise what it was, meh) so you can stop lying about when the sabbat appeared, because they are as core as the cam, at least from 2e onwards.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25011,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","user":"Taggie","date":". 12-20-2020, 02:09 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","name":"Taggie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1047"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-20T11:17:31-08:00","id":1429190,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taggie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1428599-v5-vampire-companion?p=1429186#post1429186\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I started playing in 1996, the first book I bought for myself, rather than clubbing together to buy the ST was a second hand copy of the Chicago Chronicles (I was 16, and didn't realise what it was, meh) so you can stop lying about when the sabbat appeared, because they are as core as the cam, at least from 2e onwards.</div> </div> </div> </div>You don\u2019t need to justify your own playing experience to me - its fine - you just need to acknowledge that your own personal experience did not include the origins of the game from 1st edition. The Sabbat, as stated, were detailed as Clans until a 2nd edition supplement - they were merely background antagonists before then. They were never in the core (ie in the core rule books) till Vampire Revised. I know this because I own the books and was there at the time of the original game. Nobody is lying here apart from you to yourself.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2517-trippy","name":"Trippy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2517_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1018"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-20T11:27:21-08:00","id":1429196,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Trippy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1428599-v5-vampire-companion?p=1429190#post1429190\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You don\u2019t need to justify your own playing experience to me - its fine - you just need to acknowledge that your own personal experience did not include the origins of the game from 1st edition. The Sabbat, as stated, were detailed as Clans until a 2nd edition supplement - they were merely background antagonists before then. They were never in the core (ie in the core rule books) till Vampire Revised. I know this because I own the books and was there at the time of the original game. Nobody is lying here apart from you to yourself.</div> </div> </div> </div>Core was: CRB, Players Guides, Storytellers Guides. Then the Clan, setting, etc etc books built the world around that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25011,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","user":"Taggie","date":". 12-20-2020, 02:31 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","name":"Taggie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1047"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-20T11:28:10-08:00","id":1429197,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:#FF0000\">A warning here before things get out of hand. There is no wrong way to play Vampire: The Masquerade.<br /> <br /> High Humanity Louis types mourning their lost humanity.<br /> <br /> Badass Anarchs fighting against Camarilla enforcers for the Revolution.<br /> <br /> Sabbat who raise hell and do sadistic games.<br /> <br /> Thin Bloods drinking nothing but animal blood and stalking high school girls while covered in body glitter.<br /> <br /> All of it is equally valid.<br /> <br /> Respect your fellow posters playstyles.</span><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taggie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1428599-v5-vampire-companion?p=1429196#post1429196\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">again with the lies. I mean come on,</div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">For example, don't say shit like this.<br /> <br /> I say this as someone who wants everyone to feel welcome and accepted here.</span><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-20T11:33:48-08:00","id":1429199,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taggie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1428599-v5-vampire-companion?p=1429196#post1429196\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Core was: CRB, Players Guides, Storytellers Guides. Then the Clan, setting, etc etc books built the world around that.</div> </div> </div> </div>The \u201ccore\u201d is the core rule book. Indeed, in the original Guide to the Sabbat, it is stressed that the ST makes the call as to whether player options included could be used by players or not. They can choose to keep them as antagonists - the core game at that point was still based on Camarilla vampires.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2517-trippy","name":"Trippy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2517_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1018"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-20T11:49:54-08:00","id":1429201,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taggie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1428599-v5-vampire-companion?p=1429175#post1429175\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Am watching now, so will update as I get thru it<br /> <br /> * Anarch Tzimisce making zero sense, and craps on there history</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah so more people that haven't read V20 Anarchs Unbound which already retconned that, making it so that there always were Tzimisce that stayed Anarch. Because when I think of the Tzimisce, I think of a Clan of uniform individuals that will all agree on the same thing and all come together for form their own Sect. Just like how in V5 the Brujah and Gangrel have all gone 100% Anarch.<br /> <br /> ...Oh wait, they haven't. So why should the Tzimisce all be either Sabbat Monsters or Old Clan Fossils?<br /> <br /> Also, how does the Tzimisce write-up crap on their lore? At most I can see people getting upset with the whole dragon and their hoard stuff that ties into their Compulsion and personally I don't see those as anything out of line from established lore. Frankly it gels with the anachronistic side of the Clan that's been there from the beginning.<br /> <br /> Or are you talking about them having Anarch members? Because again, V20 established that just as Rev Ed did that with Lasombra Anarchs.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> *Vozhd being a joke now </div> </div> </div>Can't comment on that as I have yet to be able to play V5 so I don't yet have a real grasp on the rules.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> *Tzimisce bane causing physical damage, and making no sense compared to what it used to be, and what originally caused it. </div> </div> </div>What? It doesn't cause Physical damage, it causes Willpower damage.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The Tzimisce are grounded: Each Tzimisce must choose a specific charge \u2014 a physical domain, a<br /> group of people, an organization, or even something more esoteric \u2014 but clearly defined and limited. The Kindred must spend their daysleep surrounded by their chosen charge. Historically this has often meant slumbering in the soil of their land, but it can also mean being surrounded by that which they tonight rule: a certain kind of people, a building<br /> deeply tied to their obsession, a local counterculture faction, or other, more outlandish elements. If they do not, they sustain aggravated Willpower damage equal to their Bane Severity upon waking the following night. </div> </div> </div>It's the Ravnos Bane that causes physical damage which they connected to the death of [Ravnos].<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> *Amalgams are making things more complicated and difficult to find, not easier. </div> </div> </div>Again, no comment on mechanical stuff.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://youtu.be/_yBS2EZFduI?t=2m13s\" target=\"_blank\">Homo sapiens. What an inventive, invincible species. It's only a few million years since they crawled up out of the mud and learned to walk. Puny, defenceless bipeds. They've survived flood, famine and plague. They've survived cosmic wars and holocausts. And now, here they are, out among the stars, waiting to begin a new life. Ready to outsit eternity. They're indomitable. Indomitable.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/420-akatsukileader13","name":"AkatsukiLeader13","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar420_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1637"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-20T12:05:44-08:00","id":1429204,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AkatsukiLeader13</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1428599-v5-vampire-companion?p=1429201#post1429201\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Ah so more people that haven't read V20 Anarchs Unbound which already retconned that, making it so that there always were Tzimisce that stayed Anarch. Because when I think of the Tzimisce, I think of a Clan of uniform individuals that will all agree on the same thing and all come together for form their own Sect. Just like how in V5 the Brujah and Gangrel have all gone 100% Anarch.</div> </div> </div> </div>You mean all of two paragraphs? What about the rest of the book, none of that never made it into V5?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3953-dwight","name":"Dwight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3953_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-20T12:06:10-08:00","id":1429205,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AkatsukiLeader13</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1428599-v5-vampire-companion?p=1429201#post1429201\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Ah so more people that haven't read V20 Anarchs Unbound which already retconned that, making it so that there always were Tzimisce that stayed Anarch. Because when I think of the Tzimisce, I think of a Clan of uniform individuals that will all agree on the same thing and all come together for form their own Sect. Just like how in V5 the Brujah and Gangrel have all gone 100% Anarch.<br /> <br /> ...Oh wait, they haven't. So why should the Tzimisce all be either Sabbat Monsters or Old Clan Fossils?<br /> <br /> Also, how does the Tzimisce write-up crap on their lore? At most I can see people getting upset with the whole dragon and their hoard stuff that ties into their Compulsion and personally I don't see those as anything out of line from established lore. Frankly it gels with the anachronistic side of the Clan that's been there from the beginning.<br /> <br /> Or are you talking about them having Anarch members? Because again, V20 established that just as Rev Ed did that with Lasombra Anarchs.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Can't comment on that as I have yet to be able to play V5 so I don't yet have a real grasp on the rules.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> What? It doesn't cause Physical damage, it causes Willpower damage.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> It's the Ravnos Bane that causes physical damage which they connected to the death of [Ravnos].<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Again, no comment on mechanical stuff.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Mea Culpea on the bane damage thing, was writing the points as they where raised and missed putting willpower/","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","name":"Taggie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1047"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-20T12:27:08-08:00","id":1429211,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dwight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1428599-v5-vampire-companion?p=1429204#post1429204\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You mean all of two paragraphs? What about the rest of the book, none of that never made it into V5?</div> </div> </div> </div>My point is that modern Anarch Tzimisce were an established thing already. Accusing V5 of somehow breaking the lore by making Anarch Tzimisce a thing is wrong because V20 already retconned that into having been a thing. If you're up in arms about V5 having Anarch Tzimisce, you have to be up in arms about V20 and Anarchs Unbound as well.<br /> <br /> As for V5 and Anarchs Unbound, aside from the Ministry write-up, I haven't yet read V5 Anarchs so I can't comment much about that but I have seen other V5 material reference things in Anarchs Unbound. So I'm gonna doubt that notion of yours until I see evidence to the contrary.<br /> <br /> EDIT: It's also worth noting that they couldn't really do anything with the Tzimisce up til now because they hadn't yet been brought in properly to V5. It was the same thing with the Lasombra who also had Anarchs but couldn't be talked about in V5 Anarchs because the Clan hadn't been added back into V5 yet. And I will admit, that was one of the problems with V5, that they went back to the early nights with just the Cam Seven, Caitiff and Thinbloods available at the start. While I get what they were going for, a return to basics, it was a mistake because we are long past those early days of VtM. We have been long use to the 13 Clans, taking nearly half of them out of the rulebook and taking so long to finally put them back in helped hobble the Edition when it comes to lore and politics.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://youtu.be/_yBS2EZFduI?t=2m13s\" target=\"_blank\">Homo sapiens. What an inventive, invincible species. It's only a few million years since they crawled up out of the mud and learned to walk. Puny, defenceless bipeds. They've survived flood, famine and plague. They've survived cosmic wars and holocausts. And now, here they are, out among the stars, waiting to begin a new life. Ready to outsit eternity. They're indomitable. Indomitable.</a>","edited":{"userid":420,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/420-akatsukileader13","user":"AkatsukiLeader13","date":". 12-20-2020, 03:34 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/420-akatsukileader13","name":"AkatsukiLeader13","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar420_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1637"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-20T12:34:07-08:00","id":1429212,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AkatsukiLeader13</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1428599-v5-vampire-companion?p=1429211#post1429211\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> My point is that modern Anarch Tzimisce were an established thing already. Accusing V5 of somehow breaking the lore by making Anarch Tzimisce a thing is wrong because V20 already retconned that into having been a thing. If you're up in arms about V5 having Anarch Tzimisce, you have to be up in arms about V20 and Anarchs Unbound as well.<br /> <br /> As for V5 and Anarchs Unbound, aside from the Ministry write-up, I haven't yet read V5 Anarchs so I can't comment much about that but I have seen other V5 material reference things in Anarchs Unbound. So I'm gonna doubt that notion of yours until I see evidence to the contrary.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sounds like you need to do some research (i.e read some books) because it's not my job to prove anything to you that you can easily find on your own time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3953-dwight","name":"Dwight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3953_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-20T13:02:27-08:00","id":1429220,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dwight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1428599-v5-vampire-companion?p=1429212#post1429212\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Sounds like you need to do some research (i.e read some books) because it's not my job to prove anything to you that you can easily find on your own time.</div> </div> </div> </div>You're the one that claimed that the rest of the material from Anarchs Unbound didn't make it into V5. I merely replied that while I hadn't read nor remember anything that contradicts Anarchs Unbound, that wouldn't have me assuming that V20AU is somehow non-canon to V5.<br /> <br /> Also, my point wasn't that V5 was using V20AU but that Anarch Tzimisce had already been established as a thing. Nor have they presented anything to indicate that this is sudden change in the Clan like with the V5 Lasombra. There are Tzimisce Anarchs because there already were Tzimisce Anarchs as established in V20AU. And it's not like they even put an overemphasis on the Anarchs over the Sabbat members in the write-up which would be understandable given the current non-playable state of the Sabbat in V5.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://youtu.be/_yBS2EZFduI?t=2m13s\" target=\"_blank\">Homo sapiens. What an inventive, invincible species. It's only a few million years since they crawled up out of the mud and learned to walk. Puny, defenceless bipeds. They've survived flood, famine and plague. They've survived cosmic wars and holocausts. And now, here they are, out among the stars, waiting to begin a new life. Ready to outsit eternity. They're indomitable. Indomitable.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/420-akatsukileader13","name":"AkatsukiLeader13","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar420_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1637"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-20T13:18:57-08:00","id":1429224,"title":"","content":"You sure are making a mountain out of two cherry picked paragraphs from a book that's been widely disregarded in V5, if you read the v5 anarch book you would know this.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3953-dwight","name":"Dwight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3953_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-20T13:19:51-08:00","id":1429225,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AkatsukiLeader13</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1428599-v5-vampire-companion?p=1429160#post1429160\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's nearly two hours long. Do you have a summary?</div> </div> </div> </div>This one is shorter, although I do not know if it'd merit Dwight's endorsement (that's not sarcasm just to be clear)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=GuuXuhU08wA\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=GuuXuhU08wA\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=GuuXuhU08wA\" target=\"_blank\"> https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=GuuXuhU08wA </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-20T13:29:48-08:00","id":1429226,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chris24601</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1428599-v5-vampire-companion?p=1429134#post1429134\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would. Because it IS a new game in the same way that D&amp;D 5e is a new game compared to 4E, 3e and AD&amp;D. The mechanics ARE different. That's inarguable.<br /> <br /> What is supposed to be the same between editions of VtM is the SETTING and the new additions of late seem to be getting it more back onto that course. I may not like all the metaplot-y bits (the changes to the Ravnos bane basically make V5 impossible to convert to until the current chronicle is well and truly ended), but at least they're a bit more recognizable now.<br /> <br /> As this relates the Sabbat; it means there's still a bit of work to do... alternate mechanical options from the Humanity/Touchstone system primarily... before the Sabbat can be properly played as Taggie would like in V5. By the same token, they'd need to do some work on presenting some of the original clan banes before V5 would be very useful in presenting a historical campaign (ex. the new Ravnos bane specifically mentions it becoming such with the Antediluvian's death... so it shouldn't apply in the 1980's or 1780's).<br /> <br /> Those are only flaws in the system if no upcoming work (ex. the Sabbat book) is used to add those elements to the system. Until then we can just say the new system is incomplete.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, all of this. Character sheets still have the dots and I do love dots. But the rules are different. They still use D10s and the same basic mechanics, but hunger dice? Rousing the blood? The new Disciplines? Each clan getting a makeover? The addition of clan compulsions? <i>Post-</i>Gehenna setting? The whole &quot;blankbody&quot; thing? The Second Inquisition? Setting's been updated a ton and rules are largely different. It's Vampire, but it's not the same game as V20, and in a lot of ways, that's actually good. And I love all of the previous editions and would play any of them in a heartbeat.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1428599-v5-vampire-companion?p=1429147#post1429147\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Didn't the Tzmisce and Lasombra come in with <i><u>The Players Guide</u> to the Sabbat. ? </i><br /> <br /> Does V5 really have a sabbat book coming, in any recognizable form? If they say Sabbat but we get... Anarchs but Chaotic Evil or Baali but not really inferalist... is that really &quot;The Sabbat&quot;? With everyone in the middle east, what are we even dealing with? Remnants? Something entirely different? Vampires in an active armed conflict set in a place the majority of our pasty-faced players aren't familiar with and aren't likely to do justice? We gonna have some Morytania style city where vampires rule openly? I'd like to believe in a reconquista, but based off of current trends, it's doubtful they'd do something so... damage control based.</div> </div> </div> </div>The upcoming Sabbat book is mentioned in this video, I believe:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=T-C1bj0rZPM\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=T-C1bj0rZPM\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=T-C1bj0rZPM\" target=\"_blank\"> https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=T-C1bj0rZPM </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> There might be more information in the interview with Justin:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=ukzSdu1q54E\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=ukzSdu1q54E\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=ukzSdu1q54E\" target=\"_blank\"> https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=ukzSdu1q54E </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> So it's clear there will be a Sabbat book. What that book will entail, I do not know. I do think it's in good hands at this point.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-20T13:31:47-08:00","id":1429227,"title":"","content":"And I apologize for my depraved with no consequences comment. My intended point was that it's fine to play any way you want, and even under the current Humanity system you can get that with the right convictions and tenets, but it <i>was</i> inflammatory.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-20T13:49:12-08:00","id":1429229,"title":"","content":"-Young Tzmisce among the Anarchs makes sense, moreso when whole cities are anarchs and the Cam are a distant minority without local power. Truly though, most Tzmisce should be Autarks<br /> -Tzmisce in the Cam is HERESY<br /> -The story of the Lasombra joining the Cam in V5 is very stupid and as a modestly intelligent clan they'd be a million times better off joining the Anarchs. However, if Lasombra joined the Cam in an organic, sensible way, it'd work and I'd be all for it; the method described in V5 is severe idiot ball. <br /> -Salubri warriors should be THE salubri and healers should be bygones and oddities.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-20T13:53:00-08:00","id":1429230,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_