the more the answer becomes a no-brainer, and while Lasombra aren't renowned for their mental primaries (no Auspex bro) they've got &quot;standards&quot; and don't like idiots dragging their clan 'brand' down. So Toadying up with the Cam is a lose-lose-lose. Yeah the Sabbat's a sinking ship, but you don't leave one sinking ship for an equaly-sinking ship. As much as I loath the concept, the Anarchs are clearly the future for the defecting Lasombra if we pretend they have brains.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-23T09:30:06-08:00","id":1429634,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1428599-v5-vampire-companion?p=1429632#post1429632\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Nah, serious answers only; Why would the Lasombra go through all that camarilla bullshit and testing when they could just... join/conquer the anarchs? Remember that in V5 the Camarilla aren't a dominant sect so Lasombra have plenty of options. The Anarchs provide both an easier transition and more opportunities, they're on the up, and the camarilla is on the down.<br /> <br /> It's like asking 'do you want to invest in Netflix or blockbuster' 'do you wanna buy a robust and reliable Japanese/European bike or do you wanna splurge on a Harley Davidson that costs an arm and a leg and doesn't run half as well but has maybe subjective value in the brand...' Like, the more you know about any of this stuff, the more the answer becomes a no-brainer, and while Lasombra aren't renowned for their mental primaries (no Auspex bro) they've got &quot;standards&quot; and don't like idiots dragging their clan 'brand' down. So Toadying up with the Cam is a lose-lose-lose. Yeah the Sabbat's a sinking ship, but you don't leave one sinking ship for an equaly-sinking ship. As much as I loath the concept, the Anarchs are clearly the future for the defecting Lasombra if we pretend they have brains.</div> </div> </div> </div>Then play it your own way and perhaps, start asking serious questions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2517-trippy","name":"Trippy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2517_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1018"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-23T09:30:49-08:00","id":1429635,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1428599-v5-vampire-companion?p=1429632#post1429632\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Nah, serious answers only; Why would the Lasombra go through all that camarilla bullshit and testing when they could just... join/conquer the anarchs? Remember that in V5 the Camarilla aren't a dominant sect so Lasombra have plenty of options. The Anarchs provide both an easier transition and more opportunities, they're on the up, and the camarilla is on the down.</div> </div> </div> </div>1. Because the Anarchs cannot be controlled. If the Lasombra joined they'd be in the exact situation they would be in the Sabbat where the lesson is, &quot;We actually can't rule this unruly band of degenerates.&quot;<br /> 2. The Camarilla is already returning to its prominence with the Banu Haqim replacing the Gangrel. With the Lasombra, they're back to full strength.<br /> 3. Marcus Vitel is the only one who actually is able to rule the East Coast anarchs and he's a Methuselah.<br /> <br /> I suppose it depends on the idea whether you think the Anarchs are sincere about their desire for freedom and capable of standing up against Elders like the Lasombra. If they are, it makes sense. If you don't think it, you may wonder why they're not being led around like children.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It's like asking 'do you want to invest in Netflix or blockbuster' 'do you wanna buy a robust and reliable Japanese/European bike or do you wanna splurge on a Harley Davidson that costs an arm and a leg and doesn't run half as well but has maybe subjective value in the brand...' Like, the more you know about any of this stuff, the more the answer becomes a no-brainer, and while Lasombra aren't renowned for their mental primaries (no Auspex bro) they've got &quot;standards&quot; and don't like idiots dragging their clan 'brand' down. So Toadying up with the Cam is a lose-lose-lose. Yeah the Sabbat's a sinking ship, but you don't leave one sinking ship for an equaly-sinking ship. As much as I loath the concept, the Anarchs are clearly the future for the defecting Lasombra if we pretend they have brains. </div> </div> </div>Uh, they actually say in CBN this is WHY they joined the Camarilla.<br /> <br /> &quot;Why join the Camarilla?&quot;<br /> <br /> The Lasombra think the Anarchs would be low-selling themselves versus the actual classy movers and shakers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-23T10:03:36-08:00","id":1429638,"title":"","content":"I pegged the lasombra mostly as pragmatists, honestly. Yeah, the Camarilla has an impressive brand, but it's a train wreck, A total train wreck in V5. Kinda like Harley Davidson; super famous even to people who don't like bikes, but actually a garbage company that reports nothing but losses.<br /> <br /> I'm not questioning that some Lasombra would want to join the cam. After all, HD still sells a few bikes to dentists upon the mid-life crisis, but the majority of Lasombra should clearly favour the ship that isn't sinking, the Anarchs. They don't even have to call themselves anarchs. They just have to establish their own factions within the anarchs, bringing with them some of the former sabbat that were in their packs; it makes <i>more </i>sense given that they can take their pack with them to join the Anarchs, rather than abandon their pack to join the Cam. Since anarchs are a disorganized mess, it should be very easy for any Lasombra worth their blood to claim turf. Their Tzmisce friends can come with them, their Salubri friends can come with them, their ravnos friends can come with them. I don't think I can fully articulate how perfect the Anarch opportunity is for the Lasombra, and how utterly raw the Camarilla deal is. The Lasombra aren't meant to be masochists, but sadists (because they got potence rather than fortitude; true story. All clans with fortitude are masochists. Just try and refute this. It's just facts.) and so becoming the Camarilla whipping boy is a million times less sexy than going to anarch town and putting the boot to a few faces.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-23T10:10:51-08:00","id":1429639,"title":"","content":"Really? You think the Camarilla is sinking.<br /> <br /> They drove out the Anarchs from their ranks and now have two incredibly powerful new clans to replace the Old. They also have taken a lot of old Sabbat territory.<br /> <br /> Yes, Second Inquisition is bad and so is the Beckoning but the Ancilla are there to fill the gaps of the missing Elders.<br /> <br /> Just my thoughts.<br /> <br /> I'm interested in hearing your thoughts.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-23T10:33:08-08:00","id":1429642,"title":"","content":"I see the reason the reason the lasombra joining the camarilla is pretty obvious. The anarchs don't stand a long term chance. The anarchs are fodder for the second inquisition and one hundred years from now will probably be in worse shape than now. The camarilla is a powerful long term institution. Join the winning side, Not the losing side.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3901-radiofreedeath","name":"RadioFreeDeath","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-23T11:23:57-08:00","id":1429645,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1428599-v5-vampire-companion?p=1429639#post1429639\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> They drove out the Anarchs from their ranks and now have two incredibly powerful new clans to replace the Old. They also have taken a lot of old Sabbat territory.<br /> .</div> </div> </div> </div>Lasombra defects are not equal to the brujah, and losing the brujah is an absolutely brutal blow (also it's completely out of character but I digress) <br /> Similarly, Assamite Schismatics aren't really all that much when you think about it. Most of them are Toreador-lite. They left the Loyalists because half of them are potentially destabilizing religious nuts and the other half are conflict adverse. The Schismatics are significantly weaker than the loyalists. <br /> <br /> The SI is probably the Camarilla's work, really. <br /> But with the elders gone the Camarilla has been weekened. Sure, the rulership might become a little more reasonable, but it's lost it's muscle. I guess in V5 not having elders is an advantage (because they're hungry messes after potency 5) but... <br /> <br /> Monopoly is a powerful thing, and the Cam gave it up. It would've been easier to fix the fleet, rather than give all the damaged ships to the enemy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-23T12:05:03-08:00","id":1429651,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1428599-v5-vampire-companion?p=1429645#post1429645\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Lasombra defects are not equal to the brujah, and losing the brujah is an absolutely brutal blow (also it's completely out of character but I digress)<br /> Similarly, Assamite Schismatics aren't really all that much when you think about it. Most of them are Toreador-lite. They left the Loyalists because half of them are potentially destabilizing religious nuts and the other half are conflict adverse. The Schismatics are significantly weaker than the loyalists.<br /> <br /> The SI is probably the Camarilla's work, really.<br /> But with the elders gone the Camarilla has been weekened. Sure, the rulership might become a little more reasonable, but it's lost it's muscle. I guess in V5 not having elders is an advantage (because they're hungry messes after potency 5) but...<br /> <br /> Monopoly is a powerful thing, and the Cam gave it up. It would've been easier to fix the fleet, rather than give all the damaged ships to the enemy.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well the Brujah are disloyal and were the biggest threat to the Camarilla within the Camarilla.<br /> <br /> You also forgot the Sorcerer Caste of the Assamites who defected en masse.<br /> <br /> So the Lasombra are much better to recruit than the Brujah, especially since they trashed the Sabbat ob their way out.<br /> <br /> And the Schismatics are 1/3rd of the Assamites according to Assamite Revised, with another 1/3rd defecting to the Sabbat.<br /> <br /> This is just my opinion, though.<br /> <br /> You could disagree.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-23T13:15:38-08:00","id":1429658,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1428599-v5-vampire-companion?p=1429645#post1429645\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">also it's completely out of character but I digress</div> </div> </div> </div>You think it's out of character for a clan defined by challenging social conventions and refusing to unthinkingly accept authority to back out of the singular vampire government which does things the way it does because this is how they've always been done? Really?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25972-illithidactivity","name":"IllithidActivity","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25972_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"103"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-23T13:39:04-08:00","id":1429662,"title":"","content":"I disagree with MWIS on a lot of things, but I'm in general more sympathetic to his views here than others.<br /> <br /> One thing I'm not seeing discussed (though I could easily miss it by mostly skimming over 25 pages of thread and reading only some in detail) is the issue of the Vinculum. How exactly can all these Sabbat vampires betray their fellow sect members by joining the enemy? Even low levels of the Vinculum would seem to prevent that.<br /> <br /> Furthermore, how is it going to affect the Camarilla when huge members of the enemy sect arrive inside, and they have the ability to break any blood bond currently in existence in the Camarilla (and which would also install a low level blood bond to these &quot;ex-Sabbat&quot; members - who of course still have Vinculum with all the other members of the Sabbat)? There aren't any objections to this? Wouldn't this destroy the sect long term? Do all these Lasombra just make a pinky-swear that they'd never do such a thing?<br /> <br /> To me, this is a pretty insurmountable obstacle to this scenario. Unless there is a way to destroy the Vinculum and prevent the Vaulderie from working, I can't accept it even on a theoretical basis.<br /> <br /> Besides that, there is another issue. There's some level of logic to the people who support this scenario, but ultimately it's the same kind of logic that Hitler had when he thought he could split the Western Allies and the Soviet Union and make separate peaces with them in 1944/1945, or that Himmler and Goering had that they could negotiate a beneficial surrender with Eisenhower because he'd just jump at getting all those SS and Wehrmacht units at his command so he could fight that inevitable war with the Soviet Union. Or if you don't want WWII analogies, then Napoleon leaving Elba in the 100 Days but offering peace with his former enemies so they'd just accept him coming back into power. All of this had a certain kind of logic and evidence to support it too - except that nobody else was ever going to stand for it. These were just desperate gambles with no chance of success.<br /> <br /> In history, you do sometimes have cases where the world suddenly changes. Hitler and Stalin make a pact. France and Austria can become allies in the Diplomatic Revolution of 1756. But these kind of reversals tend to be short lived, collapse into acrimony, and the age old rivalries resume. When real reversals are made, it generally takes a long time and reflects long term trends changing the nature of international politics.<br /> <br /> In Professional Wrestling, you can do these kind of things. You can have Hitler or Himmler &quot;turn&quot; and all that matters is whether the audience at the moment think its &quot;cool&quot;. You can bring back the Napoleon &quot;character&quot; out of retirement because the audience kept demanding it. In the real world these kind of things are much harder to pull off. To me, much of the V5 scenarios are at the level of a Professional Wrestling story. If you like those kind of things, this is awesome and everyone else should shut up about how Hulk Hogan would never join the NWO. That Hogan turned heel in this stunt is so much fun so who cares. If you like a more serious setting, you're left with your mouth gaped open wondering why Wellington and Napoleon have teamed up to fight Andrew Jackson and a six-year old Abraham Lincoln. They'd be doomed except that the Japanese Shogun is sending his samurai army to New Orleans right now - if they can reach there in time! That this would never happen destroys any enjoyment for you.<br /> <br /> I'm sure there are scenarios where I could accept a large scale defection of Sabbat Lasombra to the Camarilla. But the way this was done is not one of them. If I was asked to write such a scenario that I'd be happy with, I could probably do so with enough time. But there would still be just as many complaints as there is now that it still doesn't make sense <i>to them</i>. Everyone is going to have their own take on the setting and their own tastes to the style of play at their table.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-23T13:54:45-08:00","id":1429668,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampir