oleon leaving Elba in the 100 Days but offering peace with his former enemies so they'd just accept him coming back into power. All of this had a certain kind of logic and evidence to support it too - except that nobody else was ever going to stand for it. These were just desperate gambles with no chance of success.<br /> <br /> In history, you do sometimes have cases where the world suddenly changes. Hitler and Stalin make a pact. France and Austria can become allies in the Diplomatic Revolution of 1756. But these kind of reversals tend to be short lived, collapse into acrimony, and the age old rivalries resume. When real reversals are made, it generally takes a long time and reflects long term trends changing the nature of international politics.<br /> <br /> In Professional Wrestling, you can do these kind of things. You can have Hitler or Himmler &quot;turn&quot; and all that matters is whether the audience at the moment think its &quot;cool&quot;. You can bring back the Napoleon &quot;character&quot; out of retirement because the audience kept demanding it. In the real world these kind of things are much harder to pull off. To me, much of the V5 scenarios are at the level of a Professional Wrestling story. If you like those kind of things, this is awesome and everyone else should shut up about how Hulk Hogan would never join the NWO. That Hogan turned heel in this stunt is so much fun so who cares. If you like a more serious setting, you're left with your mouth gaped open wondering why Wellington and Napoleon have teamed up to fight Andrew Jackson and a six-year old Abraham Lincoln. They'd be doomed except that the Japanese Shogun is sending his samurai army to New Orleans right now - if they can reach there in time! That this would never happen destroys any enjoyment for you.<br /> <br /> I'm sure there are scenarios where I could accept a large scale defection of Sabbat Lasombra to the Camarilla. But the way this was done is not one of them. If I was asked to write such a scenario that I'd be happy with, I could probably do so with enough time. But there would still be just as many complaints as there is now that it still doesn't make sense <i>to them</i>. Everyone is going to have their own take on the setting and their own tastes to the style of play at their table.</div> </div> </div> </div>While I disagree with most of V5's changes, history shows us things can change very quickly. Alexander the great's conquest of Persia, the Anglo-Saxon invasion of England, the Norman conquest, the founding of the modern state of Israel, the revolutions in Egypt and Iran, The Soviet and Maoist revolutions, the internet, the American Revolution, the American Civil War (massive changes to the Southern States), the end of segregation in the Southern states, the Mongol conquests, etc etc. Also Napolean did come out of retirement, although it didn't do him or France a lot of good.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14519-drhappyangry","name":"DrHappyAngry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14519_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"233"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-23T14:33:03-08:00","id":1429670,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1428599-v5-vampire-companion?p=1429651#post1429651\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well the Brujah are disloyal and were the biggest threat to the Camarilla within the Camarilla.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Brujah would never let one person speak for all of them. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> You also forgot the Sorcerer Caste of the Assamites who defected en masse. </div> </div> </div>I did not, cannot, and would not. I wrote a whole book on Quietus to boot. :P<br /> The Assamite sorcerers have consistently been written as by far the absolute smallest caste. The warriors dwarf the Viziers, and the Viziers Dwarf the Sorcerers. As for the Shism, they were split 50-50. <br /> Furthermore, Assamite sorcerers have consistently failed to match up to the Tremere. The Tremere's entire organization is centred around making mages. The Assamites just happen to have mages. Tremere magic is regimented and structured, Assamites have a very loose collection of systems that lead to internal conflict. Tremere magic allows initiates from any faith, Assamite magic is heretical in most religions and much of the schismatics are such because religion and... yeah. You read up on Sihr? That's terrible stuff. There's a reason why, although the Assamite magic is thousands of years older, the Tremere have a lot more abilities... <br /> All the Assamite sorcerers do is weaken the Tremere monopoly ever so slightly. There's not even enough of them to spread to all the cities the schismatics have joined. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> So the Lasombra are much better to recruit than the Brujah, especially since they trashed the Sabbat ob their way out.<br /> . </div> </div> </div>The Brujah were plentiful and mostly pretty simple. The Lasombra are few and complicated.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-23T14:42:15-08:00","id":1429673,"title":"","content":"I kinda hope there is a big ole retcon in the sabbat book. Lasombra leaving? Chaff who couldn't hack it. Tizimice anarchs? Lost lambs who will figure it one day. Everyone else? Anties still here, everything else is lies.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3953-dwight","name":"Dwight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3953_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-23T14:53:08-08:00","id":1429675,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrHappyAngry</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1428599-v5-vampire-companion?p=1429668#post1429668\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">While I disagree with most of V5's changes, history shows us things can change very quickly.</div> </div> </div> </div>I wasn't talking about armed conquests, but sudden reversals in diplomatic stances.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrHappyAngry</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1428599-v5-vampire-companion?p=1429668#post1429668\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also Napolean did come out of retirement, although it didn't do him or France a lot of good.</div> </div> </div> </div>I actually mentioned that. My comment about the 100 Days, and that he tried to come back and failed was exactly my point.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-23T15:08:49-08:00","id":1429679,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dwight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1428599-v5-vampire-companion?p=1429673#post1429673\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I kinda hope there is a big ole retcon in the sabbat book. Lasombra leaving? Chaff who couldn't hack it. Tizimice anarchs? Lost lambs who will figure it one day. Everyone else? Anties still here, everything else is lies.</div> </div> </div> </div>That would make the Sabbat look pretty terrible to get utterly gutted by the Lasombra chafe. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> But yes, I want the Lasombra to still be with the Sabbat. I just want them to be playable with the Camarilla nad have the best enemies possible: themselves.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-23T15:55:06-08:00","id":1429687,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1428599-v5-vampire-companion?p=1429501#post1429501\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The thing about the Anarchs, Taggie, is that you can play them anyway you want, though. If you hate the way the guy who offended you played them (and he sounds like a real jerk), you can remake them pretty much however you wish.<br /> <br /> Because its up to each ST to interpret the Clans as they wish for their games.<br /> <br /> Everything is broad strokes.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't like them as a theme, at all, nothing published about them ever makes them sound interesting. If I remade them, we have that, it is the Sabbat.<br /> <br /> The guys plural who broke Anarchs for me took it from, I don't want to play one to I don't want to be in the same game as one.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","name":"Taggie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1047"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-23T15:57:52-08:00","id":1429688,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1428599-v5-vampire-companion?p=1429675#post1429675\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I wasn't talking about armed conquests, but sudden reversals in diplomatic stances.<br /> <br /> <br /> I actually mentioned that. My comment about the 100 Days, and that he tried to come back and failed was exactly my point.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sorry missed the last part, that's what I get for trying to read the forum in between working.<br /> <br /> You can't entirely separate the two since they're two sides of the same coin, but I can give some examples of diplomatic shifts with long term consequences. From the top of my head, the formation of the modern state of Israel, the Syracusians switching to backing the Carthaginians, the Persians switching between backing the Pelopennesian League and the Delian League, Nixon going to China, Ben Franklin's trips to France for support, NAFTA, the formation of the European Union and the Catholic church arbitrating the dispute over the new world (and Africa and Asia) between Spain and Portugal. War, or the possibility of war, is tied up in a lot of these, but that's because you cannot separate it from diplomacy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14519-drhappyangry","name":"DrHappyAngry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14519_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"233"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-24T00:05:00-08:00","id":1429721,"title":"","content":"Tzmisce anarchs are totally fine. I don't get why people don't like them. All those weird thematic ideas you have keeping them out of the anarchs are for elders, and Tzmisce aren't a clan entirely made up of elders.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-24T00:42:26-08:00","id":1429723,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1428599-v5-vampire-companion?p=1429651#post1429651\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well the Brujah are disloyal and were the biggest threat to the Camarilla within the Camarilla.<br /> <br /> You also forgot the Sorcerer Caste of the Assamites who defected en masse.<br /> <br /> So the Lasombra are much better to recruit than the Brujah, especially since they trashed the Sabbat ob their way out.<br /> <br /> And the Schismatics are 1/3rd of the Assamites according to Assamite Revised, with another 1/3rd defecting to the Sabbat.<br /> <br /> This is just my opinion, though.<br /> <br /> You could disagree.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> All Banu Haqim are sorcerer caste now. Their disciplines dictate that it's a matter of education not Blood Line as to whether you have rituals or not.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1428599-v5-vampire-companion?p=1429721#post1429721\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Tzmisce anarchs are totally fine. I don't get why people don't like them. All those weird thematic ideas you have keeping them out of the anarchs are for elders, and Tzmisce aren't a clan entirely made up of elders.</div> </div> </div> </div>Given how picky they used to be about the embrace, those ideas where for neonates.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","name":"Taggie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1047"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-24T03:06:05-08:00","id":1429732,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taggie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1428599-v5-vampire-companion?p=1429723#post1429723\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Given how picky they used to be about the embrace, those ideas where for neonates.</div> </div> </div> </div>My Sabbat Players Guide said the Tzimisce would grab well-dressed people to be Shovelheads. It was the Tremere Antitribu who never did War Parties.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-24T04:55:19-08:00","id":1429734,"title":"","content":"The thing about shovelheads is that they're not true sabbat and only the worthy will survive so you can make as many mistakes as you like so long as you can kill em all afterwards. The only clan that should really hold off on them is the Nosferatu... I don't think I need to explain that one.<br /> <br /> Anyhow, Tzmisce for me are definetly Big-Brain people. I mean literally they should use fleshcrafting to expand their heads. but in seriousness Vicissitude needs a medical degree's worth of knowledge to pull off. It's the only Discipline outside of the sorceries that routinely needs a knowledge rather than a talent or skill. (ok, like, I guess older versions might have had bodycrafts as a skill? but yeah, definetly more on the right-hand side of the paper) Anyone that's gonna be a Tzmisce is gonna be well educated. They're going to need money to fund their 'research', and they're going to need space to keep their 'research material' isolated from the rest of the world. Also they're gonna want a swarm of dogs because dogs are great and for so many dogs you're either going to need private land or you need to corrupt officials so that nobody takes away the local strays.<br /> <br /> What I'm trying to get at, is that I think Tzmisce lend themselves naturally to the demographics that generally hold conservative policital opinions. and thus even among neonates its strange to find many who would actively support anarch ideals. That said, I can certainly imagine many younger Tzmisce using the Anarchs for their own gains (let's face it, not many anarchs really hold to anarch ideals beyond -I want to be the boot, not the face-) Thus while i think the majority of Tzmisce would wince at the prospect of being labeled an anarch, many would be very happy offering their services to anarchs in exchange for space and security. Maybe they might even push the anarchs into becoming a camarilla that suits them.<br /> <br /> On the opposite end of the spectrum, Tzmisce might embrace tattoo artists and people in the body mod scene.<br /> Junk yard folk and gangsters make good Tzmisce, though honestly a lot of such people generally have &quot;conservative&quot; opinions even if they're poor. I imagine these people make a sizable minority and could support the anarchs.<br /> As for Trans people... I imagine Tzmisce are more apathetic than we'd like to imagine. Oh, certainly, they'll take your money and transform you, and they might make a show of being your ally if it suits them and brings them more demand, But Tzmisce are people who've skinned thousands of kittens for research purposes, they're not going to embrace someone out of charity, and someone who might just get charitable is a risk the Tzmisce don't want to take. A Tzmisce might be sympathetic, and they're definitely going to be up there in terms of having trans-people of the blood, but they're not going to embrace champions, and champions are the types that flock to the anarchs. Trans people are going to support the Tzmisce to achieve their goals, and Tzmisce are going to support trans people because... they're a great market.<br /> <br /> Essentially, the Tzmisce:<br /> -likes working with anarchs<br /> -Doesn't want to be called an anarch.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-24T06:37:54-08:00","id":1429739,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1428599-v5-vampire-companion?p=1429734#post1429734\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> What I'm trying to get at, is that I think Tzmisce lend themselves naturally to the demographics that generally hold conservative policital opinions.</div> </div> </div> </div>maybe, but those ideas don't last long in the sabbat<br /> <br /> you're more likely to find a tzimisce holding human conservative values in the anarchs than in the sabbat","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>-</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10998-pleiades","name":"Pleiades","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10998_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1844"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-24T07:08:16-08:00","id":1429743,"title":"","content":"Human conservative values have their parallels in vampire conservative values. <br /> Religion-Vampire religion<br /> Racism-Clanism/generation<br /> Body is god-given and shouldn't be changed- Immortal body should be unchanging and Vicissitude is bad<br /> Hierarchy is important- Hierarchy is important <br /> Charity over welfare- same thing<br /> <br /> <br /> It's not just values, it's a mindset. I could go on forever with examples. <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-24T12:41:10-08:00","id":1429771,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrHappyAngry</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1428599-v5-vampire-companion?p=1429688#post1429688\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sorry missed the last part, that's what I get for trying to read the forum in between working.<br /> <br /> You can't entirely separate the two since they're two sides of the same coin, but I can give some examples of diplomatic shifts with long term consequences. From the top of my head, the formation of the modern state of Israel, the Syracusians switching to backing the Carthaginians, the Persians switching between backing the Pelopennesian League and the Delian League, Nixon going to China, Ben Franklin's trips to France for support, NAFTA, the formation of the European Union and the Catholic church arbitrating the dispute over the new world (and Africa and Asia) between Spain and Portugal. War, or the possibility of war, is tied up in a lot of these, but that's because you cannot separate it from diplomacy.</div> </div> </div> </div>I am talking about sudden diplomatic reversals that aren't just tactical in nature and last for a long time. Thanks for your reply, but I don't think your examples qualify unfortunately.<ul><li>Not sure what you mean about the establishment of Israel. There were lots of things against its establishment, but the creation of Israel was a process that took decades and WWII to set the conditions for it. If the Arabs of 1947 decided a Jewish state was great, recognized its borders, and established normal relations with it - then it'd be a sudden reversal.</li> <li>Syracuse was a heavily divided city. It's not surprising that it would support one side versus the other depending on what temporary event put one faction in charge instead of another. An example of what you would want would be if Rome decided Hannibal was its best friend.</li> <li>Persia was the enemy of Greece. It used divide and conquer and tactics. It supported one over the other simply based on what would weaken the Greeks. What you actually want is something like Alexander the Great deciding to be best friends with the Persian Empire and not invading it.</li> <li>Nixon going to China was an expedient move to split the Communist Bloc. Mao all of a sudden didn't end the Cultural Revolution and support everything the US did in foreign policy, and Nixon didn't give the go ahead for China to invade Taiwan. Relations were often strained, and there was no formal alliance between them. These were limited tactical moves at a time when both sides saw the Soviet Union as their main threat, not a rapprochement similar to the century long politics that saw the UK becoming allies with France and the US by the early 20th century. This was simply the start of a process that might have seen Chinese and US become good friends and full allies by now - but we'd likely need some alternate history around 1989 and after.</li> <li>French support for the US also not surprising since both were enemies of the UK at the time, and of course an ongoing anti-French bias in the US as a result of them being culturally English meant the US immediately counterbalanced its French ties by being extremely favorable to Britain after the war. The US even abrogated its alliance with France as a result of the Jacobins killing Louis XIV.</li> <li>NAFTA doesn't represent any sudden reversal at all. US and Mexico were never enemies except when territorial dispute of the old Texas border lead it to war; Mexican insecurity at US dominance not withstanding. Closer economic ties in the form of an FTA is simply something that was part of normal politics of the time depending on domestic and international politics.</li> <li>The formation of the EU took place several decades after the first Treaty of Rome which in turn was over a decade after the end of WWII. It was a gradual rapprochement between France and Germany as a result of both of them being big losers of the war and needing a forum by which both can regain their power. In Germany's case, it was also an essential diplomatic move given that their country was divided between two hostile blocs, occupied, and they accepted they had lost two great wars in a bid to overcome the Western powers and weren't going to have a third shot. If the French Third Republic embraced Wilhelmine Germany after 1871 and decided to become allies, then you'd have that scenario.</li> <li>The Pope acting as mediator between Catholic countries is normal and routine. Neither Portugal or Span were hateful enemies of each other.</li> </ul>You are right that one can't separate war from diplomacy. But you're still misunderstanding my point. Sorry if it hasn't been clear.<br /> <br /> With the possible exception of France and Germany in the EU - which I've already explained required complete ruin and defeat in war and took decades to achieve - none of your examples deal with hated rivals suddenly (and without long preparation time and changes) becoming allies and being permanent.<br /> <br /> You can get temporary alliances based on immediate needs that resort to the status quo ante, but that is not the same. You might also get one side decisively beating the other in war, and one is forced to abide by the decisions of the other. But that's not the same either.<br /> <br /> Something like the Sabbat Lasombra joining the Camarilla en masse would be like Rome becoming friendly with Hannibal, Alexander the Great choosing not to invade Persia but become friends, France teaming up with the Habsburgs; or the Pope joining forces with the Ottomans.<br /> <br /> When we do see things like two bitter, historical enemies joining forces and that works out long term, we see the change happen over a long time and long term trends explain why these states now have common interests instead of being rivals. It's not sudden. It takes place over time so attitudes change as common interests converge.<br /> <br /> In order to see something like huge numbers of Sabbat Lasombra abandon their sect and join the Camarilla (even handwaving the Vinculum issues - which we shouldn't do), we'd have to see that there was a huge division within the Sabbat Lasombra occurring over a long time so that such a betrayal makes sense because it completely destroys Lasombra prestige, clan pride, brood loyalty, etc. We'd need to see the reasons for such a cultural revolution. We don't because this is something new invented for this edition of the game, and it doesn't have the proper support in the setting history.<br /> <br /> Maybe if the old Lasombra clanbooks had gone into detail about how the clan was bitterly divided between Lasombra holding to the old anarch ideals, and Lasombra who joined the sect afterwards merely to advance power, and that these two groups - old foes from the Anarch Revolt - were in constant turmoil despite being in the sect, then we'd have something like that. And maybe we're also told how some Lasombra AT were still in contact with one of these factions (or a part of them) and could act as a means of assisting such a betrayal. Then we could see how one faction decided to bolt (though here too, we'd need to address the Vinculum) and be successful given a sufficient pretext or proximate cause. But the old books never gave us that. The Sabbat Lasombra appeared unified without severe tension between its members, and always tried to kill their antitribu. We're not given any previous conditions that would justify it - hence a comparison to a Professional Wrestling story instead.<br /> <br /> On the other hand, let's look at an alternate scenario - the Followers of Set join the Camarilla. This would have made much more sense given the lore of the setting. We know the Camarilla actually offered the Setites membership at the time of their founding. We know the Setites are enemies of the Sabbat because of the Serpents of the Light (and that sect's general hatred of antedeluvians). And the clan has been developed much further from its roots of Wyrm minions who twirl their moustaches and do evil. So if we're told that clan joined the Camarilla in some alternate-V5, we already have long standing historical elements that could explain why, and it'd be much easier to justify (though it would still take work). That would be something much more believable - prior ties, common enemies.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-24T14:05:13-08:00","id":1429776,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1428599-v5-vampire-companion?p=1429662#post1429662\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I disagree with MWIS on a lot of things, but I'm in general more sympathetic to his views here than others.<br /> <br /> One thing I'm not seeing discussed (though I could easily miss it by mostly skimming over 25 pages of thread and reading only some in detail) is the issue of the Vinculum. How exactly can all these Sabbat vampires betray their fellow sect members by joining the enemy? Even low levels of the Vinculum would seem to prevent that.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I am mostly avoiding posting in this thread because the Companion failed to get me past my dislike of fifth edition, but I have seen this point and wonder why it's an issue.<br /> <br /> If the Vinculum ritual breaks a real blood bond, something stronger than the ties of the Vinculum, then why can't it break someone's Vinculum with one group in favor of a new group's Vinculum. Why can't the Lasombra who want out perform the Vinculum amongst themselves to break away from the old gang I guess is what I am asking as a player who does not overly like and play with the Sabbat?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24221-vamps-like-us","name":"Vamps Like Us","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"390"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-24T15:35:27-08:00","id":1429782,"title":"","content":"Honestly, that actually is the easiest answer, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24221-vamps-like-us\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"24221\" data-vbnamecard=\"24221\">Vamps Like Us</a>.<br /> <br /> &quot;How do they break the Vinculum?&quot;<br /> <br /> Well, all they'd have to do is share the Vinculum among themselves a bunch of times until their Bond to their fellow Lasombra is Level 10 versus the Level of their fellow Pack members. Remember the Vinculum doesn't prevent monomancy and that's, &quot;I feel like this fellow Sabbat member has to go.&quot; The Vinculum also doesn't provide loyalty to the SABBAT.<br /> <br /> It provides loyalty to your PACK members and the Sabbat you share with.<br /> <br /> Every member of the Lasombra can decide, bluntly, the Sect is a threat to themselves and their Pack members.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-24T15:41:10-08:00","id":1429784,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vamps Like Us</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1428599-v5-vampire-companion?p=1429776#post1429776\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I am mostly avoiding posting in this thread because the Companion failed to get me past my dislike of fifth edition, but I have seen this point and wonder why it's an issue.<br /> <br /> If the Vinculum ritual breaks a real blood bond, something stronger than the ties of the Vinculum, then why can't it break someone's Vinculum with one group in favor of a new group's Vinculum. Why can't the Lasombra who want out perform the Vinculum amongst themselves to break away from the old gang I guess is what I am asking as a player who does not overly like and play with the Sabbat?</div> </div> </div> </div>The Vinculum doesn't fade unless you roll a 1 to someone whos in the same drinking session as you, you can have unlimited vinculum ratings. I think drinking <i>really</i> potent, like 4th gen methusela blood, might break it, but only if it's potent enough to instantly fully bond you to them.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Prone to being a Classic Curmudgeon, goshdarned whippersnappers...","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1037-jamiemalk","name":"jamiemalk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1037_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"399"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-24T15:45:42-08:00","id":1429786,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1428599-v5-vampire-companion?p=1429782#post1429782\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Honestly, that actually is the easiest answer, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24221-vamps-like-us\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"24221\" data-vbnamecard=\"24221\">Vamps Like Us</a>.<br /> <br /> &quot;How do they break the Vinculum?&quot;<br /> <br /> Well, all they'd have to do is share the Vinculum among themselves a bunch of times until their Bond to their fellow Lasombra is Level 10 versus the Level of their fellow Pack members. Remember the Vinculum doesn't prevent monomancy and that's, &quot;I feel like this fellow Sabbat member has to go.&quot; The Vinculum also doesn't provide loyalty to the SABBAT.<br /> <br /> It provides loyalty to your PACK members and the Sabbat you share with.<br /> <br /> Every member of the Lasombra can decide, bluntly, the Sect is a threat to themselves and their Pack members.</div> </div> </div> </div>Eh, they'd need to do it hundreds of times to get close to having tens all round<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Prone to being a Classic Curmudgeon, goshdarned whippersnappers...","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1037-jamiemalk","name":"jamiemalk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1037_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"399"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-24T16:34:02-08:00","id":1429790,"title":"","content":"How much vinculum us left? Most packs went to the middle east where huge percentages were obliterated. I suspect there are hundreds of lasombra who were the only survivors of packs otherwise destroyed. My guess is that in the last twenty years there's a lot of tzimisce and lasombra suddenly packless and free to choose their own future.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3901-radiofreedeath","name":"RadioFreeDeath","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-24T16:48:25-08:00","id":1429792,"title":"","content":"<div c