ppy</a> if you have an issue with some posters, just report and the mods (Phipps) will handle it,<br /> it's better to involve a third party to avoid flame wars</div> </div> </div> </div>You\u2019re right of course, but by golly it\u2019s frustrating reading through this stuff all the time. The Facebook and other online fora are more constructive at least. Basically, the Companion has been a good supplement, although I\u2019d like to see the new Clans put into hardcopy at some point (in another supplement).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2517-trippy","name":"Trippy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2517_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1018"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-30T04:57:07-08:00","id":1430447,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1428599-v5-vampire-companion?p=1430378#post1430378\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\"><br /> <br /> But the Lasombra are an explictly real-religion themed group so its weird to make them the Cosmic Horror one. However, I think it's worth an entire thread to discuss the role of Cosmic Horror vs. Personal Horror in V:TM if you want to make it.</span></div> </div> </div> </div>Would that be a Cosmic Horror in V:tM or Cosmic Horror in WoD? Because the what gives Abyss Mysticism, and the Path of Night (as well as Vis and Koldunism in general, however badly the implementation of that idea sucked.) the CH vibe, is related to how they tie into themes from Mage, and to an extent WtA...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","name":"Taggie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1047"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-30T07:54:05-08:00","id":1430460,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1428599-v5-vampire-companion?p=1430399#post1430399\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well that's fine for you but for some of us, the whole appeal of V5 is following up the changes of earlier editions like Chicago by Night and with BJD.</div> </div> </div> </div>Isn't that a question of story, though? Not mechanics? It's perfectly possible to use the V5 metaplot with V20 or earlier rules, or conversely, use V5 mechanics with earlier settings. You could make Kevin Jackson Prince of Chicago and have Decker as a police-state tyrant using the mechanics and stats in the original Chicago and Milwaukee by Night books, if you wished. There was a rather good Victorian V5 on that charity play-through just recently. Just assume matching histories in each reality with individual characters having roughly equivalent but different abilities.<br /> <br /> I'm not really bothered either way. I'm just as happy to suspend disbelief and retcon. But if V5 is the same reality as V20, you <i>do </i>need to retcon.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/100-jezmiller","name":"JezMiller","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"437"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-30T08:57:25-08:00","id":1430466,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1428599-v5-vampire-companion?p=1430399#post1430399\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well that's fine for you but for some of us, the whole appeal of V5 is following up the changes of earlier editions like Chicago by Night and with BJD.</div> </div> </div> </div>None of which requires V5 to be in the precise identical universe as V20... any more than Revised V, W and M all having the Red Star and a shared destruction in the unworld causing the Wraith maelstrom and the Mage avatar storm require them to all be in the precise same universe with each other vs. being in neighboring universes that are very close to each other.<br /> <br /> Events play out almost identically in each parallel universe, but there are minor differences where mechanics and/or canon conflicts (ex. in the V5 universe Chimerstry has always been an Obfuscate power that required Presence).<br /> <br /> Even more fundamentally, saying their parallel universes just makes logical sense for the simple reason we\u2019re not all playing in the same shared universe. Half the Vamps in the V5 Chicago By Night book have been dead for decades in my ongoing Mage campaign. They didn\u2019t automatically die in anyone else\u2019s campaign so clearly these events happened in separate universes.<br /> <br /> Similarly, no version of Gehenna as laid out in the final book of the Revised line ever happened in the V20 universe so, again, clearly a separate universe from the one where, say, Wormwood was canon.<br /> <br /> The main reason I like it is that it\u2019s just a more harmonious answer than your efforts to hammer lore bits together while selectively ignoring others to try and justify changes with all the associated animosity and strife... when \u201cV5 happens in a parallel universe where it\u2019s mostly the same except for [insert version differences here]\u201d gives you everything you want (its still continuing all the lore you\u2019re interested in continuing) while also neatly putting the complaints to rest (because all the contradictory lore people are fighting you over just doesn\u2019t exist in the V5 universe).<br /> <br /> Because of your position as Mod, your pronouncements are given more weight, almost as if they\u2019re official OP pronouncements on canon rather than your personal opinions. It because of this extra weight and your personal beliefs that it all needs to fit together into a coherent one universe model that results in excessive pushback and acrimony (where as if you were just another poster more people would be willing to let things go as a difference of opinion... just as you dismiss my idea as a difference of opinion because I\u2019m just another poster).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1328-chris24601","name":"Chris24601","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-30T10:12:31-08:00","id":1430475,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JezMiller</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1428599-v5-vampire-companion?p=1430460#post1430460\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <b>Isn't that a question of story, though? Not mechanics? </b>It's perfectly possible to use the V5 metaplot with V20 or earlier rules, or conversely, use V5 mechanics with earlier settings. You could make Kevin Jackson Prince of Chicago and have Decker as a police-state tyrant using the mechanics and stats in the original Chicago and Milwaukee by Night books, if you wished. There was a rather good Victorian V5 on that charity play-through just recently. Just assume matching histories in each reality with individual characters having roughly equivalent but different abilities.<br /> <br /> I'm not really bothered either way. I'm just as happy to suspend disbelief and retcon. But if V5 is the same reality as V20, you <i>do </i>need to retcon.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't really think mechanics have ever reflected the in-story reality of the setting.<br /> <br /> Story trumps all.<br /> <br /> But mind you, I've never actually considered each clan to have &quot;Three&quot; Disciplines that are more important than other Disciplines for the most part. I don't think of the Weaknesses as things that are really central to their characterization. I feel that was a mistake of game design. Vampires don't have Humanity or Path scores, they're just extrapolations of story elements.<br /> <br /> Which should always be the primary concern.<br /> <br /> If you're overly focused on the rules, I feel like you lose what's most important in V:TM which is a focus on the characterization of the NPCs and interaction with the pCs.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-30T10:34:41-08:00","id":1430478,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1428599-v5-vampire-companion?p=1430475#post1430475\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don't really think mechanics have ever reflected the in-story reality of the setting.<br /> <br /> Story trumps all.<br /> <br /> But mind you, I've never actually considered each clan to have &quot;Three&quot; Disciplines that are more important than other Disciplines for the most part. I don't think of the Weaknesses as things that are really central to their characterization. I feel that was a mistake of game design. Vampires don't have Humanity or Path scores, they're just extrapolations of story elements.<br /> <br /> Which should always be the primary concern.<br /> <br /> If you're overly focused on the rules, I feel like you lose what's most important in V:TM which is a focus on the characterization of the NPCs and interaction with the pCs.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, you know my view, rules are the skeleton, setting is the sinew, plot is the muscle, they have to work together to build the game, if the rules don't reflect the setting, or the story ignores rules, things collapse.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","name":"Taggie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1047"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-31T01:18:55-08:00","id":1430546,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1428599-v5-vampire-companion?p=1430475#post1430475\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don't really think mechanics have ever reflected the in-story reality of the setting.<br /> <br /> Story trumps all.<br /> <br /> But mind you, I've never actually considered each clan to have &quot;Three&quot; Disciplines that are more important than other Disciplines for the most part. I don't think of the Weaknesses as things that are really central to their characterization. I feel that was a mistake of game design. Vampires don't have Humanity or Path scores, they're just extrapolations of story elements.<br /> <br /> Which should always be the primary concern.<br /> <br /> If you're overly focused on the rules, I feel like you lose what's most important in V:TM which is a focus on the characterization of the NPCs and interaction with the pCs.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm more interested in character than rules as well. But mechanical changes have character- and story-relevant effects, because &quot;mechanics&quot; is simply a shorthand for &quot;what a character can and cannot do&quot;. Making it easier for the Ravnos to enchant people or the Salubri to make people forget that they were there is likely to affect character choices and histories. Taking Auspex away from the Tzimisce shifts the clan away from its &quot;mystic&quot; aspect and towards its &quot;warlord&quot; one. These things do impact the in-story reality. They don't necessarily involve gross changes to the big picture, but they're changes nonetheless.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/100-jezmiller","name":"JezMiller","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"437"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-31T05:09:04-08:00","id":1430560,"title":"","content":"If, mechanically, I can no longer imitate others or create a series of alternative personas to deal with many mortals with obfuscate 3, that has very serious implications as to the story of my character. .<br /> If I had four in one discipline and four in another, and they're merged and I have to make sacrifices and cut away abilities that I use extensively, that has very serious implications to the story of my character.<br /> <br /> If thaumaturgy goes from an expensive array of powers I've sunk 200 xp into, and then I need to cut it down to five powers and maybe beg the ST for a lot of rituals that no longer have the same functionality, that's has pretty serious story implications. If Thaumaturgy goes from 'exciting' to 'just another discipline' as it has then that's a pretty big impact on the story.<br /> <br /> The 'everyone choses their powers' thing is just a completely different thing to 'everyone gets the same 1-5 powers' both in mechanics and in thematic connotations. The former says 'you are powerful and special' the latter says 'you are weak and insignificant and there are many more like you'. The later alone gave us incentive to diablerize our way down to 7th gen where we could transcend such limitations and have our own thing. But now the potential uniqueness of 6+ disciplines belong in the 1-5 rating.<br /> <br /> Fluff wise, chimestry worked on a completely different principle to obfuscate. Obfuscate just muddled minds to fool people. Chimestry made stuff out of illusory matter for everyone to see. Having them the same thing mechanically ruins that, and in turn ruins the occult/philosophy/religion kinda thing you build out of such powers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-31T07:32:53-08:00","id":1430566,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1428599-v5-vampire-companion?p=1430475#post1430475\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don't really think mechanics have ever reflected the in-story reality of the setting.<br /> <br /> Story trumps all.</div> </div> </div> </div>As an author you know stories without structure (i.e. rules) are shit. This goes double for fantasy (and VtM is urban fantasy) where consistent rules for the supernatural are key to maintaining suspension of disbelief.<br /> <br /> Even soft magic systems have rules that keep them from being the resolution to the story\u2019s climax (ex. Captain Marvel\u2019s powers are pretty much pure soft magic; the climax was her overcoming the conditioning/inhibitor; her kicking everyone\u2019s ass and blowing the crap out of the Kree fleet was pure catharsis... conversely, Aladdin doesn\u2019t beat Jafar by wielding the genie\u2019s soft magic power, but by tricking Jafar into making a wish that, by the established rules would trap him in a lamp).<br /> <br /> So when one rule has been established and then at a later point you break it (without first setting up the loophole earlier in the story) it\u2019s just bad storytelling. V5 changes a number of rules relative to prior editions (your V20 Thinblood suddenly uses alchemy instead of specific disciplines... Chimerstry is suddenly mind tricks instead of physical illusions) so trying to sell it as a continuation of the same story (versus a new story in a very similar universe) is, frankly, bad storytelling.<br /> <br /> If you answered the question \u201cWhy can\u2019t the protagonist use [previously established ability] to solve the problem?\u201d with \u201cBecause I changed the rules so he can no longer do that,\u201d you\u2019d be righly called out for crap writing.<br /> <br /> By contrast \u201cI wanted to explore a \u2018what if\u2019 scenario so this story takes place in a different universe... the protagonist could never do that here so now we get to explore how they would overcome a similar problem using different tools\u201d at least sounds like you give a damn about presenting a coherent story where solutions aren\u2019t just pulled out of the writer\u2019s ass in the name of \u201cdrama.\u201d","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1328-chris24601","name":"Chris24601","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-31T09:06:41-08:00","id":1430576,"title":"","content":"Is there a problem with V5 being a very similar story rather than the same one?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3523-spencer-from-the-hills","name":"Spencer from The Hills","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"546"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-31T09:25:04-08:00","id":1430580,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Spencer from The Hills</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1428599-v5-vampire-companion?p=1430576#post1430576\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is there a problem with V5 being a very similar story rather than the same one?</div> </div> </div> </div>it is when it's claiming to be the same one.<br /> <br /> besides the disconnect between mechanics and the lore is still present when you exclusively look at V5 and ignore the things that weren't carried over from V20 (yet)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25992,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25992-archderd","user":"archderd","date":". 12-31-2020, 12:28 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25992-archderd","name":"archderd","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25992_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-31T09:39:09-08:00","id":1430582,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Spencer from The Hills</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1428599-v5-vampire-companion?p=1430576#post1430576\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is there a problem with V5 being a very similar story rather than the same one?</div> </div> </div> </div>Not from my end. I happen to think that makes more sense than the alternative.<br /> <br /> One of the biggest issues with Forgotten Realms has been trying to keep it &quot;the same universe&quot; even as the rules have shifted quite extensively between editions of D&amp;D. That's why FR has had a &quot;Trouble&quot; event coinciding with virtually every new edition that throws the whole nature of reality into chaos and ends with things settling down into the new status quo.<br /> <br /> But at least they're acknowledging that some force altered the cosmos from what was previously known.<br /> <br /> The problem some of us have isn't with V5, its in the insistence by certain people that &quot;This is absolutely the same setting/universe and nothing within it is anything other than a direct continuation of prior editions even though X and Y are different and Z is being ignored.&quot;<br /> <br /> Frankly, I wouldn't need the multi-post apology (in this case in the original context of &quot;an explanation&quot; vs. the modern context of &quot;I'm sorry&quot;) threads if the explanation was just &quot;yeah, this is the next reality over on the Quantum Mirror (SG-1 reference; I've been binge-re-watching it on Netflix).&quot;<br /> <br /> Lasombra in the Camarilla because X reason that applies in this universe even if it doesn't quite make sense in the V20, Revised, 1e/2e universes? Sure. The underlying rules of reality are a little different so why not? (ex. letting your blood sit for X time in V5 removes its ability to form a blood bond so in V5 universe the Vlauderie is more symbolic and thus, easier for the Lasombra to ignore. Makes sense in V5-verse while it would be an issue in V20-verse).<br /> <br /> Toreador now need to surround themselves in beauty as their bane vs. risking being enthralled by beauty (which is now a clan compulsion that doesn't apply at all times)? Sure. Slightly different clan curses and disciplines/powers are a thing in the V5-verse.<br /> <br /> It really is just a much cleaner answer to a lot of the complaints that doesn't require logical contortions to explain or insults to intelligence/questioning motives by one side or the other of the discussion (which have even come up in this thread as the red text from our Mod shows).<br /> <br /> How many of Taggie's complaints about V5 become moot (beyond the &quot;I just don't like how this mechanic/change works&quot; which is just personal preference) if its just acknowledged that V5 is NOT the V20 universe? How many of the things CTPhipps likes are lost (beyond &quot;It MUST be the same exact universe even though every group plays in their own variation of it anyway&quot;) if its acknowledged that V5 mostly mirrors the history of the V20 universe except for the necessary changes to make the present V5 lore coherant?<br /> <br /> I'd argue &quot;most, if not all complaints&quot; and &quot;little, if any, losses&quot; which is why I think its the most harmonious answer towards avoiding things like edition warring on the boards.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1328-chris24601","name":"Chris24601","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-31T11:35:32-08:00","id":1430594,"title":"","content":"The setting sets the mechanics, not the other way around.<br /> <br /> Example: the setting of VtM makes it clear vampires can be superfast. THEN the game translates this into the celerity discipline. It's important to note that the exact mechanical workings are not set in stone and there's not just a single&quot;right&quot; way to implement the ability effect as long as it makes vampires fast in game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24992-haquim","name":"Haquim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24992_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-31T11:40:56-08:00","id":1430595,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Haquim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1428599-v5-vampire-companion?p=1430594#post1430594\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The setting sets the mechanics, not the other way around.</div> </div> </div> </div>Wait, aren't you a V5 fan? This is clearly an argument against v5, which has disregarded numerous setting establishments for mechanics.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-31T11:46:15-08:00","id":1430596,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chris24601</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1428599-v5-vampire-companion?p=1430582#post1430582\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But at least they're acknowledging that some force altered the cosmos from what was previously known.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Red Star could serve as that altering force - the Withering weakened Kindred Disciplines and clan Banes (remember, Beckett loses his glowing eyes in the Gehenna novel), and when the Red Star recedes, both return in altered form. If you want to move from V20 to V5 in the same universe you could do it that way, and any XP spent on non-V5 stuff like Thaumaturgy Paths could be &quot;redeployed&quot;. But that would just get you to exactly the same place as &quot;these are your characters in a different leg of the Trousers of Time&quot;.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/100-jezmiller","name":"JezMiller","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"437"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-31T11:52:29-08:00","id":1430599,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chris24601</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1428599-v5-vampire-companion?p=1430582#post1430582\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not from my end. I happen to think that makes more sense than the alternative.<br /> <br /> One of the biggest issues with Forgotten Realms has been trying to keep it &quot;the same universe&quot; even as the rules have shifted quite extensively between editions of D&amp;D. That's why FR has had a &quot;Trouble&quot; event coinciding with virtually every new edition that throws the whole nature of reality into chaos and ends with things settling down into the new status quo.<br /> <br /> But at least they're acknowledging that some force altered the cosmos from what was previously known.<br /> <br /> The problem some of us have isn't with V5, its in the insistence by certain people that &quot;This is absolutely the same setting/universe and nothing within it is anything other than a direct continuation of prior editions even though X and Y are different and Z is being ignored.&quot;<br /> <br /> Frankly, I wouldn't need the multi-post apology (in this case in the original context of &quot;an explanation&quot; vs. the modern context of &quot;I'm sorry&quot;) threads if the explanation was just &quot;yeah, this is the next reality over on the Quantum Mirror (SG-1 reference; I've been binge-re-watching it on Netflix).&quot;<br /> <br /> Lasombra in the Camarilla because X reason that applies in this universe even if it doesn't quite make sense in the V20, Revised, 1e/2e universes? Sure. The underlying rules of reality are a little different so why not? (ex. letting your blood sit for X time in V5 removes its ability to form a blood bond so in V5 universe the Vlauderie is more symbolic and thus, easier for the Lasombra to ignore. Makes sense in V5-verse while it would be an issue in V20-verse).<br /> <br /> Toreador now need to surround themselves in beauty as their bane vs. risking being enthralled by beauty (which is now a clan compulsion that doesn't apply at all times)? Sure. Slightly different clan curses and disciplines/powers are a thing in the V5-verse.<br /> <br /> It really is just a much cleaner answer to a lot of the complaints that doesn't require logical contortions to explain or insults to intelligence/questioning motives by one side or the other of the discussion (which have even come up in this thread as the red text from our Mod shows).<br /> <br /> How many of Taggie's complaints about V5 become moot (beyond the &quot;I just don't like how this mechanic/change works&quot; which is just personal preference) if its just acknowledged that V5 is NOT the V20 universe? How many of the things CTPhipps likes are lost (beyond &quot;It MUST be the same exact universe even though every group plays in their own variation of it anyway&quot;) if its acknowledged that V5 mostly mirrors the history of the V20 universe except for the necessary changes to make the present V5 lore coherant?<br /> <br /> I'd argue &quot;most, if not all complaints&quot; and &quot;little, if any, losses&quot; which is why I think its the most harmonious answer towards avoiding things like edition warring on the boards.</div> </div> </div> </div>Fact is it is the same universe BUT for the fact Gehenna (and the Apocalypse and Ascension and all the other end of times scenarios) didn't happen. V5 metaplot is the continuation of what V20 evolved into (BJD mainly) and tries to keep most if not all of the Gehenna developments as well. So for example you have Theo Bell killing Hardestadt, the Beckoning which is a replacement for the Withering, the Tremere clan ALMOST getting turned to ash (while in Gehenna they all get dusted but for the possible exception of Tremere himself), a part of the Assamites joining the Camarilla and so on. If you read the Gehenna novel all of that stuff is in there although they had to make some changes to make the most extreme events fit into the &quot;no Gehenna&quot; continuity (the Withering would have been way more extreme than the Beckoning for example).<br /> <br /> As for the Lasombra joining the Camarilla the event is actually explained in detail if you care to read instead of complaining because you don't like it. Roughly HALF of the Lasombra clan, mainly those obeying the Amici Noctis and the Ashirra part of the clan, considered their options and decided that the Gehenna crusade was suicide, so they swallowed their pride and accepted to join the creation of their most hated rivals (i.e. the Ventrue) rather than dying in the middle east. It's a perfectly fine and rational choice for vampires like the Lasombras. Also the other half of the clan remained Sabbat true believers and DID NOT leave that sect. It's a change but it's rational and it's explained in the metaplot. Then of course some of the people who don't like it moan and will keep moaning hoping that someone will reverse it. It's not very mature but everyone has a right to express its own personality, I guess.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24992-haquim","name":"Haquim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24992_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-31T11:58:54-08:00","id":1430600,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1428599-v5-vampire-companion?p=1430595#post1430595\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wait, aren't you a V5 fan? This is clearly an argument against v5, which has disregarded numerous setting establishments for mechanics.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm a VtM fan and I was since 1st edition, I think V5 did some things right and some things wrong and even some things potentially right but the execution was so hamfisted the effect was badly implemented. Anyway I like to think I'm mature enough to understand the setting evolved (less than you may think because as I explained above the metaplot tried to integrate Gehenna without Gehenna really happening) and changed. I don't like all of those changes (the beckoning for one) but I can live with them, in no way they are completely irrational but a rationale is provided (well except for Theo Bell killing Hardestadt but still being considered a trustworthy mediator by the Camarilla in case of conflict with the Anarchs... that is moronic and doesn't make any sense).<br /> <br /> TL; DR: V5 did not really change much of the setting at all, mechanics changed instead.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24992-haquim","name":"Haquim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24992_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-31T12:47:14-08:00","id":1430602,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Haquim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1428599-v5-vampire-companion?p=1430600#post1430600\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">well except for Theo Bell killing Hardestadt but still being considered a trustworthy mediator by the Camarilla in case of conflict with the Anarchs... that is moronic and doesn't make any sense</div> </div> </div> </div>Ho-hum. Doesn't that rather depend on whether or not Hardestadt's assassination was a joint project between Bell and the Camarilla faction which is now willing to use him as a mediator? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/100-jezmiller","name":"JezMiller","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"437"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-31T16:21:12-08:00","id":1430626,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JezMiller</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1428599-v5-vampire-companion?p=1430602#post1430602\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Ho-hum. Doesn't that rather depend on whether or not Hardestadt's assassination was a joint project between Bell and the Camarilla faction which is now willing to use him as a mediator? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>No, because the event was &quot;public&quot; (as public as possible for kindred under the Silence of Blood) and it is well known. Bell killed one of the founders of the Camarilla, disrupted a Conclave and got away scot free leading a great clan to break from the Ivory Tower. That's pure and simple defiance and even if the event was engineered with the aid of Camarilla conspirators (this is actually hinted in the V5 Camarilla book I believe) the public role of Theo Bell and his actions such as they were could never have been pardoned or ignored by the Camarilla.<br /> <br /> It's like an official of the US army who fought against the british killed George Washington, escaped, joined the spanish empire and american soldiers still considered him a trustworthy person to talk and set up truces with.<br /> <br /> The loss of face caused to the Camarilla by what Theo Bell did and how he did it is too great for the Ivory Tower to just forget and forgive yet that stupid loresheet wants us to believe that's what happened and everyone is fine with it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24992,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24992-haquim","user":"Haquim","date":". 01-01-2021, 02:41 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24992-haquim","name":"Haquim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24992_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-31T17:26:27-08:00","id":1430631,"title":"","content":"I think the situation with Bell is supposed to highlight (A) vampires are all liars, creatures without integrity and that the Camarilla makes a nest of vipers look like models of moral and ethical forbearance, (B) Bell is a rock star and everyone wants his autograph (C) the PC can try to get close enough to Bell to kill or capture him and try to take the bounty.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","name":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1208_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-01T07:34:29-08:00","id":1430664,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Haquim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1428599-v5-vampire-companion?p=1430599#post1430599\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Fact is it is the same universe BUT for the fact Gehenna (and the Apocalypse and Ascension and all the other end of times scenarios) didn't happen. V5 metaplot is the continuation of what V20 evolved into (BJD mainly) and tries to keep most if not all of the Gehenna developments as well.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u201cIt\u2019s exactly the same except for X\u201d is basically the textbook definition for a parallel universe story.<br /> <br /> Likewise, as I\u2019ve stated before I don\u2019t consider BJD to be a part of the natural V20 canon. It was the last V20 book published barely six-months (Jan 2018) ahead of V5 (Aug 2018) when the changes Paradox had made for V5 were already well known. It was a patch product akin to many of the last products released by D&amp;D ahead of an edition change that are more about pitching a \u201cnew normal\u201d than actually following the previous edition\u2019s lore with any great accuracy (and to get any last mechanical bits for V20 out there).<br /> <br /> Basically it\u2019s hard for me to say \u201cV5 is a logical continuation of V20\u201d when the only thing ot logically continues is a lore dump book that threw all sorts of new plots out there six months before an edition change versus all the lore that V20 presented throughout the rest of V20\u2019s seven year run.<br /> <br /> If I were to break down \u201cuniverses\u201d I\u2019d do it as follows;<br /> <br /> - V1/2/Rev (ended with Gehenna c. Jan 2004)<br /> - V20 (entire V20 line less BJD lore, no Withering/Gehenna, possibly even no Week of Nightmares)<br /> - V5 (a universe with slightly different mechanics, but most of the VRev and BJD events occurred)<br /> - VtR (another close, but different universe whose metaphysics place it somewhere past, but linked to V5).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1328-chris24601","name":"Chris24601","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-01T09:53:19-08:00","id":1430676,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chris24601</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1428599-v5-vampire-companion?p=1430664#post1430664\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">- VtR (another close, but different universe whose metaphysics place it somewhere past, but linked to V5).</div> </div> </div> </div>It might just be your wording, but this makes light of vast differences from the VtM games, of which I assume you know. Its mechanics are cross between 90s VtM, V5, and its own elements. However, it has none of VtM's fictional characters and history, except for somebody who looked like Damsel. One can question whether or how the Theo Bell of Revised would assassinate Hardestat and become an intermediate between the Camarilla and Anarchs. You can't do that in Requiem, because it doesn't have Theo Bell, Hardestat, the Camarilla or Anarchs.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3523-spencer-from-the-hills","name":"Spencer from The Hills","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"546"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-01T11:39:26-08:00","id":1430683,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chris24601</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1428599-v5-vampire-companion?p=1430664#post1430664\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u201cIt\u2019s exactly the same except for X\u201d is basically the textbook definition for a parallel universe story.<br /> <br /> Likewise, as I\u2019ve stated before I don\u2019t consider BJD to be a part of the natural V20 canon. It was the last V20 book published barely six-months (Jan 2018) ahead of V5 (Aug 2018) when the changes Paradox had made for V5 were already well known. It was a patch product akin to many of the last products released by D&amp;D ahead of an edition change that are more about pitching a \u201cnew normal\u201d than actually following the previous edition\u2019s lore with any great accuracy (and to get any last mechanical bits for V20 out there).<br /> <br /> Basically it\u2019s hard for me to say \u201cV5 is a logical continuation of V20\u201d when the only thing ot logically continues is a lore dump book that threw all sorts of new plots out there six months before an edition change versus all the lore that V20 presented throughout the rest of V20\u2019s seven year run.<br /> <br /> If I were to break down \u201cuniverses\u201d I\u2019d do it as follows;<br /> <br /> - V1/2/Rev (ended with Gehenna c. Jan 2004)<br /> - V20 (entire V20 line less BJD lore, no Withering/Gehenna, possibly even no Week of Nightmares)<br /> - V5 (a universe with slightly different mechanics, but most of the VRev and BJD events occurred)<br /> - VtR (another close, but different universe whose metaphysics place it somewhere past, but linked to V5).</div> </div> </div> </div>If you want to say the old WoD ceased to exist with the end of times events and the current timeline is taking palce into a parallel universe it makes sense, but ultimately it changes little: we are dealing with what we have at our disposal and obviously something that went through the apocalypse is not.<br /> Also, V20 wasn't originally meant to &quot;continue&quot; anything it was just a compilation and a commemorative edition, its success caused it to restart the metaplot.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24992-haquim","name":"Haquim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24992_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-01T12:18:41-08:00","id":1430687,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Haquim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1428599-v5-vampire-companion?p=1430683#post1430683\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Also, V20 wasn't originally meant to &quot;continue&quot; anything it was just a compilation and a commemorative edition, its success caused it to restart the metaplot.</div> </div> </div> </div>don't let Rich hear you say that ._.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>-</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10998-pleiades","name":"Pleiades","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10998_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1844"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-11T11:11:12-08:00","id":1431851,"title":"","content":"Nate from the old VtM25 podcast has a review out on the compendium <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://youtu.be/PJkDge_vzfI\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://youtu.be/PJkDge_vzfI\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://youtu.be/PJkDge_vzfI\" target=\"_blank\"> https://youtu.be/PJkDge_vzfI </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3953,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3953-dwight","user":"Dwight","date":". 01-11-2021, 02:23 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3953-dwight","name":"Dwight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3953_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-11T16:25:40-08:00","id":1431896,"title":"","content":"Do we know if Onyx Path will be releasing errata/updates for their. characters now that the Companion has been released? Shejana is pretty Ravnos already and her write-up fits with the general mood of the clan as defined in the Companion, but *technically* Erzulie doesn't have the Viccisitude portions portions of Protean as they require Discipline 2. Not trying to be a stick in the mud or anything like that, just curious how this kind of situation will resolve itself.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25976-differentjustin","name":"DifferentJustin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"47"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-12T07:47:18-08:00","id":1431969,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DifferentJustin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1428599-v5-vampire-companion?p=1431896#post1431896\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do we know if Onyx Path will be releasing errata/updates for their. characters now that the Companion has been released? Shejana is pretty Ravnos already and her write-up fits with the general mood of the clan as defined in the Companion, but *technically* Erzulie doesn't have the Viccisitude portions portions of Protean as they require Discipline 2. Not trying to be a stick in the mud or anything like that, just curious how this kind of situation will resolve itself.</div> </div> </div> </div><a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=ruHUzqfQNSg&amp;t=2504s\" target=\"_blank\">Here's your answer</a><br /> <br /> But if you don't want to check the video the answer is: it's likely they'll update the pdf with the errata and it's also possible that the Salubri material will be expanded.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24992-haquim","name":"Haquim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24992_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-01T08:48:18-08:00","id":1437489,"title":"","content":"I took forever doing this review:<br /> <br /> 4/5<br /> <br /> The VAMPIRE: THE MASQUERADE COMPANION is a relatively short sixty-five page book that was released for free by the folks at White Wolf and Paradox Interactive. I have the suspicion it was what was written up for the Vampire: The Masquerade Players Guide that was going to be released by Modiphius Entertainment but was delayed until the point of cancellation. If so, I think it was very nice of them to release it. Certainly, it helps keep the updates flowing into the setting and helps motivate the fanbase into continuing to play the game.<br /> <br /> The biggest update to the setting is the book finally provides rules for the Tzimisce, Ravnos, and Salubri clans. One of the biggest complaints about the initial release of Fifth Edition was the fact that it only provided rules for the original seven Camarilla clans as well as Thin Bloods. Later supplements added write-ups for the Ministry, Banu Haqim [Assamites], Lasombra, and Hecate [Giovanni]. I always felt this was one of the Fifth Edition's biggest issues as Vampire: The Masquerade 20th Anniversary Edition provided rules for all thirteen clans in the main book.<br /> <br /> As a long time fan of the Tzimisce, I was really appreciative of their write-up. I felt the absence of the Sabbat was another flaw of Fifth Edition and it was impossible to adapt them for my games because I didn't have the rules for its two Clans. I like the remake of the Fiends, focusing more on them as vampire-shaped dragons consumed with greed as well as wrath versus sadistic Buffalo Bill-esque psycho killers. Their new version is heavily influenced by the Dark Ages interpretation of the Clan and I like that a lot. I've always felt the more overtly &quot;gross&quot; Tzimisce were inferior to the voivodes of old.<br /> <br /> The Ravnos update is something I'm a little iffier on because I already felt the Clan had already been &quot;fixed&quot; by playing up their Indian subcontinent roots. I've always felt V:TM should be more international and incorporating the Rakahasa myth felt like it expanded the story significantly. The new versions of the Ravnos are a more regionally neutral &quot;Trickster&quot; Clan that exist for the purposes of robbing from the rich and laying low the haughty.<br /> <br /> The Ravnos are also possessed of a much better Clan Flaw this time around: being unable to stay in one place rather than having to commit crimes (that plays into unfortunate stereotypes). Even so, I feel like this infringes on my favorite elements of the Malkavians as the Trickster Clan as I was one of the few people who took their position as the pranksters of Kindred society seriously. Still, I think this version of the Ravnos is likely to stick and fits the more universal Clan approach that V5 seems to be going with.<br /> <br /> One thing I liked about the treatment of the Ravnos is that it establishes the Week of Nightmares did occur and the Clan is a shadow of its former self. The consequences for the previous metaplot aren't glossed over and weigh heavily on the Clan. It makes you wonder if trying to destroy one's Antediluvian is even worth it given the horrifying results. Then again, the Hecate seemed to have gotten away with it so maybe the lesson learned is, &quot;Don't nuke your Antediluvian. He'll take it personally.&quot;<br /> <br /> The Salubri are kind of an odd pick for the third Clan as while they're historically important, I'm not really sure anyone was overly clamoring for their return. At least over any other Bloodlines. On the other hand, I actually feel like the Salubri may have been the Clan most improved by its update. Previous versions of the Salubri have leaned hard either into them as vampire saints or deranged fundamentalists. Their Jesusian power of healing was also something of a gamebreaker Humanity-wise.<br /> <br /> The new Salubri having the relatively normal discipline spread of Auspex, Dominate, and Fortitude means that they're significantly more usable in a &quot;normal&quot; campaign. While they still have the Clan Flaw of Hunted as well as their Third Eye, I could easily see these Salubri staying hidden for centuries without their Discipline outing them. Their previous Clan Flaw of being unable to feed from the unwilling also made it hard to tell horror stories, which defeats the purpose of the game. The write-up seems to imply the Salubri numbers are tiny, though, and I was hoping we'd get around that. The Tremere undoubtedly exterminated them in Europe but there's plenty of other continents for them to have fled to.<br /> <br /> The book also provides a nice little section on coteries that explains why vampires choose to band together when they're normally solitary creatures of the night. I really enjoyed this part but don't have much to add other than its good flavor text. The book also provides updated rules on ghouls and talks about the challenges of roleplaying consent when dealing with the fact that they're inherently a master/slave relationship. I appreciated this discussion and the maturity with which it's handled. People come to vampire to play horrifying things but it's important to understand what your players are comfortable with.<br /> <br /> The additional rules and Disciplines that the book provides are okay. A lot of fans are going to be annoyed at the apparent nerfing that Vicissitude, Chimestry, and Obeah have all received. Vicissitude is now a subset of Protean, Chimestry of Dominate, and Obeah of Auspex. The fact Salubri cannot heal physical injuries anymore is something that is probably a wise decision for game balance but still is a huge change. Presumably any actual healers were Blood Sorcerers or possessed of Vicissitude Protean variants.<br /> <br /> Overall, I was very fond of this book and it provides a lot of useful material for Fifth Edition. I'm going to be honest that I probably think this should have been part of a Player's Handbook. On the other hand, it's hard to argue with free as a price tag. The information on the remaining Clans, mortals, and ghouls opens up a lot of options. I also approve of the majority of updates. Some people will be off-put by the changes but I think it makes all three Clans much more playable in mixed coteries. I also think the rules for ghouls, coterie rules, and roleplaying suggestions are very helpful.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-12T10:48:55-08:00","id":1439480,"title":"","content":"Ok, maybe I'm a little late here. But why did the Ravnos lost Fortitude for Presence? It makes no sense at all. I can understand the whole Obfuscate thing, but that is such a strange unnecessary change. I don't like much the Tzimisce change from Auspex to Dominate, but I guess it was much more discussed here already...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26311-ulbrecht","name":"Ulbrecht","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26311_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"33"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-12T12:06:36-08:00","id":1439489,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ulbrecht</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1428599-v5-vampire-companion?p=1439480#post1439480\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ok, maybe I'm a little late here. But why did the Ravnos lost Fortitude for Presence? It makes no sense at all. I can understand the whole Obfuscate thing, but that is such a strange unnecessary change. I don't like much the Tzimisce change from Auspex to Dominate, but I guess it was much more discussed here already...</div> </div> </div> </div>because amalgams my dude<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25992-archderd","name":"archderd","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25992_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-12T12:17:59-08:00","id":1439493,"title":"","content":"I've always thought of Ravnos as skating by on their charm (and a good exit strategy) rather than being stalwart tough guy types, so the discipline switch makes sense to me with regard to the essence of the clan.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-12T12:29:20-08:00","id":1439496,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ulbrecht</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1428599-v5-vampire-companion?p=1439480#post1439480\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ok, maybe I'm a little late here. But why did the Ravnos lost Fortitude for Presence? It makes no sense at all. I can understand the whole Obfuscate thing, but that is such a strange unnecessary change. I don't like much the Tzimisce change from Auspex to Dominate, but I guess it was much more discussed here already...</div> </div> </div> </div>Presence and Obfuscate seems a good basis for Combo Chimestry-like effects.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-12T15:51:29-08:00","id":1439529,"title":"","content":"I still think Obfuscate and Fortitude would have been a better combo for Chimerstry. Obfuscate has all the mental manipulation/illusion stuff baked into it already, just a little fluff about how Fortitude makes it lasting outside of the vampire's sphere of influence is all it would take. Making it Presence instead gives them a weird overlap in that now the Ministry can also pick up Chimerstry in-clan, as opposed to the Samedi Hecata who would have if it were Fortitude. And while the Ministry can probably use Chimerstry to great effect, it feels weird to give them that and the Serpentis amalgam running off of Presence too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25972-illithidactivity","name":"IllithidActivity","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25972_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"103"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-12T16:23:35-08:00","id":1439533,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>IllithidActivity</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1428599-v5-vampire-companion?p=1439529#post1439529\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I still think Obfuscate and Fortitude would have been a better combo for Chimerstry. Obfuscate has all the mental manipulation/illusion stuff baked into it already, just a little fluff about how Fortitude makes it lasting outside of the vampire's sphere of influence is all it would take. Making it Presence instead gives them a weird overlap in that now the Ministry can also pick up Chimerstry in-clan, as opposed to the Samedi Hecata who would have if it were Fortitude. And while the Ministry can probably use Chimerstry to great effect, it feels weird to give them that and the Serpentis amalgam running off of Presence too.</div> </div> </div> </div>Depends on how common you think Discipline spreads are.<br /> <br /> I don't think Out of Clan Disciplines are meant to be uncommon at all in this setting and virtually every vampire can have weird mixes of powers now.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-12T19:57:07-08:00","id":1439583,"title":"","content":"I think the amalgam explanation is kind of weak. Making Chimestry with Fortitude makes as much sense as with Presence. If it was a change centered on some obscure lore that I don't know, but could be explained somehow, I would feel more at ease, I guess...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26311-ulbrecht","name":"Ulbrecht","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26311_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"33"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-13T00:31:17-08:00","id":1439607,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ulbrecht</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1428599-v5-vampire-companion?p=1439583#post1439583\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think the amalgam explanation is kind of weak. Making Chimestry with Fortitude makes as much sense as with Presence. If it was a change centered on some obscure lore that I don't know, but could be explained somehow, I would feel more at ease, I guess...</div> </div> </div> </div>a presence amalgam makes alot more sense then fortitude. i still don't like it but still","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25992-archderd","name":"archderd","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25992_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-13T00:59:25-08:00","id":1439609,"title":"","content":"Personally, I think that Presence and Obfuscate make perfect sense for the Ravnos. I seem to recall suggesting those Disciplines for them years ago.<br /> <br /> Edit: here it is<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sergeant Brother</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/828040-which-bloodlines-and-clans-could-remain-interesting-without-a-special-discipline?p=828422#post828422\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ravnos - Celerity, Obfuscate, Presence. Being quick to use slight of hand, pick locks or pockets, get away fast. Obfuscate to sneak into or out of places or disguise yourself as somebody else. Presence to charm people into believing your cons.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1129,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","user":"Sergeant Brother","date":". 03-13-2021, 04:08 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-13T01:32:35-08:00","id":1439615,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sergeant Brother</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1428599-v5-vampire-companion?p=1439609#post1439609\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Personally, I think that Presence and Obfuscate make perfect sense for the Ravnos. I seem to recall suggesting those Disciplines for them years ago.<br /> <br /> Edit: here it is<br /> <br /> \u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>i see why you'd think it makes sense but it doesn't when you think about it long term. one of the well established aspects of the ravnos is that ppl don't like or trust them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25992-archderd","name":"archderd","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25992_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-13T01:56:32-08:00","id":1439620,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>archderd</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1428599-v5-vampire-companion?p=1439615#post1439615\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> i see why you'd think it makes sense but it doesn't when you think about it long term. one of the well established aspects of the ravnos is that ppl don't like or trust them.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would like or trust anyone with Presence and Obfuscate unless I was directly under the influence of Presence.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-13T02:34:53-08:00","id":1439622,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sergeant Brother</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1428599-v5-vampire-companion?p=1439620#post1439620\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I would like or trust anyone with Presence and Obfuscate unless I was directly under the influence of Presence.</div> </div> </div> </div>let's do a little comparison if you will the setites/ministry isn't trusted or liked by ppl that know the setites/ministry but they're about building a cult, a loyal following who deeply trusts them. the ravnos don't have such a thing because they're not about creating massive followings.when the topic of ravnos herds comes up they almost always mention how they're fighting with the gangrel, the fucking forest hobos of kindred, and you're hear willing to tell me that the clan that fights with the forest hobo clan over food sources has the same magical charisma as a ventrue or toreador?<br /> <br /> i'm sorry but that's complete nonsense.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25992,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25992-archderd","user":"archderd","date":". 03-13-2021, 05:37 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25992-archderd","name":"archderd","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25992_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-13T23:07:13-08:00","id":1439795,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>archderd</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1428599-v5-vampire-companion?p=1439622#post1439622\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> let's do a little comparison if you will the setites/ministry isn't trusted or liked by ppl that know the setites/ministry but they're about building a cult, a loyal following who deeply trusts them. the ravnos don't have such a thing because they're not about creating massive followings.when the topic of ravnos herds comes up they almost always mention how they're fighting with the gangrel, the fucking forest hobos of kindred, and you're hear willing to tell me that the clan that fights with the forest hobo clan over food sources has the same magical charisma as a ventrue or toreador?<br /> <br /> i'm sorry but that's complete nonsense.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don\u2019t recall ever reading that they fight the Gangrel for territory. It doesn\u2019t matter though. For any such change, obviously there is going to be some setting elements that are tied to the old concept and/or mechanics. The old Ravnos were a mess. They have been changed in a way to give them a more meaningful and coherent theme and Presence matches with that. They aren\u2019t building a cult because they aren\u2019t cultists, but it completely makes sense that a Clan of this type would be able to charm or manipulate people on an individual level and yet still be disliked as a whole because of their misbehavior.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-14T07:07:37-07:00","id":1439807,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sergeant Brother</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1428599-v5-vampire-companion?p=1439795#post1439795\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don\u2019t recall ever reading that they fight the Gangrel for territory. It doesn\u2019t matter though. For any such change, obviously there is going to be some setting elements that are tied to the old concept and/or mechanics. The old Ravnos were a mess. They have been changed in a way to give them a more meaningful and coherent theme and Presence matches with that. They aren\u2019t building a cult because they aren\u2019t cultists, but it completely makes sense that a Clan of this type would be able to charm or manipulate people on an individual level and yet still be disliked as a whole because of their misbehavior.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> not territory, they fight over herds but it seems you've missed the point in general. my point was that all clans with presence are on some level about building large following whether that's the ventrue, toreador, brujah or ministry i just picked ministry because out of that group the ministry are the least trusted and they're still doing better then the ravnos.<br /> <br /> it makes no sense that the clan with the same discipline used to create massive herds and followings by every other clan that has it somehow is fighting with the gangrel over herds unless you are drastically underestimating the discipline's power. presence isn't about making ppl like you, it's about demanding fear and respect to the point that being in you good graces is like fucking heroine to ppl<br /> <br /> also the ravnos are still a mess, they're just a different kind of mess and even then it was never the disciplines the ravnos had that caused them to be a mess.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25992,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25992-archderd","user":"archderd","date":". 03-14-2021, 10:41 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25992-archderd","name":"archderd","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25992_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-14T07:46:38-07:00","id":1439811,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>archderd</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1428599-v5-vampire-companion?p=1439807#post1439807\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> not territory, they fight over herds but it seems you've missed the point in general. my point was that all clans with presence are on some level about building large following whether that's the ventrue, toreador, brujah or ministry i just picked ministry because out of that group the ministry are the least trusted and they're still doing better then the ravnos.<br /> <br /> it makes no sense that the clan with the same discipline used to create massive herds and followings by every other clan that has it somehow is fighting with the gangrel over herds unless you are drastically underestimating the discipline's power. presence isn't about making ppl like you, it's about demanding fear and respect to the point that being in you good graces is like fucking heroine to ppl<br /> <br /> also the ravnos are still a mess, they're just a different kind of mess and even then it was never the disciplines the ravnos had that caused them to be a mess.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think its particularly difficult to see them fighting over traveling nomadic groups. I.e. Circus People, Truckers, theater troupes, and whoever else that the two carry with them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB