m":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-14T09:30:14-07:00","id":1439824,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>archderd</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1428599-v5-vampire-companion?p=1439615#post1439615\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> i see why you'd think it makes sense but it doesn't when you think about it long term. one of the well established aspects of the ravnos is that ppl don't like or trust them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Another well-established fact is that the are wanderers. This is even double-downed upon with the new Bane - they <i>have </i>to move or they could receive Aggravated Damage...not the best time to lose Fortitude. In fact, they shouldn't lose Fortitude at all, as &quot;wandering vampire&quot; is way too dangerous a lifestyle in the WoD. Especially for a clan whose members almost always rub someone the wrong way. Survival is too important, and being hard to kill feels more important to the clan now than ever before. I would never take their Fortitude away.<br /> <br /> Animalism also feels pretty important. For a nomad, it's one of the best feeding Disciplines in or out of the city, not to mention a little extra muscle/day time protection with easy-to-manage pets.<br /> <br /> These already-well-established Ravnos Disciplines still fit the clan nicely for feeding and survival, but their third Discipline was the one for fun and flavor. Obfuscate would be my choice for them, as it not only helps with getting out of Dodge, but it most closely resembles the mind-trickery people play Ravnos for: seeing things differently from how they are, not seeing anything at all, etc. Working illusions into it seems to fit better than any other Discipline.<br /> <br /> The drawback is that, admittedly, Animalism, Fortitude, Obfuscate doesn't feel very interesting. Like Nosferatu but with less oomph. But to be a good Ravnos, one needs to be imaginative.<br /> <br /> Just my thoughts on the new Disc line up. I agree that giving them Presence feels strange... a bit too on-the-nose for my taste. An &quot;easy-mode&quot; crutch.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24351,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24351-garygeneric","user":"Garygeneric","date":". 03-14-2021, 12:42 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24351-garygeneric","name":"Garygeneric","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24351_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"108"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-14T10:26:27-07:00","id":1439835,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>archderd</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1428599-v5-vampire-companion?p=1439812#post1439812\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">not when the ravnos have presence, when they don't it makes perfect sense</div> </div> </div> </div>The Ravnos still have to move all the time.<br /> <br /> Also, when the Ravnos turn a Gangrel's herd against them, the Gangrel has the adv